<Document>
<name>مواقع نبوي مابس</name>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد القبلتين</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد القبلتين من المساجد التاريخية البارزة في المدينة المنورة، ويقع في منطقة بني سلمة شمال غربي المسجد النبوي بالقرب من وادي العقيق. يعود اسمه إلى الحدث العظيم الذي ارتبط به، وهو تحويل القبلة من بيت المقدس إلى الكعبة المشرفة أثناء صلاة المسلمين فيه، فاشتهر منذ ذلك الحين بمسجد القبلتين. ويُعد من المساجد التي صلى فيها النبي ﷺ، وقد شهد عبر تاريخه عدة مراحل من الترميم والتجديد، بدءًا من بنائه البسيط في العصور الأولى وصولًا إلى إعادة بنائه وتوسعته في عهد المملكة العربية السعودية ، ليصبح مسجدًا متكامل المرافق يتسع لأعداد كبيرة من المصلين.||EN::Masjid Al-Qiblatayn (The Mosque of the Two Qiblas) is one of the prominent historical mosques in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located in the Bani Salama area, northwest of the Prophet's Mosque, near Wadi Al-Aqeeq. Its name goes back to the great event associated with it, which is the changing of the Qibla (direction of prayer) from Bait Al-Maqdis (Jerusalem) to the Honorable Kaaba while Muslims were praying in it, so it became famous since then as the Mosque of the Two Qiblas. It is considered one of the mosques in which the Prophet ﷺ prayed, and it has witnessed throughout its history several stages of restoration and renovation, starting from its simple construction in the early eras, all the way to its reconstruction and expansion during the era of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, to become a mosque with integrated facilities that accommodates large numbers of worshipers.||TR::Mescid-i Kıbleteyn (İki Kıbleli Mescit), Medine-i Münevvere'deki önde gelen tarihi mescitlerden biridir ve Mescid-i Nebevi'nin kuzeybatısında, Akik Vadisi yakınlarındaki Beni Seleme bölgesinde yer almaktadır. Adı, onunla ilişkilendirilen büyük bir olaya, yani Müslümanların içinde namaz kıldıkları sırada kıblenin Beytü'l-Makdis'ten (Kudüs) Kâbe-i Müşerrefe'ye çevrilmesine dayanır ve o zamandan beri Mescid-i Kıbleteyn olarak meşhur olmuştur. Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ içinde namaz kıldığı mescitlerden biri olarak kabul edilir ve tarihi boyunca, ilk çağlardaki basit yapısından başlayarak Suudi Arabistan Krallığı döneminde yeniden inşa edilip genişletilmesine kadar birçok restorasyon ve yenileme aşamasına tanık olmuş, böylece çok sayıda ibadet edeni barındıran tam donanımlı tesisleri olan bir mescit haline gelmiştir.||ID::Masjid Qiblatain adalah salah satu masjid bersejarah yang menonjol di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan terletak di wilayah Bani Salamah, barat laut Masjid Nabawi di dekat Lembah Al-Aqiq. Namanya berasal dari peristiwa besar yang terkait dengannya, yaitu pemindahan kiblat dari Baitul Maqdis (Yerusalem) ke Ka'bah yang mulia ketika umat Islam sedang shalat di dalamnya, sehingga sejak saat itu terkenal sebagai Masjid Qiblatain (Dua Kiblat). Masjid ini dianggap sebagai salah satu masjid di mana Nabi ﷺ pernah shalat, dan telah menyaksikan sepanjang sejarahnya beberapa tahap pemugaran dan renovasi, mulai dari bangunan sederhananya di era-era awal hingga rekonstruksi dan perluasannya di era Kerajaan Arab Saudi, untuk menjadi masjid dengan fasilitas terpadu yang dapat menampung jamaah dalam jumlah besar.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/gv1JjawD5fwPLyVM7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.57893968800128,24.48407738857632,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>سقيفة بني ساعدة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::تُعد "سقيفة بني ساعدة" الواقعة شمال غربي المسجد النبوي معلماً تاريخياً بارزاً؛ حيث ورد جلوس النبي ﷺ فيها كما في حديث سهل بن سعد الساعدي، وشهدت مبايعة أبي بكر الصديق رضي الله عنه بأول خلافة للمسلمين بعد وفاة النبي ﷺ. وقد أولت المملكة العربية السعودية اهتماماً كبيراً بالموقع؛ حيث طوّرته وحوّلته إلى حديقة تاريخية خضراء متكاملة الخدمات ضمن الساحات الغربية للمسجد النبوي، ومزودة بممرات للمشاة ومناطق للجلوس تتماشى مع الهوية العمرانية للمسجد، وذلك بهدف الحفاظ على الإرث الإسلامي وإثراء التجربة الثقافية والدينية لضيوف الرحمن.||EN::"Saqifah Bani Saidah", located northwest of the Prophet's Mosque, is a prominent historical landmark. It is mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ sat there, as narrated in the hadith of Sahl bin Sa'd Al-Sa'idi, and it witnessed the pledge of allegiance to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, as the first Caliph of the Muslims after the death of the Prophet ﷺ. The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has paid great attention to the site, developing and transforming it into a fully serviced green historical park within the western courtyards of the Prophet's Mosque. It is equipped with pedestrian walkways and seating areas that align with the architectural identity of the mosque, aiming to preserve Islamic heritage and enrich the cultural and religious experience for the Guests of Allah.||TR::Mescid-i Nebevi'nin kuzeybatısında yer alan "Sakife-i Beni Saide", önde gelen tarihi bir simge yapıdır. Sehl bin Sa'd es-Saidi'nin hadisinde belirtildiği üzere Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ burada oturduğu rivayet edilmiş ve Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ vefatından sonra Müslümanların ilk halifesi olarak Ebubekir es-Sıddık'a (r.a.) biat edilmesine tanıklık etmiştir. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı bu alana büyük önem vermiş; onu geliştirerek Mescid-i Nebevi'nin batı avluları içerisinde, mescidin mimari kimliğiyle uyumlu yaya yürüyüş yolları ve oturma alanlarıyla donatılmış, tam hizmet sunan tarihi yeşil bir parka dönüştürmüştür. Bununla, İslami mirasın korunması ve Rahman'ın misafirlerinin kültürel ve dini deneyimlerinin zenginleştirilmesi amaçlanmaktadır.||ID::"Saqifah Bani Sa'idah", yang terletak di sebelah barat laut Masjid Nabawi, merupakan landmark bersejarah yang menonjol. Disebutkan bahwa Nabi ﷺ pernah duduk di sana, sebagaimana diriwayatkan dalam hadis Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi, dan tempat ini menyaksikan baiat (sumpah setia) kepada Abu Bakar As-Siddiq radhiyallahu 'anhu sebagai khalifah pertama umat Islam setelah wafatnya Nabi ﷺ. Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah memberikan perhatian besar terhadap situs ini; dengan mengembangkan dan mengubahnya menjadi taman bersejarah hijau berfasilitas lengkap di dalam area halaman barat Masjid Nabawi. Taman ini dilengkapi dengan jalur pejalan kaki dan area tempat duduk yang selaras dengan identitas arsitektur masjid, dengan tujuan untuk melestarikan warisan Islam serta memperkaya pengalaman budaya dan keagamaan bagi para Tamu Allah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/9aXLenPQFAng6Ve89]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.606785,24.4703265,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>ثنية الوداع</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::ثنية الوداع من أشهر المعالم التاريخية في المدينة المنورة، وهي ممر جبلي مرتفع كان يقع في الجهة الشمالية من المدينة قرب جبل سلع، على مقربة من الطرق المؤدية إلى خارجها. ارتبط اسمها بالتوديع والاستقبال، إذ كانت موضع وداع المسافرين والجيوش الخارجة من المدينة واستقبال العائدين إليها، ولذلك عُرفت منذ القدم باسم ثنية الوداع. وقد شهدت عدداً من الأحداث المهمة في السيرة النبوية، منها توديع النبي ﷺ لبعض السرايا والجيوش، واستقبال العائدين من الغزوات. وكانت الثنية عبارة عن مرتفع صخري صغير يشرف على المنطقة المحيطة، إلا أن معالمها الأصلية اندثرت مع التوسعات العمرانية الحديثة وأزيلت بالكامل في القرن الرابع عشر الهجري ضمن مشاريع تطوير المنطقة.||EN::"Thaniyat Al-Wada" (The Pass of Farewell) is one of the most famous historical landmarks in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. It was an elevated mountain pass located in the northern part of the city near Mount Sila', close to the roads leading out of it. Its name was associated with bidding farewell and welcoming, as it was the place for bidding farewell to travelers and armies leaving the city and welcoming those returning to it; therefore, it has been known since ancient times as Thaniyat Al-Wada. It witnessed a number of important events in the Prophetic Biography (Seerah), including the Prophet ﷺ bidding farewell to some expeditions and armies, and welcoming those returning from battles. The pass was a small rocky elevation overlooking the surrounding area, but its original features disappeared with modern urban expansions and it was completely removed in the fourteenth century AH as part of the region's development projects.||TR::"Seniyyetü'l-Vedâ" (Veda Tepesi), Medine-i Münevvere'deki en meşhur tarihi simge yapılardan biridir. Şehrin kuzey kesiminde, Sel Dağı'nın yakınında, şehir dışına çıkan yolların civarında yer alan yüksek bir dağ geçidiydi. Şehirden ayrılan yolcuları ve orduları uğurlama ile şehre dönenleri karşılama yeri olduğundan adı veda ve karşılama ile ilişkilendirilmiş ve bu nedenle eski çağlardan beri Seniyyetü'l-Vedâ olarak bilinmektedir. Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ bazı müfreze ve orduları uğurlaması ve gazvelerden dönenleri karşılaması dahil olmak üzere, siyerdeki bir dizi önemli olaya tanıklık etmiştir. Bu geçit, çevredeki bölgeye hakim küçük kayalık bir yükseklikti, ancak orijinal hatları modern kentsel genişlemelerle birlikte kaybolmuş ve bölgeyi geliştirme projeleri kapsamında Hicri on dördüncü yüzyılda tamamen ortadan kaldırılmıştır.||ID::"Tsaniyatul Wada'" (Bukit Perpisahan) adalah salah satu landmark bersejarah paling terkenal di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Tempat ini dulunya merupakan celah pegunungan yang tinggi yang terletak di bagian utara kota dekat Gunung Sila', berdekatan dengan jalan-jalan yang mengarah ke luar kota. Namanya dikaitkan dengan perpisahan dan penyambutan, karena tempat ini merupakan lokasi untuk melepas kepergian para pelancong dan pasukan militer yang meninggalkan kota, serta menyambut mereka yang kembali. Oleh karena itu, sejak zaman dahulu tempat ini dikenal sebagai Tsaniyatul Wada'. Tempat ini telah menyaksikan sejumlah peristiwa penting dalam Sirah Nabawiyah, di antaranya adalah ketika Nabi ﷺ melepas beberapa ekspedisi dan pasukan militer, serta menyambut mereka yang kembali dari peperangan. Bukit ini dulunya berupa dataran tinggi berbatu kecil yang menghadap ke daerah sekitarnya, namun ciri-ciri aslinya telah menghilang seiring dengan perluasan kota modern dan dihilangkan sepenuhnya pada abad keempat belas Hijriah sebagai bagian dari proyek pengembangan wilayah tersebut.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/gfSwCCBggNubeRH7A]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.605255,24.476809,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر رومة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::تُعد "بئر رومة" (المعروفة بـ "بئر عثمان") الواقعة شمال غربي المسجد النبوي معلماً تاريخياً بارزاً؛ حيث كانت من أعذب مصادر المياه التي استعذبها النبي ﷺ وشرب منها، واكتسبت مكانتها العظيمة حين اشتراها عثمان بن عفان رضي الله عنه وجعلها وقفاً للمسلمين استجابة لترغيب النبي ﷺ. ورغم مرور القرون، فقد أولت المملكة العربية السعودية اهتماماً كبيراً بالموقع، حيث عملت على ترميم البئر وتطوير المزرعة المحيطة بها لاستدامة عطاء هذا الوقف الإسلامي الخالد.||EN::"Bi'r Rumah" (known as "Bi'r Uthman"), located northwest of the Prophet's Mosque, is a prominent historical landmark; as it was one of the sweetest water sources that the Prophet ﷺ found sweet and drank from. It gained its great status when Uthman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, bought it and made it an endowment (waqf) for the Muslims in response to the Prophet's ﷺ encouragement. Despite the passing of centuries, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has paid great attention to the site, as it worked on restoring the well and developing the surrounding farm to sustain the yield of this immortal Islamic endowment.||TR::Mescid-i Nebevi'nin kuzeybatısında yer alan "Rume Kuyusu" ("Osman Kuyusu" olarak da bilinir), önde gelen tarihi bir simge yapıdır; zira Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ tatlı bulduğu ve suyundan içtiği en tatlı su kaynaklarından biriydi. Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ teşvikine cevaben Osman bin Affan'ın (r.a.) onu satın alıp Müslümanlar için bir vakıf haline getirmesiyle bu büyük konumunu kazanmıştır. Yüzyılların geçmesine rağmen Suudi Arabistan Krallığı bu alana büyük önem vermiş; bu ölümsüz İslami vakfın verimliliğini (nimetini) sürdürmek için kuyuyu restore etme ve çevresindeki çiftliği geliştirme çalışmaları yapmıştır.||ID::"Sumur Rumah" (yang dikenal sebagai "Sumur Utsman"), yang terletak di sebelah barat laut Masjid Nabawi, merupakan landmark bersejarah yang menonjol; di mana ia merupakan salah satu sumber air paling segar yang disukai dan diminum oleh Nabi ﷺ. Sumur ini mendapatkan kedudukan agungnya ketika Utsman bin Affan radhiyallahu 'anhu membelinya dan menjadikannya wakaf bagi umat Islam sebagai tanggapan atas anjuran Nabi ﷺ. Meskipun berabad-abad telah berlalu, Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah memberikan perhatian besar terhadap situs ini, di mana mereka bekerja untuk memugar sumur tersebut dan mengembangkan pertanian di sekitarnya untuk melestarikan hasil dari wakaf Islam yang abadi ini.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/ibEshA2EF7DZooKq8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.57856085434707,24.49459650714406,602.2571948290217</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد قباء</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد قباء من أبرز المعالم الإسلامية في المدينة المنورة، ويقع في حي قباء جنوب غربي المسجد النبوي. ويُعد أول مسجد أُسس في الإسلام، إذ بناه النبي ﷺ عند وصوله إلى المدينة مهاجراً، وشارك بنفسه في تحديد موضعه ووضع لبناته الأولى. وقد كان النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يصلي فيه. شهد المسجد عبر القرون العديد من أعمال الترميم والتوسعة، بدءاً من العصور الإسلامية الأولى وصولاً إلى التوسعات الحديثة في عهد المملكة العربية  السعودية، التي اهتمت بالمسجد واعتنت به وطورت المنطقة المحيطة بها.||EN::Quba Mosque is one of the most prominent Islamic landmarks in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, and it is located in the Quba neighborhood southwest of the Prophet's Mosque. It is considered the first mosque founded in Islam, as the Prophet ﷺ built it upon his arrival in Madinah as an emigrant, and he participated himself in determining its location and laying its first bricks. And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to pray in it. Throughout the centuries, the mosque has witnessed many restoration and expansion works, starting from the early Islamic eras up to the modern expansions during the era of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, which paid attention to the mosque, took care of it, and developed the surrounding area.||TR::Kuba Mescidi, Medine-i Münevvere'deki en önde gelen İslami simge yapılardan biridir ve Mescid-i Nebevi'nin güneybatısındaki Kuba mahallesinde yer almaktadır. İslam'da kurulan ilk mescit olarak kabul edilir; zira Hz. Peygamber ﷺ Medine'ye muhacir olarak vardığında onu inşa etmiş ve bizzat yerini belirleyip ilk tuğlalarını koymaya iştirak etmiştir. Ve Peygamber sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem içinde namaz kılardı. Yüzyıllar boyunca mescit, ilk İslami dönemlerden başlayarak mescide önem veren, ona özen gösteren ve çevresindeki bölgeyi geliştiren Suudi Arabistan Krallığı dönemindeki modern genişletmelere kadar birçok restorasyon ve genişletme çalışmasına tanık olmuştur.||ID::Masjid Quba adalah salah satu landmark Islam paling menonjol di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan terletak di lingkungan Quba di sebelah barat daya Masjid Nabawi. Masjid ini dianggap sebagai masjid pertama yang didirikan dalam Islam, karena Nabi ﷺ membangunnya pada saat kedatangannya di Madinah sebagai muhajir, dan beliau sendiri berpartisipasi dalam menentukan lokasinya dan meletakkan batu bata pertamanya. Dan Nabi shallallahu 'alaihi wa sallam biasa shalat di dalamnya. Sepanjang abad, masjid ini telah menyaksikan banyak pekerjaan pemugaran dan perluasan, mulai dari era awal Islam hingga perluasan modern pada era Kerajaan Arab Saudi, yang memberikan perhatian pada masjid ini, merawatnya, dan mengembangkan kawasan sekitarnya.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/eQtgiJonRxg9hPb16]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61727216567716,24.43937815289183,609.6721644672898</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر العهن أو اليسيرة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بئر العهن من الآبار التاريخية القديمة في المدينة المنورة، وتقع في منطقة العالية جنوب شرقي المسجد النبوي بالقرب من حي قباء. عُرفت قديماً ببئر بني أمية بن زيد من الأنصار، ويُرجَّح أن اسمها مشتق من العهن، وهو الصوف الملون، أو من بستان كان يحمل هذا الاسم في المنطقة. اشتهرت البئر في الماضي بغزارة مياهها وعذوبتها، وكانت تقع وسط بستان مزدهر، كما ارتبطت ببعض الروايات التاريخية التي تذكر أن النبي ﷺ مر بها وبارك ماءها وسمّاها «اليسيرة». وفي عهد المملكة العربية السعودية اهتمت بتأهيل البئر والمنطقة المحيطة بها، استكمالا لمشروعها في المحافظة على الآثار التاريخية.||EN::"Bi'r Al-Ihn" (Al-Ihn Well) is one of the old historical wells in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, and it is located in the Al-Awali area southeast of the Prophet's Mosque near the Quba neighborhood. It was known in the past as the well of Bani Umayyah bin Zaid of the Ansar, and it is likely that its name is derived from "Al-Ihn", which is colored wool, or from an orchard that bore this name in the area. The well was famous in the past for the abundance and sweetness of its water, and it was located in the middle of a flourishing orchard. It was also associated with some historical narratives that mention that the Prophet ﷺ passed by it, blessed its water, and named it "Al-Yaseerah". And in the era of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, it paid attention to rehabilitating the well and the area surrounding it, in completion of its project to preserve historical monuments.||TR::İhn Kuyusu (Bi'r-i İhn), Medine-i Münevvere'deki eski tarihi kuyulardan biridir ve Mescid-i Nebevi'nin güneydoğusundaki Âliye bölgesinde, Kuba mahallesi yakınında yer almaktadır. Geçmişte Ensar'dan Beni Ümeyye bin Zeyd kuyusu olarak bilinirdi ve adının renkli yün anlamına gelen "el-İhn"den veya bölgede bu adı taşıyan bir meyve bahçesinden türetilmiş olması muhtemeldir. Kuyu geçmişte suyunun bolluğu ve tatlılığı ile meşhurdu ve verimli bir meyve bahçesinin ortasında yer alıyordu. Ayrıca Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ oradan geçtiği, suyunu bereketlendirdiği ve ona "el-Yesire" adını verdiğini belirten bazı tarihi rivayetlerle de ilişkilendirilmiştir. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı döneminde ise tarihi eserleri koruma projesinin bir tamamlayıcısı olarak kuyunun ve çevresindeki bölgenin rehabilite edilmesine önem verilmiştir.||ID::Sumur Al-Ihn adalah salah satu sumur bersejarah kuno di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan terletak di daerah Al-Awali di sebelah tenggara Masjid Nabawi di dekat lingkungan Quba. Di masa lalu, sumur ini dikenal sebagai sumur Bani Umayyah bin Zaid dari kaum Anshar, dan kemungkinan namanya berasal dari kata "Al-Ihn", yang berarti wol berwarna, atau dari sebuah kebun yang membawa nama ini di wilayah tersebut. Sumur ini di masa lalu terkenal dengan kelimpahan dan kemanisan airnya, dan terletak di tengah-tengah kebun yang subur, sebagaimana ia juga dikaitkan dengan beberapa riwayat sejarah yang menyebutkan bahwa Nabi ﷺ pernah melewatinya, memberkahi airnya dan menamainya "Al-Yasiirah". Dan pada era Kerajaan Arab Saudi, ia memberikan perhatian untuk merehabilitasi sumur dan kawasan di sekitarnya, sebagai pelengkap bagi proyeknya dalam melestarikan monumen-monumen bersejarah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/CdSdKUhE2TXXyb2W6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.62958435844895,24.43795126973316,609.7260920482985</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل ذباب</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::جبل ذباب، المعروف أيضاً باسم جبل الراية، معلم تاريخي يقع شمال غربي المسجد النبوي على مقربة من جبل سلع. وهو عبارة عن مرتفع صخري صغير دائري الشكل من الصخور البركانية السوداء، ويُعد جزءاً من التكوين الجيولوجي لمنطقة سلع. اكتسب الجبل أهميته من ارتباطه بأحداث غزوة الخندق، إذ اتخذه النبي ﷺ موضعاً لمراقبة أعمال حفر الخندق، وضُربت عليه قبة له أثناء الغزوة، وقد بُني عليه مسجدًا وظل قائماً عبر العصور مع ما شهده من ترميمات وتجديدات. وفي عهد المملكة العربية السعودية يحيط العمران بالجبل والمسجد من معظم الجهات، إلا أنهما ما يزالان من المعالم التاريخية المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية وتاريخ المدينة المنورة.||EN::"Jabal Dhubab" (Mount Dhubab), also known as "Jabal Ar-Rayah" (Mount of the Banner), is a historical landmark located northwest of the Prophet's Mosque, close to Mount Sila'. It is a small, circular-shaped rocky elevation made of black volcanic rocks, and it is considered part of the geological formation of the Sila' area. The mountain gained its importance from its association with the events of the Battle of the Trench (Ghazwat Al-Khandaq), as the Prophet ﷺ took it as a position to monitor the trench digging works, and a dome-shaped tent was pitched for him upon it during the battle. A mosque was built on it and has remained standing throughout the ages, along with the restorations and renovations it witnessed. In the era of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, urban development surrounds the mountain and the mosque from most sides, yet they both still remain among the historical landmarks associated with the Prophetic Biography and the history of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah.||TR::"Râye Dağı" olarak da bilinen "Zübâb Dağı", Mescid-i Nebevi'nin kuzeybatısında, Sel Dağı'nın yakınında yer alan tarihi bir simge yapıdır. Siyah volkanik kayalardan oluşan küçük, dairesel şekilli kayalık bir yükseklik olup, Sel bölgesinin jeolojik oluşumunun bir parçası olarak kabul edilir. Dağ, önemini Hendek Gazvesi olaylarıyla olan bağlantısından kazanmıştır; zira Hz. Peygamber ﷺ hendek kazma çalışmalarını izlemek (denetlemek) için onu bir mevzi edinmiş ve gazve sırasında üzerinde onun için kubbe şeklinde bir çadır kurulmuştur. Üzerine bir mescit inşa edilmiş ve tanık olduğu restorasyon ve yenilemelerle birlikte çağlar boyunca ayakta kalmıştır. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı döneminde şehirleşme dağı ve mescidi çoğu yönden çevrelemektedir; ancak her ikisi de siyer (Hz. Peygamber'in hayatı) ve Medine-i Münevvere tarihi ile bağlantılı tarihi simge yapılar arasında yer almaya devam etmektedir.||ID::"Gunung Dhubab", yang juga dikenal sebagai "Gunung Ar-Rayah" (Gunung Panji), adalah landmark bersejarah yang terletak di sebelah barat laut Masjid Nabawi, dekat dengan Gunung Sila'. Ia merupakan dataran tinggi berbatu kecil berbentuk bundar dari batuan vulkanik hitam, dan dianggap sebagai bagian dari formasi geologi daerah Sila'. Gunung ini mendapatkan kepentingannya dari keterkaitannya dengan peristiwa-peristiwa Perang Khandaq (Parit), karena Nabi ﷺ menjadikannya sebagai posisi untuk memantau pekerjaan penggalian parit, dan sebuah tenda berbentuk kubah didirikan untuk beliau di atasnya selama perang tersebut. Sebuah masjid telah dibangun di atasnya dan tetap berdiri sepanjang zaman dengan pemugaran dan pembaruan yang disaksikannya. Di era Kerajaan Arab Saudi, pembangunan kota mengelilingi gunung dan masjid tersebut dari sebagian besar sisi, akan tetapi keduanya masih tetap menjadi di antara landmark bersejarah yang terkait dengan Sirah Nabawiyah dan sejarah Madinah Al-Munawwarah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/VqPLR7phEE5mbcq8A]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.6034327,24.480303,601.0019818489513</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل سلع</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::جبل سلع من أبرز المعالم الطبيعية والتاريخية في المدينة المنورة، ويقع شمال غربي المسجد النبوي على مسافة قصيرة منه. وهو جبل صخري كبير ذو تكوينات جرانيتية قديمة وشعاب متعددة، شكّل عبر التاريخ حاجزاً طبيعياً مهماً للمدينة. وتنبع أهميته من ارتباطه الوثيق بـغزوة الخندق، حيث اتخذه النبي ﷺ موقعاً استراتيجياً لقيادة المسلمين، فجعل الجبل خلف الجيش والخندق أمامه، مستفيداً من موقعه المرتفع في المراقبة والدفاع. كما كان الجبل موضعاً لمعسكر المسلمين ومبيت النبي ﷺ أثناء الغزوة، وأسهم في حماية المدينة من هجمات الأحزاب. ويضم جبل سلع عدداً من المعالم التاريخية المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية، من أبرزها مساجد الفتح، والغار المنسوب إلى مبيت النبي ﷺ، إضافة إلى ارتباطه بموضع ثنية الوداع. ولا يزال الجبل اليوم شاهداً بارزاً على أحد أهم الأحداث العسكرية في التاريخ الإسلامي، ومعلماً تاريخياً بارزاً في المدينة المنورة.||EN::"Jabal Sila" (Mount Sila') is one of the most prominent natural and historical landmarks in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, and it is located northwest of the Prophet's Mosque at a short distance from it. It is a large rocky mountain with ancient granitic formations and multiple ravines, which has formed throughout history an important natural barrier for the city. Its importance stems from its close association with the Battle of the Trench (Ghazwat Al-Khandaq), where the Prophet ﷺ took it as a strategic position to lead the Muslims, so he placed the mountain behind the army and the trench in front of it, benefiting from its elevated position in monitoring and defense. The mountain was also the site of the Muslims' camp and the Prophet's ﷺ overnight stay during the battle, and it contributed to protecting the city from the attacks of the confederates (Al-Ahzab). Jabal Sila' includes a number of historical landmarks associated with the Prophetic Biography, most notably the Al-Fath Mosques, and the cave attributed to the Prophet's ﷺ overnight stay, in addition to its connection to the location of Thaniyat Al-Wada. The mountain still remains today a prominent witness to one of the most important military events in Islamic history, and a prominent historical landmark in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah.||TR::"Sel Dağı" (Cebel-i Sel'), Medine-i Münevvere'deki en önde gelen doğal ve tarihi simge yapılardan biridir ve Mescid-i Nebevi'nin kuzeybatısında ondan kısa bir mesafede yer almaktadır. Eski granit oluşumlarına ve çok sayıda vadiye (geçide) sahip büyük kayalık bir dağdır ve tarih boyunca şehir için önemli bir doğal bariyer oluşturmuştur. Önemini, Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ onu Müslümanlara liderlik etmek için stratejik bir konum olarak edindiği Hendek Gazvesi ile olan yakın bağlantısından alır; öyle ki dağın gözetleme ve savunmadaki yüksek konumundan yararlanarak dağı ordunun arkasına, hendeği ise önüne koymuştur. Dağ ayrıca gazve sırasında Müslümanların kampının ve Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ gecelediği yerin mevkisiydi ve şehri Ahzab'ın (müttefiklerin) saldırılarından korumaya katkıda bulunmuştur. Sel Dağı, siyer (Hz. Peygamber'in hayatı) ile bağlantılı, en önde gelenleri Fetih Mescitleri ve Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ gecelediğine nispet edilen mağara olmak üzere, Seniyyetü'l-Vedâ'nın mevkisi ile olan bağlantısına ek olarak bir dizi tarihi simge yapıyı barındırmaktadır. Dağ günümüzde hala İslam tarihindeki en önemli askeri olaylardan birine önde gelen bir tanık ve Medine-i Münevvere'de önde gelen tarihi bir simge yapı olmaya devam etmektedir.||ID::"Gunung Sila'" adalah salah satu landmark alam dan sejarah paling menonjol di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan terletak di sebelah barat laut Masjid Nabawi pada jarak yang dekat darinya. Ia merupakan gunung berbatu besar dengan formasi granit kuno dan banyak jurang (lembah), yang sepanjang sejarah telah membentuk penghalang alami yang penting bagi kota. Kepentingannya bersumber dari keterkaitan eratnya dengan Perang Khandaq (Parit), di mana Nabi ﷺ menjadikannya sebagai posisi strategis untuk memimpin umat Islam, maka beliau menempatkan gunung di belakang pasukan dan parit di depannya, dengan memanfaatkan posisinya yang tinggi dalam pemantauan dan pertahanan. Gunung ini juga merupakan tempat untuk kamp umat Islam dan tempat menginap Nabi ﷺ selama peperangan, dan berkontribusi dalam melindungi kota dari serangan pasukan sekutu (Al-Ahzab). Gunung Sila' mencakup sejumlah landmark bersejarah yang terkait dengan Sirah Nabawiyah, yang paling menonjol di antaranya adalah Masjid-masjid Al-Fath, dan gua yang dinisbatkan sebagai tempat menginap Nabi ﷺ, di samping keterkaitannya dengan lokasi Tsaniyatul Wada'. Gunung ini hingga hari ini masih tetap menjadi saksi yang menonjol atas salah satu peristiwa militer paling penting dalam sejarah Islam, dan sebuah landmark bersejarah yang menonjol di Madinah Al-Munawwarah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/R5MPtok4DRNHV22S6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59929283407914,24.4755498774568,665.6877568060705</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الغمامة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد الغمامة يقع في الجهة الجنوبية الغربية من المسجد النبوي بالقرب من منطقة المناخة، ويُعد من المواضع التاريخية البارزة التي صلى فيها النبي ﷺ صلاتي العيد والاستسقاء، وهو في أصله ساحة مفتوحة كانت تُقام فيها الصلاة قبل أن يُبنى عليه مسجد لاحقاً. ارتبط اسمه بحدث الاستسقاء حيث قيل إن غمامة ظللت النبي ﷺ أثناء الصلاة، فغلب عليه اسم مسجد الغمامة. وقد بُني المسجد أول مرة في العهد الأموي ثم توالت عليه أعمال التجديد والترميم، وفي عهد حكومة خادم الحرمين الشريفين اهتمت بالمسجد واعتنت بالمنطقة المحيطة بها.||EN::"Masjid Al-Ghamamah" (Al-Ghamamah Mosque) is located in the southwestern side of the Prophet's Mosque near the Al-Manakhah area, and it is considered one of the prominent historical places where the Prophet ﷺ prayed the Eid and Istisqa (rain-seeking) prayers. It is originally an open square where the prayer used to be held before a mosque was built on it later. Its name was associated with the event of the Istisqa, where it was said that a cloud (ghamamah) shaded the Prophet ﷺ during the prayer, so the name Al-Ghamamah Mosque became dominant for it. The mosque was built for the first time in the Umayyad era, then works of renovation and restoration followed upon it, and in the era of the government of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques, it paid attention to the mosque and took care of the area surrounding it.||TR::Gamâme Mescidi, Mescid-i Nebevi'nin güneybatı tarafında, el-Manaha bölgesinin yakınında yer almaktadır ve Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ Bayram ve İstiska (yağmur duası) namazlarını kıldığı önde gelen tarihi yerlerden biri olarak kabul edilir. Ve aslı itibarıyla, daha sonra üzerine bir mescit inşa edilmeden önce içinde namazın kılındığı açık bir alandır (meydandır). Adı İstiska olayıyla ilişkilendirilmiştir; zira namaz sırasında Hz. Peygamber'i ﷺ bir bulutun (gamâme) gölgelediği söylenmiş, bu nedenle Gamâme Mescidi adı ona galip gelmiştir. Mescit ilk kez Emevi döneminde inşa edilmiş, ardından üzerine yenileme ve restorasyon çalışmaları birbirini izlemiştir ve İki Kutsal Caminin Hizmetkârı (Hâdimu'l-Haremeyni'ş-Şerîfeyn) hükümeti döneminde mescide önem verilmiş ve çevresindeki alanla ilgilenilmiştir.||ID::Masjid Al-Ghamamah terletak di sisi barat daya Masjid Nabawi di dekat kawasan Al-Manakhah, dan dianggap sebagai salah satu tempat bersejarah yang menonjol di mana Nabi ﷺ melaksanakan shalat Id dan Istisqa (memohon hujan). Pada asalnya ia adalah sebuah lapangan terbuka di mana shalat biasa didirikan sebelum sebuah masjid dibangun di atasnya di kemudian hari. Namanya dikaitkan dengan peristiwa Istisqa, di mana dikatakan bahwa sebuah awan (ghamamah) menaungi Nabi ﷺ selama shalat, sehingga nama Masjid Al-Ghamamah menjadi dominan baginya. Masjid ini dibangun untuk pertama kalinya pada era Umayyah kemudian pekerjaan pembaruan dan pemugaran berlanjut (berturut-turut) atasnya, dan pada era pemerintahan Pelayan Dua Tanah Suci (Khadimul Haramain Asy-Syarifain), ia memberikan perhatian kepada masjid tersebut dan merawat kawasan di sekitarnya.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/WAuct9k5UzAAAwwaA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60691411998654,24.46576529992775,604.1117421109293</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الفسح</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد الفسح من المساجد التاريخية الصغيرة في المدينة المنورة، يقع عند جبل أحد قرب شعب الجرار وتحت الغار المنسوب لأحداث غزوة أحد. لم يكن له اسم محدد في المصادر المبكرة، ثم عُرف لاحقاً باسم مسجد الفسح وانتشر هذا الاسم منذ القرن التاسع الهجري، ويُسمى أحياناً مسجد أحد. وقد اهتمت المملكة العربية السعودية بالعناية به من ضمن مشروع المحافظة على الأماكن التراثية||EN::Al-Fash Mosque is one of the small historical mosques in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located at Mount Uhud near Shi'b Al-Jarrar and under the cave attributed to the events of the Battle of Uhud. It did not have a specific name in early sources, then it was later known as Al-Fash Mosque, and this name spread since the ninth century AH, and it is sometimes called Uhud Mosque. The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has taken interest in caring for it as part of the project to preserve heritage places.||TR::Fesah Mescidi, Medine-i Münevvere'deki küçük tarihi mescitlerden biridir; Uhud Dağı'nda, Cerrar Şi'bi'nin yakınında ve Uhud Gazvesi olaylarına nispet edilen mağaranın altında yer alır. Erken dönem kaynaklarında belirli bir adı yoktu, daha sonra Fesah Mescidi adıyla bilindi ve bu isim Hicri dokuzuncu yüzyıldan itibaren yayıldı, bazen de Uhud Mescidi olarak adlandırılır. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı, miras alanlarını koruma projesi kapsamında ona özen göstermekle yakından ilgilenmiştir.||ID::Masjid Al-Fash adalah salah satu masjid bersejarah kecil di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, terletak di Gunung Uhud di dekat Syi'ib Al-Jarrar dan di bawah gua yang dinisbatkan pada peristiwa Perang Uhud. Ia tidak memiliki nama tertentu dalam sumber-sumber awal, kemudian belakangan dikenal dengan nama Masjid Al-Fash dan nama ini menyebar sejak abad kesembilan Hijriah, dan terkadang disebut Masjid Uhud. Dan Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah memberikan perhatian untuk merawatnya sebagai bagian dari proyek pelestarian tempat-tempat warisan.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/WpGuxymP3umKgp6V9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61288807512531,24.50999008157751,621.2440309756032</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل وعيرة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::جبل وعيرة هو سلسلة جبلية وعرة تنقسم لقطعتين (الكبرى والصغرى) وتقع شمال شرق جبل أحد وغرب المطار بالمدينة المنورة، وترتبط تاريخياً بالسيرة النبوية لوقوعها خلف ساحة غزوة أحد الشهيرة ودخولها ضمن نطاق حمى المدينة المنورة وحرمها الجغرافي الذي عظمه النبي ﷺ.||EN::Mount Wa'irah is a rugged mountain range that is divided into two pieces (the greater and the lesser), and is located northeast of Mount Uhud and west of the airport in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. It is historically linked to the Prophetic Biography due to its location behind the arena of the famous Battle of Uhud and its inclusion within the scope of the sanctuary (Hima) of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah and its geographical sacred precinct (Haram) which the Prophet ﷺ venerated.||TR::Va'ire Dağı, iki parçaya (Büyük ve Küçük) ayrılan engebeli bir sıradağdır ve Medine-i Münevvere'de Uhud Dağı'nın kuzeydoğusunda, havalimanının batısında yer alır. Meşhur Uhud Gazvesi meydanının arkasında bulunması ve Medine-i Münevvere'nin koruma alanı (Hima) ile Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ yücelttiği coğrafi hareminin (kutsal sınırının) kapsamına girmesi sebebiyle tarihi olarak Nebevi Siyer ile bağlantılıdır.||ID::Gunung Wa'irah adalah rangkaian pegunungan terjal di timur laut Gunung Uhud. Kawasan ini merupakan bagian dari lanskap bersejarah Madinah dan terkait dengan wilayah Perang Uhud serta batas suci kota yang ditetapkan pada masa Nabi.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/Tb9ZVZaHUk59dnye7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.66860926746156,24.56004612269548,1070.136430871569</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حصن الضحيان</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::الضحيان (الأطم الأسود) هو حصن جاهلي من الحجارة السوداء بناه أحيحة بن الجلاح في منطقة العصبة غرب مسجد قباء جنوب غرب المدينة المنورة، وكان يُرى من مسافات بعيدة بسبب ارتفاعه وبروزه على الحرة، وقد أعاد بناؤه بعد أن تهدّم أول مرة عندما شُيّد بحجارة بيضاء. يتميز بموقعه المرتفع وإشرافه على المنطقة المحيطة، ما جعله جزءاً من منظومة التحصين القديمة للمدينة في العصر الجاهلي، حيث استخدم كحصن دفاعي وسكن لسيد بني جحجبا، ولعب دوراً في صراعاتهم مع قبائل الأوس والخزرج، إذ ارتبط بعدة حوادث حربية وقصص تاريخية تبرز وظيفته العسكرية والحماية، منها صدّ الهجمات والاحتماء به أثناء النزاعات. ومع مرور الزمن تتابعت الإشارات إليه في كتب المؤرخين، وقد وصفه بعضهم بأنه كان بناءً ضخماً نسبياً (حوالي 27م طولاً و12م عرضاً)، إلا أنه تعرض للتدهور التدريجي بفعل العوامل الطبيعية والزحف العمراني حتى لم يبق منه اليوم إلا أساسات بسيطة وربوة الموقع، بينما بقيت بعض معالمه مثل بئر قديمة مجاورة له. ويُعد هذا الأطم من الشواهد التاريخية على نظام التحصينات في المدينة المنورة قبل الإسلام، وعلى طبيعة الحياة القبلية والصراعات التي كانت تدور في تلك الفترة. وقد حافظت المملكة العربية السعودية على الأماكن التراثية وذلك بإدخاله ضمن مشاريع تطوير الأماكن التاريخية||EN::Al-Dhahyan (The Black Fortress) is a pre-Islamic fortress made of black stones built by Uhayhah bin Al-Julah in the Al-Usbah area west of the Quba Mosque, southwest of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. It could be seen from long distances due to its height and prominence on the Harrah (volcanic field), and he rebuilt it after it collapsed the first time when it was constructed with white stones. It is distinguished by its elevated location and its overlooking of the surrounding area, making it part of the old fortification system of the city in the pre-Islamic era, where it was used as a defensive fortress and a residence for the master of Banu Jahjaba. It played a role in their conflicts with the Aws and Khazraj tribes, as it was associated with several war incidents and historical stories that highlight its military and protective function, including repelling attacks and taking shelter in it during disputes. With the passage of time, references to it continued in the books of historians, and some of them described it as a relatively massive structure (about 27m long and 12m wide), except that it was subjected to gradual deterioration due to natural factors and urban expansion until nothing remains of it today except simple foundations and the hill of the site, while some of its landmarks, such as an old well adjacent to it, remained. This fortress is considered one of the historical witnesses to the fortification system in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah before Islam, and to the nature of tribal life and the conflicts that took place in that period. The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has preserved heritage places by including it within the projects of developing historical places.||TR::Ed-Dahyan (Kara Kale), Medine-i Münevvere'nin güneybatısındaki Kuba Mescidi'nin batısında yer alan Asabe bölgesinde Uhayha bin el-Cülah tarafından siyah taşlardan inşa edilmiş İslam öncesi (Cahiliye dönemi) bir kaledir. Yüksekliği ve Harre (volkanik arazi) üzerindeki belirginliği nedeniyle uzak mesafelerden görülebiliyordu ve beyaz taşlarla inşa edildiğinde ilk kez yıkılmasının ardından onu yeniden inşa etmiştir. Yüksek konumu ve çevresindeki bölgeye hakim olmasıyla öne çıkar; bu da onu Cahiliye döneminde şehrin eski tahkimat sisteminin bir parçası yapmıştır, zira savunma kalesi ve Beni Cehceba efendisinin konutu olarak kullanılmış, Evs ve Hazrec kabileleriyle olan çatışmalarında rol oynamıştır. Çünkü saldırıları püskürtmek ve anlaşmazlıklar sırasında içine sığınmak da dahil olmak üzere, askeri ve koruma işlevini vurgulayan birçok savaş olayı ve tarihi hikaye ile ilişkilendirilmiştir. Zaman geçtikçe tarihçilerin kitaplarında ona yönelik atıflar birbirini izlemiş ve bazıları onu nispeten devasa bir yapı (yaklaşık 27m uzunluğunda ve 12m genişliğinde) olarak tanımlamıştır; ancak doğal faktörler ve kentsel genişleme nedeniyle kademeli bir bozulmaya maruz kalmış, öyle ki bugün ondan sadece basit temeller ve sit alanının tepesi kalmıştır, bitişiğindeki eski bir kuyu gibi bazı kalıntıları ise ayakta kalmıştır. Bu kale, İslam öncesi Medine-i Münevvere'deki tahkimat sisteminin ve o dönemde meydana gelen kabile hayatının doğasının ve çatışmaların tarihi tanıklarından biri olarak kabul edilir. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı, onu tarihi mekanları geliştirme projelerine dahil ederek miras alanlarını korumuştur.||ID::Ad-Dhahyan (Benteng Hitam) adalah sebuah benteng pra-Islam dari batu-batu hitam yang dibangun oleh Uhayhah bin Al-Julah di daerah Al-'Usbah di sebelah barat Masjid Quba, barat daya Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Ia dapat dilihat dari jarak jauh karena ketinggiannya dan penonjolannya di atas Harrah (medan vulkanik), dan ia membangunnya kembali setelah runtuh pertama kalinya ketika dibangun dengan batu-batu putih. Ia dibedakan oleh lokasinya yang tinggi dan pengawasannya terhadap daerah sekitarnya, yang menjadikannya bagian dari sistem pertahanan kuno kota pada zaman pra-Islam, di mana ia digunakan sebagai benteng pertahanan dan tempat tinggal bagi pemimpin Bani Jahjaba, serta memainkan peran dalam konflik mereka dengan suku Aus dan Khazraj, karena ia terkait dengan beberapa insiden perang dan cerita sejarah yang menyoroti fungsi militer dan perlindungannya, termasuk menangkis serangan dan berlindung di dalamnya selama perselisihan. Seiring berjalannya waktu, penyebutan tentangnya terus berlanjut di buku-buku para sejarawan, dan beberapa dari mereka menggambarkannya sebagai bangunan yang relatif besar (panjang sekitar 27m dan lebar 12m), akan tetapi ia mengalami kemerosotan bertahap akibat faktor-faktor alam dan perluasan kota sehingga tidak ada yang tersisa darinya hari ini kecuali fondasi sederhana dan bukit situs tersebut, sementara beberapa tengaranya seperti sumur tua yang berdekatan dengannya tetap ada. Benteng ini dianggap sebagai salah satu saksi sejarah sistem pertahanan di Madinah Al-Munawwarah sebelum Islam, dan sifat kehidupan suku serta konflik yang terjadi pada masa itu. Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah melestarikan tempat-tempat warisan dengan memasukkannya ke dalam proyek-proyek pengembangan tempat-tempat bersejarah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/cnp5kwTfPjbqMkxr9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60634043597972,24.43307290752997,609.7103571461652</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حصن راتج</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::راتج هو أطم (حصن قديم) من آطام المدينة المنورة، كان يقع شمال شرق جبل ذباب في منطقة المصانع تقريباً، وكان من التحصينات التي استخدمتها القبائل قديماً للدفاع عن مساكنها. اختلفت الروايات حول أصله وملكيته، لكنه ارتبط بمجموعات سكنت المنطقة في فترات مختلفة، ويُرجح أنه أقدم من الاستقرار العربي الكامل فيها.كان لراتج دور في الأحداث العسكرية حول المدينة، خاصة في غزوة الخندق، حيث كان ضمن نطاق المنطقة التي مر بها الخندق، كما ارتبط لاحقاً بأحداث وقعة الحرة في العصر الأموي. وقد اندثر الأطم تماماً اليوم ولم يبق منه أثر ظاهر، وبقي فقط اسمه في المصادر التاريخية كشاهد على نظام الدفاع القديم في المدينة.||EN::Ratj is an utum (ancient fortress) among the fortresses of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah; it was located northeast of Mount Dhubab approximately in the Al-Masanai area, and it was one of the fortifications that the tribes used in ancient times to defend their dwellings. Narrations differed about its origin and ownership, but it was associated with groups that inhabited the region in different periods, and it is likely that it is older than the complete Arab settlement in it. Ratj had a role in the military events around the city, especially in the Battle of the Trench, where it was within the scope of the area through which the trench passed, as it was also later associated with the events of the Battle of Al-Harrah in the Umayyad era. The fortress has completely disappeared today and no visible trace of it remains, and only its name remains in historical sources as a witness to the ancient defense system in the city.||TR::Ratic, Medine-i Münevvere'nin utumlarından (eski kalelerinden) bir utumdur (eski kaledir); yaklaşık olarak el-Mesani bölgesinde, Zübab Dağı'nın kuzeydoğusunda yer alıyordu ve eski çağlarda kabilelerin meskenlerini savunmak için kullandıkları tahkimatlardan biriydi. Kökeni ve mülkiyeti hakkındaki rivayetler farklılık göstermiştir, ancak farklı dönemlerde bölgede yaşayan gruplarla ilişkilendirilmiştir ve büyük olasılıkla oradaki tam Arap yerleşiminden daha eskidir. Ratic'in şehrin etrafındaki askeri olaylarda, özellikle de hendeğin geçtiği bölgenin sınırları içinde olduğu Hendek Gazvesi'nde bir rolü vardı; ayrıca daha sonra Emevi dönemindeki Harre Vakası olaylarıyla da ilişkilendirilmiştir. Kale bugün tamamen yok olmuştur ve ondan görünür hiçbir iz kalmamıştır; şehirdeki eski savunma sisteminin bir tanığı olarak sadece adı tarihi kaynaklarda kalmıştır.||ID::Ratj adalah sebuah utum (benteng kuno) dari benteng-benteng di Madinah Al-Munawwarah; ia terletak di sebelah timur laut Gunung Dhubab, kira-kira di wilayah Al-Masanai, dan merupakan salah satu benteng yang digunakan oleh kabilah-kabilah pada zaman dahulu untuk mempertahankan tempat tinggal mereka. Riwayat-riwayat berbeda mengenai asal-usul dan kepemilikannya, tetapi ia dikaitkan dengan kelompok-kelompok yang mendiami wilayah tersebut pada periode-periode yang berbeda, dan kemungkinan besar ia lebih tua dari pemukiman Arab seutuhnya di sana. Ratj memiliki peran dalam peristiwa-peristiwa militer di sekitar kota, terutama dalam Perang Khandaq, di mana ia berada di dalam ruang lingkup wilayah yang dilewati oleh parit tersebut, sebagaimana ia juga belakangan dikaitkan dengan peristiwa-peristiwa Perang Al-Harrah pada era Umayyah. Benteng tersebut telah lenyap sepenuhnya hari ini dan tidak ada jejak yang terlihat yang tersisa darinya, dan hanya namanya yang tersisa di sumber-sumber sejarah sebagai saksi bagi sistem pertahanan kuno di kota tersebut.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/VxWdH2fJDPMdg15F9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60958573811864,24.4798200918135,599.9919408146576</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حرة الوبرة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::حرة الوَبَرة هي إحدى الحرات السوداء المحيطة بالمدينة المنورة، تقع في الجهة الغربية على بعد نحو ثلاثة أميال من المسجد النبوي، وتمتد من جنوب المدينة عند قباء حتى شمالها عند مسجد القبلتين، وتعد جزءاً من اللابتين اللتين تحيطان بالمدينة. تتميز بتضاريس بركانية فيها تلال ومنخفضات وشقوق وأودية تتجمع فيها مياه الأمطار، مما جعل بعض مناطقها صالحة للسكن قديماً، بينما أصبحت اليوم ضمن النطاق العمراني بعد استصلاح معظم أراضيها. وتكتسب هذه الحرة أهمية تاريخية ودينية لكونها من حدود حرم المدينة، وارتباطها بعدد من أحداث السيرة النبوية، كما تضم معالم بارزة مثل مسجد القبلتين ومناطق بني سلمة وعدد من الآبار والأماكن التاريخية، مما يجعلها من أبرز المعالم الجغرافية والتاريخية في المدينة المنورة.||EN::Harrah Al-Wabarah is one of the black harrahs (volcanic fields) surrounding Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located in the western side at a distance of about three miles from the Prophet's Mosque, and it extends from the south of the city at Quba to its north at the Qiblatain Mosque, and it is considered part of the two labahs (lava tracts) that surround the city. It is distinguished by volcanic terrain in which there are hills, depressions, fissures, and valleys where rainwater gathers, which made some of its areas suitable for habitation in ancient times, while today it has become within the urban scope after the reclamation of most of its lands. This harrah gains historical and religious importance for being one of the boundaries of the city's sanctuary (Haram), and its association with a number of events of the Prophetic Biography, as it also includes prominent landmarks such as the Qiblatain Mosque, the areas of Banu Salamah, and a number of wells and historical places, which makes it one of the most prominent geographical and historical landmarks in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah.||TR::Harretü'l-Vebera, Medine-i Münevvere'yi çevreleyen siyah harrelerden (volkanik alanlardan) biridir; batı yönünde, Mescid-i Nebevi'den yaklaşık üç mil uzaklıkta yer alır ve şehrin güneyinde Kuba'dan kuzeyinde Kıbleteyn Mescidi'ne kadar uzanır ve şehri çevreleyen iki labenin (lav akıntısının) bir parçası olarak kabul edilir. İçinde yağmur sularının toplandığı tepeler, çukurlar, çatlaklar ve vadiler bulunan volkanik bir arazi yapısıyla öne çıkar, ki bu da eski zamanlarda bazı bölgelerini yaşama elverişli kılmıştır, oysa bugün arazilerinin çoğunun ıslah edilmesinden sonra kentsel alanın (imar sınırının) içine girmiştir. Bu harre, şehrin hareminin (kutsal sınırlarının) sınırlarından biri olması ve Nebevi Siyer'in bir dizi olayıyla bağlantısı sebebiyle tarihi ve dini bir önem kazanır; ayrıca Kıbleteyn Mescidi, Beni Seleme bölgeleri ve bir dizi kuyu ve tarihi mekan gibi önemli simge yapıları da içerir, ki bu da onu Medine-i Münevvere'deki en belirgin coğrafi ve tarihi simgelerden biri yapar.||ID::Harrah Al-Wabarah adalah salah satu harrah (medan vulkanik) hitam yang mengelilingi Madinah Al-Munawwarah, terletak di arah barat pada jarak sekitar tiga mil dari Masjid Nabawi, dan ia membentang dari selatan kota di Quba hingga ke utaranya di Masjid Qiblatain, dan dianggap sebagai bagian dari dua labah (bidang lava) yang mengelilingi kota tersebut. Ia dibedakan oleh topografi vulkanik di mana terdapat bukit-bukit, lekukan-lekukan, celah-celah, dan lembah-lembah tempat berkumpulnya air hujan, yang menjadikan beberapa wilayahnya cocok untuk tempat tinggal pada zaman dahulu, sementara saat ini ia telah berada di dalam lingkup perkotaan setelah reklamasi (pemulihan) sebagian besar tanahnya. Harrah ini memperoleh kepentingan sejarah dan agama karena ia merupakan salah satu dari batas-batas wilayah suci (Haram) kota, dan hubungannya dengan sejumlah peristiwa Sirah Nabawiyah, sebagaimana ia juga mencakup tengara-tengara (landmark) menonjol seperti Masjid Qiblatain, wilayah Bani Salamah, dan sejumlah sumur serta tempat-tempat bersejarah, yang menjadikannya salah satu tengara geografis dan sejarah yang paling menonjol di Madinah Al-Munawwarah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/Dudj2PpEegnfMjseA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.58838997559637,24.45394018856468,634.453482216247</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>أطم صرار</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::صِرار هو حصن قديم يقع شرق المدينة المنورة، بُني الأطم من حجارة الحرة السوداء على مرتفع بارز يزيد عن محيطه.وهو من آطام بني عبد الأشهل في الجاهلية، ثم ارتبط بعد الهجرة النبوية بعدد من الأحداث التاريخية المهمة، إذ نزل به النبي ﷺ في بعض غزواته، كما وردت فيه وقائع تتعلق بالصحابة كعمر بن الخطاب رضي الله عنه أثناء تجهيز الجيوش، إضافة إلى أحداث لاحقة في صدر الإسلام.||EN::Sirar is an ancient fortress located east of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah; the utum (fortress) was built from the black stones of the Harrah (volcanic field) on a prominent elevation that is higher than its surroundings. It is one of the fortresses of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal in the pre-Islamic era, then it was associated after the Prophetic Migration with a number of important historical events, as the Prophet ﷺ camped at it in some of his expeditions. Likewise, incidents occurred in it relating to the Companions, such as 'Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, during the preparation of the armies, in addition to subsequent events in the early days of Islam.||TR::Sirar, Medine-i Münevvere'nin doğusunda yer alan eski bir kaledir; utum (kale), çevresinden daha yüksek olan belirgin bir yükselti üzerinde siyah harre (volkanik alan) taşlarından inşa edilmiştir. O, Cahiliye döneminde Beni Abdüleşhel'in kalelerinden biridir; daha sonra Nebevi Hicret'in ardından bir dizi önemli tarihi olayla ilişkilendirilmiştir, zira Hz. Peygamber ﷺ bazı gazvelerinde (seferlerinde) orada konaklamıştır. Nitekim orduların hazırlanması (teçhiz edilmesi) sırasında Ömer bin Hattab (Allah ondan razı olsun) gibi sahabelerle ilgili olayların orada geçtiği gibi, ayrıca İslam'ın ilk dönemlerindeki (sadru'l-İslam) sonraki olaylara ek olarak.||ID::Sirar adalah sebuah benteng kuno yang terletak di sebelah timur Madinah Al-Munawwarah; utum (benteng) tersebut dibangun dari batu-batu hitam harrah (medan vulkanik) di atas dataran tinggi menonjol yang lebih tinggi dari sekitarnya. Dan ia termasuk dari benteng-benteng Bani 'Abd al-Ashhal pada zaman pra-Islam (Jahiliyah), kemudian ia dikaitkan setelah Hijrah Nabawiyah dengan sejumlah peristiwa sejarah yang penting, karena Nabi ﷺ singgah (berkemah) di sana dalam beberapa peperangannya (ekspedisinya). Sebagaimana juga terjadi di dalamnya insiden-insiden yang berkaitan dengan para Sahabat seperti 'Umar bin Al-Khattab radhiyallahu 'anhu selama persiapan pasukan, sebagai tambahan pada peristiwa-peristiwa selanjutnya di masa-masa awal Islam.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/VJAfu7CEJs5CEkvJ7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.64519704630376,24.48670395780245,611.1867355664966</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>ذات الجيش</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::ذات الجيش موضع تاريخي يقع جنوب غرب المدينة المنورة بعد ذي الحليفة على طريق مكة القديم، وهو وادٍ وسهل فسيح كانت تمر به القوافل.يُعد من المواضع القديمة المعروفة في طريق السفر بين مكة والمدينة، وورد ذكره في عدد من الوقائع التاريخية المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية، كما كان من منازل الطريق ومحطات التوقف للقوافل والمسافرين.||EN::Dhat al-Jaysh is a historical place located southwest of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah after Dhu al-Hulayfah on the old Makkah road, and it is a valley and a spacious plain through which caravans used to pass. It is considered one of the known ancient places on the travel route between Makkah and Al-Madinah, and it was mentioned in a number of historical events associated with the Prophetic Biography, as it was also one of the waystations and stopovers for caravans and travelers.||TR::Zatü'l-Ceyş, Medine-i Münevvere'nin güneybatısında, eski Mekke yolu üzerindeki Zülhuleyfe'den sonra yer alan tarihi bir yerdir ve kervanların içinden geçtiği bir vadi ve geniş bir ovadır. Mekke ile Medine arasındaki seyahat güzergahında bilinen eski yerlerden biri olarak kabul edilir ve Nebevi Siyer ile bağlantılı bir dizi tarihi olayda zikredilmiştir; tıpkı kervanlar ve yolcular için yol konaklama yerlerinden ve duraklarından biri olduğu gibi.||ID::Dhat al-Jaysh adalah sebuah tempat bersejarah yang terletak di barat daya Madinah Al-Munawwarah setelah Dzulhulaifah di jalan lama Makkah, dan ia adalah sebuah lembah dan dataran luas yang dilalui oleh karavan-karavan. Ia dianggap sebagai salah satu tempat kuno yang dikenal di rute perjalanan antara Makkah dan Madinah, dan telah disebutkan dalam sejumlah peristiwa sejarah yang berkaitan dengan Sirah Nabawiyah, sebagaimana ia juga merupakan salah satu tempat persinggahan dan tempat perhentian bagi karavan-karavan dan para pelancong.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/HYmZATXTKRX9ZapGA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.47771082686548,24.38055049913562,729.5435155709728</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حرة واقم</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::حرة واقم (الحرة الشرقية) هي منطقة بركانية واسعة تقع شرق المدينة المنورة، وتمتد من جهة وادي بطحان شمالاً حتى أطراف جبل أحد وما يقابله من الجهات الشرقية للمدينة. سُمّيت بـ“واقم” نسبة إلى أطم واقم أحد الآطام القديمة في المنطقة، وتُعرف أيضاً بعدة تسميات فرعية بحسب القبائل التي سكنت أطرافها.تتكون من صخور وحمم بركانية سوداء جعلت سطحها حاراً وقاسياً، وتُعد من اللابتين المحيطتين بالمدينة، وتشكل حاجزاً طبيعياً من جهتها الشرقية. تضم عدداً من الأودية والجبال مثل وادي بطحان والعقيق وجبل أحد، وكانت منطقة سكنى لعدد من قبائل الأوس والخزرج وبعض القبائل اليهودية قديماً.ارتبطت الحرة بأحداث تاريخية مهمة، إذ تُعد من حدود حرم المدينة، وشهدت وقائع بارزة في التاريخ الإسلامي، كما عرفت بنشاطها البركاني في فترات تاريخية مختلفة. وتُعد اليوم من المناطق التي امتدت إليها عمران المدينة بشكل واسع.||EN::Harrah Waqim (The Eastern Harrah) is a vast volcanic area located east of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, and it extends from the direction of Wadi Buthan in the north to the edges of Mount Uhud and what faces it from the eastern sides of the city. It was named "Waqim" in relation to the Utum (fortress) of Waqim, one of the ancient fortresses in the region, and it is also known by several sub-names according to the tribes that inhabited its edges. It consists of black volcanic rocks and lava that made its surface hot and harsh, and it is considered one of the two labahs (lava tracts) surrounding the city, and it forms a natural barrier from its eastern side. It includes a number of valleys and mountains such as Wadi Buthan, Al-Aqiq, and Mount Uhud, and it was a residential area for a number of the Aws and Khazraj tribes and some Jewish tribes in ancient times. The Harrah was associated with important historical events, as it is considered one of the boundaries of the city's sanctuary (Haram), and it witnessed prominent incidents in Islamic history, just as it was known for its volcanic activity in different historical periods. And today it is considered one of the areas to which the urban expansion of the city has widely extended.||TR::Harretü Vakım (Doğu Harresi), Medine-i Münevvere'nin doğusunda yer alan geniş bir volkanik alandır ve kuzeyde Buthan Vadisi yönünden Uhud Dağı'nın eteklerine ve şehrin doğu yönlerinden onun karşısına denk gelen yerlere kadar uzanır. Bölgedeki eski kalelerden (utumlardan) biri olan Vakım kalesine (utumuna) nispetle "Vakım" olarak adlandırılmıştır ve etraflarında (kenarlarında) yaşayan kabilelere göre çeşitli alt isimlerle de bilinir. Yüzeyini sıcak ve sert (zorlu) hale getiren siyah volkanik kayalar ve lavlardan oluşur ve şehri çevreleyen iki labeden (lav akıntısından) biri olarak kabul edilir ve doğu yönünden doğal bir bariyer oluşturur. Buthan Vadisi, Akik ve Uhud Dağı gibi bir dizi vadi ve dağı içerir ve eski zamanlarda Evs ve Hazrec kabilelerinden birçoğu ile bazı Yahudi kabileleri için bir yerleşim bölgesiydi. Harre, şehrin hareminin (kutsal sınırlarının) sınırlarından biri olarak kabul edildiği için önemli tarihi olaylarla ilişkilendirilmiştir ve İslam tarihinde belirgin vakalara tanık olmuştur, tıpkı farklı tarihi dönemlerdeki volkanik aktivitesiyle bilindiği gibi. Ve bugün, şehrin kentleşmesinin (imarının) geniş çapta yayıldığı bölgelerden biri olarak kabul edilmektedir.||ID::Harrah Waqim (Harrah Timur) adalah kawasan vulkanik luas yang terletak di sebelah timur Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan membentang dari arah Lembah (Wadi) Buthan di utara hingga ke pinggiran Gunung Uhud dan apa yang menghadapnya dari sisi-sisi timur kota. Ia dinamakan "Waqim" dinisbatkan pada utum (benteng) Waqim, salah satu benteng kuno di wilayah tersebut, dan ia juga dikenal dengan beberapa penamaan cabang (sub-nama) menurut kabilah-kabilah yang mendiami pinggirannya. Ia terdiri dari batu-batu dan lava vulkanik hitam yang membuat permukaannya panas dan keras, dan ia dianggap sebagai salah satu dari dua labah (bidang lava) yang mengelilingi kota, dan membentuk penghalang alami dari sisi timurnya. Ia mencakup sejumlah lembah dan gunung seperti Lembah Buthan, Al-Aqiq, dan Gunung Uhud, dan ia merupakan kawasan tempat tinggal bagi sejumlah kabilah Aus dan Khazraj serta beberapa kabilah Yahudi pada zaman dahulu. Harrah tersebut dikaitkan dengan peristiwa-peristiwa sejarah yang penting, karena ia dianggap sebagai salah satu dari batas-batas wilayah suci (Haram) kota, dan ia menyaksikan insiden-insiden menonjol dalam sejarah Islam, sebagaimana ia dikenal dengan aktivitas vulkaniknya pada periode-periode sejarah yang berbeda. Dan hari ini ia dianggap sebagai salah satu kawasan di mana perluasan perkotaan (pembangunan) kota telah meluas secara luas.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/4D7gDjH6HABZurox8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.76226274685699,24.35083378656112,853.2664316188826</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>روضة خاخ</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::خاخ (روضة خاخ) موضع بين مكة والمدينة قرب وادي العقيق وحمراء الأسد، وهو روضة معروفة بكثرة الماء والخضرة، وكان ضمن طريق السفر بين المدينتين.أبرز ما ورد عنه في السيرة النبوية أن النبي ﷺ أرسل علي بن أبي طالب والزبير بن العوام والمقداد بن الأسود إلى هذا الموضع، فوجدوا امرأة معها رسالة مخفية، فأخذوها وأحضروها للنبي ﷺ، فإذا فيها كتاب من حاطب بن أبي بلتعة إلى أهل مكة يُخبرهم ببعض أمر النبي ﷺ، وهي الحادثة المعروفة في كتب الحديث والسيرة بواقعة كتاب حاطب بن أبي بلتعة.||EN::Khakh (Rawdat Khakh) is a place between Makkah and Al-Madinah near Wadi Al-Aqiq and Hamra Al-Asad, and it is a rawdah (meadow) known for its abundance of water and greenery, and it was within the travel route between the two cities. The most prominent of what was mentioned about it in the Prophetic Biography is that the Prophet ﷺ sent 'Ali bin Abi Talib, Al-Zubayr bin Al-'Awwam, and Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad to this place, so they found a woman with a hidden letter, so they took it and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ, and behold, in it was a letter from Hatib bin Abi Balta'ah to the people of Makkah informing them of some of the affairs of the Prophet ﷺ, and it is the incident known in the books of Hadith and Biography as the incident of the letter of Hatib bin Abi Balta'ah.||TR::Hah (Ravzatü Hah), Mekke ile Medine arasında, Akik Vadisi ve Hamraü'l-Esed yakınlarında bir yerdir ve suyunun ve yeşilliğinin bolluğu ile bilinen bir ravzadır (çayır/bahçe) ve iki şehir arasındaki seyahat güzergahı dahilindeydi. Nebevi Siyer'de onun hakkında zikredilenlerin en belirgini, Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ Ali bin Ebi Talip, Zübeyr bin Avvam ve Mikdad bin Esved'i bu yere göndermesidir; böylece (orada) yanında gizlenmiş bir mektup olan bir kadın buldular, onu aldılar ve Hz. Peygamber'e ﷺ getirdiler. Bir de ne görsünler, içinde Hatıb bin Ebi Beltea'dan Mekke halkına, onlara Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ bazı işlerini (durumlarını) haber veren bir mektup vardı ve bu, Hadis ve Siyer kitaplarında Hatıb bin Ebi Beltea'nın mektubu vakası olarak bilinen olaydır.||ID::Khakh (Rawdah Khakh) adalah sebuah tempat antara Makkah dan Madinah di dekat Lembah (Wadi) Al-Aqiq dan Hamra Al-Asad, dan ia adalah sebuah rawdah (padang rumput/taman) yang dikenal dengan banyaknya air dan tanaman hijau, dan ia berada di dalam rute perjalanan antara kedua kota tersebut. Hal paling menonjol dari apa yang disebutkan tentangnya dalam Sirah Nabawiyah adalah bahwa Nabi ﷺ mengutus 'Ali bin Abi Thalib, Az-Zubair bin Al-'Awwam, dan Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad ke tempat ini, maka mereka menemukan seorang wanita yang membawa surat tersembunyi, lalu mereka mengambilnya dan membawanya kepada Nabi ﷺ, dan tiba-tiba di dalamnya terdapat sebuah surat dari Hatib bin Abi Balta'ah kepada penduduk Makkah yang mengabarkan kepada mereka tentang beberapa urusan Nabi ﷺ, dan itu adalah insiden yang dikenal dalam kitab-kitab Hadits dan Sirah sebagai peristiwa surat Hatib bin Abi Balta'ah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/VJGWJEPM2ntsK75i8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.56791520825504,24.31710666294782,651.7353474736551</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد بني دينار الأدنى</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد بني دينار من المساجد التاريخية في جنوب المدينة المنورة، يقع غرب وادي بطحان في منطقة المغيسلة (المالحة) على بعد يقارب كيلومترًا من المسجد النبوي. يُنسب إلى بني دينار من الخزرج، الذين سكنوا تلك الناحية، وكان موضعًا لمنازلهم وأحد مساجدهم القديمة.يرتبط المسجد بالسيرة النبوية بكونه من المواضع التي صلى فيها النبي ﷺ، فبُني في مكان صلاته، ثم استمر معروفًا عبر العصور، وأعيد بناؤه في عهد الخليفة عمر بن عبد العزيز أثناء ولايته على المدينة.وقد رعت المملكة العربية السعودية هذا المسجد واعتنت به من ضمن مشاريع المحافظة على المساجد||EN::Banu Dinar Mosque is one of the historical mosques in the south of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located west of Wadi Buthan in the Al-Mughaysilah (Al-Malihah) area at a distance of approximately one kilometer from the Prophet's Mosque. It is attributed to Banu Dinar of the Khazraj, who inhabited that area, and it was a site for their homes and one of their ancient mosques. The mosque is associated with the Prophetic Biography by being one of the places in which the Prophet ﷺ prayed, so it was built in the place of his prayer, then it continued to be known throughout the ages, and it was rebuilt in the era of Caliph 'Umar bin 'Abd al-'Aziz during his governorship over the city. And the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has sponsored this mosque and taken care of it as part of the projects of preserving mosques.||TR::Beni Dinar Mescidi, Medine-i Münevvere'nin güneyindeki tarihi mescitlerden biridir; Buthan Vadisi'nin batısında, el-Muğaysile (el-Maliha) bölgesinde, Mescid-i Nebevi'den yaklaşık bir kilometre uzaklıkta yer alır. O yörede yaşayan Hazrec'den Beni Dinar'a nispet edilir ve onların evlerinin bir yeri ve eski mescitlerinden biriydi. Mescit, Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ içinde namaz kıldığı yerlerden biri olması sebebiyle Nebevi Siyer ile ilişkilendirilir; bu yüzden namaz kıldığı yere inşa edildi, sonra çağlar boyunca bilinmeye devam etti ve şehre valiliği sırasında Halife Ömer bin Abdülaziz döneminde yeniden inşa edildi. Ve Suudi Arabistan Krallığı, bu mescidin himayesini üstlenmiş ve mescitleri koruma projeleri kapsamında ona özen göstermiştir.||ID::Masjid Bani Dinar adalah salah satu masjid bersejarah di selatan Madinah Al-Munawwarah, terletak di sebelah barat Lembah (Wadi) Buthan di daerah Al-Mughaysilah (Al-Malihah) pada jarak sekitar satu kilometer dari Masjid Nabawi. Ia dinisbatkan kepada Bani Dinar dari Khazraj, yang mendiami daerah tersebut, dan ia merupakan tempat bagi rumah-rumah mereka dan salah satu dari masjid-masjid kuno mereka. Masjid tersebut dikaitkan dengan Sirah Nabawiyah dengan keberadaannya sebagai salah satu tempat di mana Nabi ﷺ shalat di dalamnya, maka ia dibangun di tempat shalatnya, kemudian ia terus dikenal sepanjang zaman, dan ia dibangun kembali pada era Khalifah 'Umar bin 'Abd al-'Aziz selama masa jabatannya sebagai gubernur atas kota tersebut. Dan Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah merawat masjid ini dan memperhatikannya sebagai bagian dari proyek-proyek pemeliharaan masjid-masjid.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/WVZJEGLnRceawFCz5]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60340303567847,24.45567714946684,617.3360766070776</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>زغابة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::زغابة موضع تاريخي قريب من المدينة المنورة عند ملتقى السيول في آخر وادي العقيق غرب المدينة، حيث تجتمع فيه مياه أودية بطحان وقناة والعقيق، ويُعد من أبرز مجاري السيول في المنطقة. وقد حافظت على هذا الإسم منذ العهد النبوي||EN::"Zughabah is a historical site near Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah at the confluence of torrents at the end of Wadi Al-Aqiq, west of the city, where the waters of the valleys of Bathan, Qanat, and Al-Aqiq meet. It is considered one of the most prominent torrent courses in the region, and it has kept this name since the prophetic era."||TR::"Zuğabe, Medine-i Münevvere'ye yakın, şehrin batısındaki Akik Vadisi'nin sonunda, Bathan, Kanat ve Akik vadilerinin sularının birleştiği sel kavşağında yer alan tarihi bir yerdir. Bölgedeki en belirgin sel yataklarından biri olarak kabul edilir ve Nebi döneminden beri bu adını korumuştur."||ID::"Zughabah adalah situs bersejarah yang terletak dekat Madinah Al-Munawwarah pada pertemuan aliran banjir di ujung Wadi Al-Aqiq, sebelah barat kota, di mana air dari lembah Bathan, Qanat, dan Al-Aqiq bertemu. Tempat ini dianggap sebagai salah satu jalur aliran banjir paling menonjol di wilayah tersebut, dan telah mempertahankan nama ini sejak masa kenabian."||MAPS::]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.58585346896972,24.54132840698249,585.3122269078815</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>الغابة أرض الزبير بن العوام</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::الغابة موضع يقع شمال المدينة المنورة وسُمّيت بذلك لكثرة أشجارها ومياهها. تمتد في منطقة الخليل حيث تلتقي بعض أودية المدينة، وكانت قديماً أرضاً خصبة غنية بالنخيل والزراعة، ومن أملاك الصحابي الزبير بن العوام الذي استثمرها فازدادت قيمتها. مع مرور الزمن تراجعت زراعتها وتعرضت للإهمال بسبب السيول التي كوّنت فيها أخاديد وأحراشاً كثيفة، ثم عادت إليها الحياة الحديثة في عهد المملكة العربية السعودية فأصبحت تضم طرقاً ومزارع ومساكن، وتشمل منطقة الخليل وما حولها. وللغابة أهمية تاريخية في عصر النبوة؛ فقد كانت من مراعي إبل النبي ﷺ، ومنها انطلقت بعض سباقات الخيل التي أشرف عليها، كما ارتبطت بـ غزوة ذي قرد. كذلك امتلك فيها بعض كبار الصحابة أراضي ومزارع كالعباس بن عبدالمطلب رضي الله عنه لوفرة المياه وخصوبة التربة.||EN::"Al-Ghabah is a location situated north of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, named as such due to the abundance of its trees and water. It extends into the Al-Khalil area where some of the valleys of Madinah converge. In ancient times, it was fertile land rich in palm trees and agriculture, and it was among the properties of the Companion Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, who invested in it, thereby increasing its value. With the passage of time, its agriculture declined and it suffered from neglect due to torrents that formed gullies and dense thickets within it. Modern life then returned to it during the era of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, so it came to encompass roads, farms, and residences, including the Al-Khalil area and its surroundings. Al-Ghabah holds historical significance in the prophetic era; it was one of the grazing grounds for the camels of the Prophet (PBUH), from it some of the horse races supervised by him were launched, and it was associated with the Battle of Dhu Qarad. Likewise, some senior Companions owned lands and farms in it, such as Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him), due to the abundance of water and the fertility of the soil."||TR::"El-Gabe, Medine-i Münevvere'nin kuzeyinde yer alan, ağaçlarının ve suyunun çok olması sebebiyle bu adı almış bir yerdir. Medine'nin bazı vadilerinin birleştiği Halil bölgesinde uzanır. Eskiden hurma ağaçları ve tarım açısından zengin, verimli bir arazi idi ve buraya yatırım yaparak değerini artıran Sahabi Zübeyir bin Avvam'ın mülkleri arasındaydı. Zamanla tarımı geriledi ve içerisinde hendekler ve yoğun çalılıklar oluşturan seller nedeniyle ihmale uğradı. Daha sonra Suudi Arabistan Krallığı döneminde buraya modern hayat geri döndü; yolları, çiftlikleri ve meskenleri içine alacak şekilde gelişti ve Halil bölgesi ile çevresini kapsadı. Gabe'nin nebat devrinde tarihi bir önemi vardır; Hz. Peygamber'in (sav) develerinin otlaklarından biriydi, bizzat denetlediği bazı at yarışları buradan başlamıştı ve Zü Kered Gazvesi ile ilişkilendirilmiştir. Aynı şekilde, suyunun bol ve toprağının verimli olması nedeniyle Abbas bin Abdülmuttalib (radıyallahu anh) gibi bazı büyük sahabeler de burada arazi ve çiftliklere sahip olmuşlardır."||ID::"Al-Ghabah adalah sebuah tempat yang terletak di sebelah utara Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dinamakan demikian karena banyaknya pepohonan dan air di sana. Tempat ini membentang di wilayah Al-Khalil di mana beberapa lembah Madinah bertemu. Pada masa lampau, tempat ini merupakan tanah subur yang kaya akan pohon kurma dan pertanian, serta termasuk di antara harta milik Sahabat Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam yang mengelolanya sehingga nilainya semakin meningkat. Seiring berjalannya waktu, pertaniannya mengalami kemunduran dan menjadi terbengkalai akibat banjir yang membentuk jurang-jurang serta belukar yang lebat di dalamnya. Kehidupan modern kemudian kembali ke tempat tersebut pada era Kerajaan Arab Saudi, sehingga kini mencakup jalan-jalan, lahan pertanian, dan pemukiman, serta meliputi wilayah Al-Khalil dan sekitarnya. Al-Ghabah memiliki kepentingan historis pada masa kenabian; tempat itu merupakan salah satu tempat penggembalaan unta Nabi (SAW), darinya beberapa perlombaan kuda yang diawasi oleh beliau diberangkatkan, dan tempat itu terkait dengan Perang Dhu Qarad. Demikian pula, beberapa Sahabat senior memiliki tanah dan perkebunan di sana, seperti Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muthalib (semoga Allah meridhainya), karena kelimpahan air dan kesuburan tanahnya.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/6w6R5X7Dq3cRUGZR9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.56894795044013,24.59384506060086,577.6006292142151</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد بني دينار الأعلى</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد بني دينار الأعلى أحد المساجد التاريخية في المدينة المنورة، ويقع في ديار بني دينار بالحرة، ويُعرف أيضاً باسم مسجد المنارتين نسبة إلى جبلين أصفرين شمال الحرة، يقع المسجد على طريق عمر بن الخطاب (العنبرية سابقاً)، على بُعد نحو 2.8 كم من المسجد النبوي. وقد ظلّ عبر فترات طويلة مجرد بقايا بناء أو ركام، حتى أُعيد تشييده في عهد المملكة العربية السعودية عام 1422هـ/2002م، وأصبح مسجداً حديثاً بمساحة تقارب 2578م². وتكمن أهميته التاريخية في كونه من المساجد المأثورة التي صلى فيها النبي ﷺ، إذ ورد أنه صلى في المسجد الواقع عند أصل المنارتين على طريق العقيق الكبير. وقد ضاع تحديد موضعه في بعض العصور، مما أدى إلى إهماله زمناً طويلاً قبل إعادة بنائه وتحديد موقعه في عهد المملكة العربية السعودية||EN::"Masjid Bani Dinar Al-A'la is one of the historical mosques in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located in the dwellings of Banu Dinar in the Harrah. It is also known as Masjid Al-Manartayn (the Mosque of the Two Minarets) relative to two yellow mountains north of the Harrah. The mosque is situated on Umar ibn al-Khattab Road (formerly Al-Anbariyah), at a distance of about 2.8 km from the Prophet's Mosque. For long periods, it remained merely building remains or rubble, until it was rebuilt during the era of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia in 1422 AH / 2002 CE, becoming a modern mosque with an area of approximately 2,578 square meters. Its historical significance lies in its being one of the traditional mosques where the Prophet (PBUH) prayed, as it was reported that he prayed in the mosque located at the base of the two minarets on the road of the Great Al-Aqiq. The precise determination of its location was lost in some eras, which led to its neglect for a long time before its reconstruction and the determination of its location during the era of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia."||TR::"Beni Dinar el-A'la Mescidi, Medine-i Münevvere'deki tarihi mescitlerden biridir; Harre'deki Beni Dinar yurdunda yer alır ve Harre'nin kuzeyindeki iki sarı dağa nispetle 'İki Minare Mescidi' (Mescidü'l-Menarhteyn) olarak da bilinir. Mescit, Mescid-i Nebevi'ye yaklaşık 2.8 km mesafede, Ömer bin Hattab Yolu (eski adıyla Anbariye) üzerinde yer almaktadır. Uzun süreler boyunca sadece bir yapı kalıntısı veya enkaz halinde kalmış, nihayet Suudi Arabistan Krallığı döneminde 1422 Hicri / 2002 Miladi yılında yeniden inşa edilerek yaklaşık 2578 metrekarelik alana sahip modern bir mescit haline gelmiştir. Tarihi önemi, Hz. Peygamber'in (sav) namaz kıldığı me’sur (rivayet olunan) mescitlerden biri olmasından kaynaklanmaktadır; nitekim Büyük Akik yolu üzerindeki iki minarenin dibinde bulunan mescidde namaz kıldığı rivayet edilmiştir. Bazı dönemlerde yerinin tespiti kaybolmuş, bu da Suudi Arabistan Krallığı döneminde yeniden inşa edilip yeri tespit edilinceye kadar uzun süre ihmal edilmesine yol açmıştır."||ID::"Masjid Bani Dinar Al-A'la adalah salah satu masjid bersejarah di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, terletak di perkampungan Bani Dinar di kawasan Al-Harrah, dan dikenal juga sebagai Masjid Al-Manartayn (Masjid Dua Menara) menisbahkannya kepada dua gunung berwarna kuning di sebelah utara Al-Harrah. Masjid ini terletak di Jalan Umar bin Khattab (dahulu Al-Anbariyah), berjarak sekitar 2,8 km dari Masjid Nabawi. Selama kurun waktu yang panjang, masjid ini hanya berupa sisa-sisa bangunan atau reruntuhan, hingga akhirnya dibangun kembali pada masa Kerajaan Arab Saudi pada tahun 1422 H / 2002 M, dan menjadi masjid modern dengan luas sekitar 2.578 meter persegi. Signifikansi historisnya terletak pada posisinya sebagai salah satu masjid ma'tsurah (bersejarah) di mana Nabi (SAW) pernah shalat di dalamnya, karena diriwayatkan bahwa beliau shalat di masjid yang terletak di pangkal dua menara di jalan Al-Aqiq Al-Kabir. Penentuan lokasinya sempat hilang pada beberapa masa, yang menyebabkan masjid tersebut terabaikan untuk waktu yang lama sebelum akhirnya dibangun kembali dan ditentukan lokasinya pada masa Kerajaan Arab Saudi."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/gfpzKf2YzguJJ6j5A]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59354092233909,24.45527268191573,624.716727728233</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>موقع مسجد بني معاوية(الإجابة)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::هنا مكان مسجد بني معاوية من المساجد التاريخية في المدينة المنورة، ويقع شمال مقبرة البقيع. صلى فيه النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ودعا ربه فيه .تعرض المسجد للخراب عبر فترات من تاريخه، ثم حظي بعناية وترميم حتى أُعيد بناؤه وتوسعته في عهد خادم الحرمين الشريفين الملك فهد بن عبدالعزيز رحمه الله. ومع هذا الاهتمام بالمسجد النبوي احتيج إلى إزالته والاستفادة من مكانه بالطرق لخدمة المسجد النبوي||EN::Here is the site of the Mosque of Banu Muawiyah, one of the historical mosques in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located north of Al-Baqi' Cemetery. The Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) prayed in it and supplicated to his Lord therein. The mosque suffered ruin across periods of its history, then it received care and restoration until it was rebuilt and expanded during the era of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques, King Fahd bin Abdulaziz (may Allah have mercy on him). Despite this care for the Prophet's Mosque, it became necessary to remove it and utilize its location for roads to serve the Prophet's Mosque||TR::"Burası Medine-i Münevvere'deki tarihi mescitlerden biri olan ve Baki Mezarlığı'nın kuzeyinde yer alan Beni Muaviye Mescidi'nin yeridir. Peygamber Efendimiz (sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem) burada namaz kılmış ve Rabbine dua etmiştir. Mescit tarihin çeşitli dönemlerinde harabeye uğramış, ardından İki Haremeyn Hizmetkârı Kral Fahd bin Abdulaziz'in (Allah ona rahmet etsin) döneminde yeniden inşa edilip genişletilene kadar bakım ve restorasyon görmüştür. Mescid-i Nebevi'ye gösterilen bu alâkaya rağmen, Mescid-i Nebevi'ye hizmet etmek amacıyla kaldırılması ve yerinin yollar için değerlendirilmesi gerekmiştir.||ID::Di sinilah lokasi Masjid Bani Muawiyah, salah satu masjid bersejarah di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, yang terletak di sebelah utara Pemakaman Al-Baqi'. Nabi (semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya) pernah shalat di dalamnya dan memohon kepada Rabb-nya di sana. Masjid ini sempat mengalami kehancuran dalam beberapa periode sejarahnya, kemudian mendapat perhatian dan pemugaran hingga akhirnya dibangun kembali dan diperluas pada masa pelayan Dua Tanah Suci, Raja Fahd bin Abdulaziz (semoga Allah merahmatinya). Di samping perhatian yang besar terhadap Masjid Nabawi ini, masjid tersebut harus dibongkar dan lahannya dimanfaatkan untuk jalan demi melayani Masjid Nabawi."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/RHyzPS2hDBfRpRcU7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61846641916187,24.47212635690767,604.6384762551992</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غار السجدة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غار السجدة من المعالم التاريخية المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية، ويقع في جبل سلع بالقرب من شعب بني حرام، غربي المدينة المنورة. وقد عُرف أيضاً باسم "كهف بني حرام "وروي أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم سجد فيه شكرا لله ارتبط الكهف بعدد من الأحداث في العهد النبوي، أبرزها أنه كان موضعاً يلجأ إليه المسلمون مع النبي ﷺ خلال فترة غزوة الخندق للمبيت والتحصن.||EN::Ghar al-Sajdah is one of the historical landmarks associated with the Prophetic biography, located in Jabal Sila' near Shu'ab Banu Haram, west of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. It has also been known as 'The Cave of Banu Haram,' and it is narrated that the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) prostrated in it out of gratitude to Allah. The cave was associated with a number of events in the prophetic era, most notably that it was a place where Muslims resorted with the Prophet (PBUH) during the period of the Battle of the Trench for overnight stay and fortification||TR::Seccade Mağarası (Ğarü's-Secde), Medine-i Münevvere'nin batısında, Benî Haram Vadisi (Şu'ab Benî Haram) yakınındaki Sila Dağı'nda yer alan ve Hz. Peygamber'in hayatı (Siyer) ile ilgili tarihi simge yapıcılardan biridir. Aynı zamanda 'Benî Haram Mağarası' olarak da bilinir ve Peygamber Efendimiz'in (sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem) Allah'a şükretmek için burada secde ettiği rivayet edilmiştir. Mağara, nebat devrinde aralarında Hendek Savaşı sırasında Müslümanların Hz. Peygamber (sav) ile birlikte gecelemek ve sığınmak için başvurdukları bir yer olmasının da bulunduğu birçok olayla ilişkilendirilmiştir||ID::Ghar al-Sajdah adalah salah satu landmark historis yang berkaitan dengan sejarah kenabian, terletak di Jabal Sila' dekat Syu'ab Bani Haram, sebelah barat Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Tempat ini juga dikenal sebagai 'Gua Bani Haram', dan diriwayatkan bahwa Nabi (semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya) bersujud di dalamnya sebagai bentuk syukur kepada Allah. Gua tersebut dikaitkan dengan sejumlah peristiwa pada masa kenabian, yang paling utama adalah bahwa tempat itu menjadi lokasi perlindungan bagi umat Islam bersama Nabi (SAW) selama periode Perang Khandaq untuk bermalam dan berlindung||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/EcDyg6Wu4LyEeenS7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59869328134401,24.47420938506054,625.7712581390342</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد أول جمعة صلاها النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد الجمعة من المساجد التاريخية في المدينة المنورة. يرتبط المسجد بحدث تاريخي مهم في السيرة النبوية، فهو أول مسجد أقيمت صلاة جمعة للنبي ﷺ بعد هجرته إلى المدينة. وقد حظي المسجد بعناية متواصلة عبر العصور، فشهد أعمال بناء وترميم وتجديد من قبل عدد من الحكام والمحسنين. وفي العهد السعودي، أُعيد بناء المسجد وتوسعته، ضمن جهود المملكة في المحافظة على المساجد والمواقع التاريخية الإسلامية وتطويرها لخدمة الزوار والمصلين.||EN::Masjid Al-Jum'ah is one of the historical mosques in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. The mosque is associated with an important historical event in the prophetic biography; it is the first mosque where the Friday prayer was established for the Prophet (PBUH) after his migration to Madinah. The mosque has received continuous care across the ages, witnessing construction, restoration, and renewal works by a number of rulers and benefactors. In the Saudi era, the mosque was rebuilt and expanded as part of the Kingdom's efforts to preserve historical Islamic mosques and sites and develop them to serve visitors and worshippers||TR::Cuma Mescidi, Medine-i Münevvere'deki tarihi mescitlerden biridir. Mescit, Hz. Peygamber'in hayatındaki önemli tarihi bir olayla ilişkilendirilmektedir; Medine'ye hicretinden sonra Hz. Peygamber (sav) için Cuma namazının kılındığı ilk mescittir. Mescit, çağlar boyunca sürekli bir özen görmüş, birçok hükümdar ve hayırsever tarafından inşa, restorasyon ve yenileme çalışmalarına şahit olmuştur. Suudi Arabistan döneminde ise mescit, Krallık'ın tarihi İslam mescitlerini ve mekanlarını koruma ve bunları ziyaretçiler ile ibadet edenlere hizmet edecek şekilde geliştirme çabalarının bir parçası olarak yeniden inşa edilmiş ve genişletilmiştir||ID::Masjid Al-Jum'ah adalah salah satu masjid bersejarah di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Masjid ini berkaitan dengan peristiwa bersejarah penting dalam sirah nabawiyah, karena merupakan masjid pertama di mana shalat Jumat didirikan untuk Nabi (SAW) setelah hijrah beliau ke Madinah. Masjid ini telah mendapatkan perhatian yang berkelanjutan dari masa ke masa, serta menyaksikan berbagai pekerjaan pembangunan, pemugaran, dan pembaruan oleh sejumlah penguasa dan para dermawan. Pada era Saudi, masjid ini dibangun kembali dan diperluas sebagai bagian dari upaya Kerajaan dalam melestarikan masjid-masjid serta situs-situs sejarah Islam dan mengembangkannya untuk melayani para pengunjung dan jamaah||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/EdcxLA9MnKkBNYjY8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61531215527846,24.44546097395796,605.1024545198111</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد المستراح</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد المستراح من المساجد التاريخية في المدينة المنورة، . وسمي بمسجد بني حارثة لوقوعه في ديارهم، ووذكرت بعض الروايات أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم استراح في هذا الموضع أثناء توجهه إلى أحد وصلى فيه. وحظي المسجد بعناية كبيرة في العهد السعودي؛ إذ أُعيد بناؤه وتطويره أكثر من مرة، ويُعد المسجد اليوم من المعالم التاريخية البارزة التي تعكس اهتمام المملكة العربية السعودية بالحفاظ على المواقع المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية وإبراز قيمتها التاريخية والدينية.||EN::Masjid Al-Mustarah is one of the historical mosques in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. It was named the Mosque of Banu Harithah because it is located in their dwellings, and some narrations mention that the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) rested at this site while heading towards Uhud and prayed in it. The mosque has received great care in the Saudi era; it has been rebuilt and developed more than once. Today, the mosque is considered one of the prominent historical landmarks that reflect the interest of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia in preserving sites associated with the Prophetic biography and highlighting their historical and religious value||TR::Mescidü'l-Müsterâh, Medine-i Münevvere'deki tarihi mescitlerden biridir. Yurtlarında yer alması sebebiyle Beni Harise Mescidi olarak da adlandırılmış olup, bazı rivayetlerde Hz. Peygamber'in (sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem) Uhud'a giderken bu mevkide dinlendiği ve burada namaz kıldığı zikredilmiştir. Mescit, Suudi Arabistan döneminde büyük bir özen görmüş; birden fazla kez yeniden inşa edilmiş ve geliştirilmiştir. Bugün mescit, Suudi Arabistan Krallığı'nın Hz. Peygamber'in hayatı (Siyer) ile ilgili mekanları korumaya ve bunların tarihi ve dini değerini öne çıkarmaya verdiği önemi yansıtan en belirgin tarihi simge yapılardan biri olarak kabul edilmektedir||ID::Masjid Al-Mustarah adalah salah satu masjid bersejarah di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Masjid ini dinamakan Masjid Bani Harithah karena terletak di perkampungan mereka, dan beberapa riwayat menyebutkan bahwa Nabi (semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya) beristirahat di tempat ini saat menuju Uhud dan shalat di dalamnya. Masjid ini telah mendapatkan perhatian besar pada era Saudi; masjid ini telah dibangun kembali dan dikembangkan lebih dari sekali. Hari ini, masjid tersebut dianggap sebagai salah satu landmark historis terkemuka yang mencerminkan perhatian Kerajaan Arab Saudi dalam melestarikan situs-situs yang berkaitan dengan sirah nabawiyah serta menonjolkan nilai historis dan religiusnya.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/4EoLZXEGVAuTY6KM6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60976279883687,24.49177762070291,602.7479144115796</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل أحد</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::جبل أُحد من أشهر المعالم التاريخية والطبيعية في المدينة المنورة، ويقع شمال المدينة على بُعد نحو خمسة كيلومترات من المسجد النبوي. ويُعد من أبرز جبال المنطقة، إذ يمتد لمسافة تقارب سبعة كيلومترات ويتميز بتكوينه الصخري وألوانه المتنوعة. ارتبط الجبل ارتباطاً وثيقاً بالسيرة النبوية، فقد وقعت عنده غزوة أحد، وهي من أهم أحداث التاريخ الإسلامي.||EN::Mount Uhud is one of the most famous historical and natural landmarks in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located north of the city at a distance of about five kilometers from the Prophet's Mosque. It is considered one of the most prominent mountains in the region, extending for a distance of nearly seven kilometers and characterized by its rocky formation and diverse colors. The mountain is closely associated with the prophetic biography, as the Battle of Uhud took place near it, which is one of the most important events in Islamic history||TR::Uhud Dağı, Medine-i Münevvere'nin en meşhur tarihi ve tabii simge yapılarından biridir; şehrin kuzeyinde, Mescid-i Nebevi'ye yaklaşık beş kilometre mesafede yer alır. Yaklaşık yedi kilometre boyunca uzanan, kaya oluşumu ve çeşitli renkleriyle öne çıkan bölgenin en belirgin dağlarından biri olarak kabul edilir. Dağ, Hz. Peygamber'in hayatı (Siyer) ile sıkı bir şekilde ilişkilidir; nitekim İslam tarihinin en önemli olaylarından biri olan Uhud Gazvesi bu dağın yanında gerçekleşmiştir.||ID::Gunung Uhud adalah salah satu landmark historis dan alam paling terkenal di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, terletak di sebelah utara kota pada jarak sekitar lima kilometer dari Masjid Nabawi. Gunung ini dianggap sebagai salah satu gunung paling menonjol di wilayah tersebut, membentang sejauh hampir tujuh kilometer serta dicirikan oleh formasi batuan dan warna-warnanya yang beragam. Gunung ini sangat erat kaitannya dengan sirah nabawiyah, karena di dekatnya terjadi Perang Uhud, yang merupakan salah satu peristiwa paling penting dalam sejarah Islam||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/fpV1f5B7CqGdxhh38]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61831365681969,24.51051286169534,997.889722555941</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل الرماة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::جبل الرماة، ويُعرف أيضاً باسم جبل عينين، هو تلّ صغير يقع جنوب غربي جبل أحد في المدينة المنورة. اكتسب الجبل شهرته من أحداث غزوة أحد، عندما وضع النبي ﷺ عليه خمسين من الرماة بقيادة عبد الله بن جبير الأنصاري لحماية ظهور المسلمين ومنع التفاف المشركين حول الجيش. وقد أوصاهم بعدم مغادرة مواقعهم. في بداية المعركة حقق المسلمون تقدماً واضحاً، لكن معظم الرماة نزلوا من الجبل ظناً أن القتال انتهى، فاستغل خالد بن الوليد هذا الفراغ وقاد هجوماً التفّ به على المسلمين، مما أدى إلى تغير مجريات المعركة واستشهاد عدد من الصحابة، واليوم تبذل المملكة العربية السعودية جهودا عظيمة في تأهيل الموقع والمحافظة على الأماكن التراثية||EN::Jabal al-Rumah, also known as Jabal Aynayn, is a small hill located southwest of Mount Uhud in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. The mountain gained its fame from the events of the Battle of Uhud, when the Prophet ﷺ stationed fifty archers on it under the command of Abdullah bin Jubayr al-Ansari to protect the rear of the Muslims and prevent the polytheists from encircling the army. He instructed them not to leave their positions. At the beginning of the battle, the Muslims achieved clear progress, but most of the archers descended from the mountain thinking that the fighting had ended. Khalid bin al-Walid took advantage of this void and led an attack, encircling the Muslims, which led to a change in the course of the battle and the martyrdom of a number of Companions. Today, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia is making great efforts to rehabilitate the site and preserve heritage places.||TR::Ayneyn Dağı olarak da bilinen Rumat Dağı, Medine-i Münevvere'de Uhud Dağı'nın güneybatısında yer alan küçük bir tepedir. Bu dağ, Peygamber ﷺ'in Müslümanların arkasını korumak ve müşriklerin ordunun etrafını sarısını önlemek amacıyla Abdullah bin Cübeyr el-Ensari komutasında üzerine elli okçu yerleştirdiği Uhud Gazvesi olaylarıyla ün kazanmıştır. Onlara yerlerinden ayrılmamalarını emretmiştir. Savaşın başında Müslümanlar açık bir ilerleme kaydetmiş, ancak okçuların çoğu savaşın bittiğini zannederek dağdan inmiştir. Halid bin Velid bu boşluğu fırsat bilerek bir saldırı düzenlemiş ve Müslümanları kuşatmış, bu da savaşın seyrinin değişmesine ve birçok sahabinin şehit olmasına yol açmıştır. Bugün Suudi Arabistan Krallığı, alanı yeniden imar etmek ve kültürel miras alanlarını korumak için büyük çaba sarf etmektedir.||ID::"Jabal al-Rumah, yang juga dikenal sebagai Jabal Aynayn, adalah sebuah bukit kecil yang terletak di sebelah barat daya Gunung Uhud di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Gunung ini mendapatkan ketenarannya dari peristiwa Perang Uhud, ketika Nabi ﷺ menempatkan lima puluh pemanah di atasnya di bawah komando Abdullah bin Jubair al-Anshari untuk melindungi barisan belakang kaum Muslimin dan mencegah kaum musyrik mengepung pasukan. Beliau berpesan kepada mereka agar tidak meninggalkan posisi mereka. Pada awal pertempuran, kaum Muslimin meraih kemajuan yang nyata, tetapi sebagian besar pemanah turun dari gunung karena mengira pertempuran telah usai. Khalid bin al-Walid memanfaatkan kekosongan ini dan memimpin serangan yang melingkari kaum Muslimin, yang menyebabkan berubahnya jalannya pertempuran dan syahidnya sejumlah Sahabat. Hari ini, Kerajaan Arab Saudi mencurahkan upaya besar dalam merehabilitasi situs tersebut dan melestarikan tempat-tempat bersejarah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/zeBohPKCdTpGAnJN6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61204759929961,24.50237612243602,602.3562575155311</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>قصر عروة بن الزبير</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::قصر عروة بن الزبير من أشهر القصور التاريخية في المدينة المنورة، وينسب إلى عروة بن الزبير أحد فقهاء المدينة السبعة. يقع على ضفاف وادي العقيق غرب المدينة، في موقع متميز على الطريق التاريخي المؤدي إلى مكة المكرمة. كان القصر بناءً كبيراً شُيّد بالحجارة البركانية، وتضمّن أفنية وغرفاً متعددة، وكشفت الدراسات الأثرية عن بقايا مسجد مجاور له وقطع أثرية تعود إلى العصرين الأموي والعباسي، مما يؤكد أهميته التاريخية والعمرانية. تولت الحكومة السعودية الاهتمام به والاعتناء بترميمه.||EN::The Palace of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr is one of the most famous historical palaces in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, and is attributed to Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, one of the seven jurists of Madinah. It is located on the banks of Wadi Al-Aqiq, west of the city, in a prime location on the historical road leading to Makkah Al-Mukarramah. The palace was a large structure built of volcanic stones, and included multiple courtyards and rooms. Archaeological studies have revealed the remains of a nearby mosque and artifacts dating back to the Umayyad and Abbasid eras, which confirms its historical and architectural importance. The Saudi government has taken care of it and attended to its restoration.||TR::Urve bin Zübeyr Sarayı, Medine-i Münevvere'deki en meşhur tarihi saraylardan biridir ve Medine'nin yedi fıkhından biri olan Urve bin Zübeyr'e nisbet edilmektedir. Şehrin batısında, Akik Vadisi'nin kıyısında, Mekke-i Mükerreme'ye giden tarihi yol üzerinde seçkin bir konumda yer almaktadır. Saray, volkanik taşlarla inşa edilmiş büyük bir yapı olup, avluları ve çok sayıda odayı içermekteydi. Arkeolojik çalışmalar, yanında bulunan bir mescidin kalıntılarını ve Emevi ile Abbasi dönemlerine ait eserleri ortaya çıkarmış olup, bu durum onun tarihi ve mimari önemini teyit etmektedir. Suudi hükümeti onunla ilgilenmiş ve restorasyonunu üstlenmiştir||ID::stana Urwah bin al-Zubayr adalah salah satu istana bersejarah paling terkenal di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan dinisbahkan kepada Urwah bin al-Zubayr, salah satu dari tujuh ahli fikih Madinah. Istana ini terletak di tepi Wadi Al-Aqiq, sebelah barat kota, di lokasi yang istimewa di jalur bersejarah yang menuju ke Makkah Al-Mukarramah. Istana tersebut merupakan bangunan besar yang dibangun dari batu-batu vulkanik, serta mencakup halaman-halaman dan berbagai ruangan. Studi arkeologi telah mengungkap sisa-sisa masjid di dekatnya dan artefak yang berasal dari masa Bani Umayyah dan Abbasiyah, yang menegaskan pentingnya nilai sejarah dan arsitekturnya. Pemerintah Saudi telah memberikan perhatian padanya dan merawat pemugarannya||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/M2TpEjpFWn5i6CRw5]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.58159307748847,24.45039289044879,621.0811889466859</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد سجدة الشكر</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::هنا موضع مسجد سجدة الشكر،ارتبط المسجد بحدث من السيرة النبوية، إذ يذكر المؤرخون أنه أقيم في الموضع الذي سجد فيه النبي ﷺ سجدة شكر بعد أن بشّره جبريل عليه السلام بفضل الصلاة والسلام عليه ﷺ، واليوم دخل ضمن مشاريع تطوير المسجد النبوي والمناطق المحيطة به||EN::Here is the site of the Mosque of the Prostration of Gratitude. The mosque is associated with an event from the prophetic biography, as historians mention that it was established at the place where the Prophet ﷺ performed a prostration of gratitude after Gabriel (peace be upon him) brought him the good news of the virtue of invoking prayers and peace upon him ﷺ. Today, it has been included within the development projects of the Prophet's Mosque and its surrounding areas.||TR::Burası Şükür Secdesi Mescidi'nin yeridir. Mescid, Hz. Peygamber'in hayatı (Siyer) ile ilgili bir olayla ilişkilendirilmektedir; nitekim tarihçiler, Cebrail (aleyhisselam) kendisine Hz. Peygamber ﷺ üzerine salat ve selam getirmenin faziletini müjdeledikten sonra, Peygamber ﷺ'in şükür secdesi yaptığı yerde inşa edildiğini zikretmektedirler. Bugün ise Mescid-i Nebevi ve çevre alanlarını geliştirme projelerine dâhil edilmiştir.||ID::Di sinilah lokasi Masjid Sujud Syukur. Masjid ini berkaitan dengan sebuah peristiwa dari sirah nabawiyah, sebagaimana para sejarawan menyebutkan bahwa masjid tersebut didirikan di tempat di mana Nabi ﷺ melakukan sujud syukur setelah Jibril (alaihis salam) menyampaikan kabar gembira kepadanya tentang keutamaan bershalawat dan salam atas beliau ﷺ. Hari ini, tempat tersebut telah dimasukkan ke dalam proyek-proyek pengembangan Masjid Nabawi dan daerah sekitarnya||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/doR2c7rZBecAWWU1A]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61452140388909,24.47568068200652,601.8452347888165</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بقيع الغرقد</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بقيع الغرقد هو المقبرة التاريخية الرئيسة في المدينة المنورة، وتقع إلى الجنوب الشرقي من المسجد النبوي. سُمّيت بهذا الاسم نسبة إلى شجر الغرقد الذي كان ينبت في الموقع قبل أن يُتخذ مقبرة لأهل المدينة.يُعد البقيع من أهم المواقع الإسلامية؛ إذ دُفن فيه عدد كبير من الصحابة وأهل بيت النبي ﷺ والتابعين، مما أكسبه مكانة دينية وتاريخية كبيرة لدى المسلمين. شهد البقيع تطورات عمرانية متعددة في العهد السعودي من توسعات وترميمات وتسوير للمقبرة، وتمت توسعة المقبرة وتنظيمها وتطوير مرافقها، وإنشاء الأسوار والبوابات والممرات والخدمات المرتبطة بالدفن وتجهيز الجنائز.||EN::Baqi' al-Gharqad is the main historical cemetery in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located to the southeast of the Prophet's Mosque. It was named after the gharqad trees that used to grow at the site before it was adopted as a graveyard for the people of Madinah. Al-Baqi' is considered one of the most important Islamic sites, as a large number of Companions, members of the Prophet's household ﷺ, and the Followers (Tabi'un) are buried in it, which has earned it a great religious and historical status among Muslims. Al-Baqi' has witnessed multiple urban developments during the Saudi era, including expansions, restorations, and fencing of the cemetery. The cemetery has been expanded, organized, and its facilities developed, along with the establishment of walls, gates, pathways, and services related to burial and the preparation of funerals||TR::Baki'u'l-Garkad, Medine-i Münevvere'deki ana tarihi mezarlıktır ve Mescid-i Nebevi'nin güneydoğusunda yer alır. Yerli halk için mezarlık olarak kullanılmadan önce bu mekanda yetişen garkad ağaçlarına nispetle bu ismi almıştır. Baki', çok sayıda sahabinin, Hz. Peygamber'in ehl-i beytinin ﷺ ve tabiinin defnedilmesi nedeniyle en önemli İslam mekanlarından biri olarak kabul edilmekte olup, bu durum ona Müslümanlar nezdinde büyük bir dini ve tarihi statü kazandırmıştır. Baki', Suudi Arabistan döneminde genişletmeler, restorasyonlar ve mezarlığın duvarla çevrilmesi gibi bir dizi kentsel gelişmeye şahit olmuştur; mezarlık genişletilmiş, düzenlenmiş, tesisleri geliştirilmiş, duvarlar, kapılar, yollar ile defin ve cenaze hazırlıklarıyla ilgili hizmetler kurulmuştur.||ID::Baqi' al-Gharqad adalah pemakaman bersejarah utama di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, terletak di sebelah tenggara Masjid Nabawi. Tempat ini dinamakan demikian dinisbahkan kepada pohon gharqad yang biasa tumbuh di lokasi tersebut sebelum dijadikan sebagai pemakaman bagi penduduk Madinah. Al-Baqi' dianggap sebagai salah satu situs Islam terpenting, karena sejumlah besar Sahabat, Ahlulbait Nabi ﷺ, dan para Tabi'in dimakamkan di dalamnya, yang memberikannya kedudukan religius dan historis yang besar di kalangan umat Islam. Al-Baqi' telah menyaksikan berbagai perkembangan pembangunan pada era Saudi, termasuk perluasan, pemugaran, dan pemagaran pemakaman. Pemakaman tersebut telah diperluas, diatur, dan fasilitasnya dikembangkan, serta dibangunnya tembok-tembok, gerbang-gerbang, jalur pejalan kaki, dan layanan yang berkaitan dengan pemakaman serta penyiapan jenazah||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/RjH1P723ktHXtFaR9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61364011908702,24.4671564065386,607.4148432140648</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الفتح</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد الفتح، ويُعرف أيضاً بمسجد الأحزاب أو المسجد الأعلى، من أبرز المساجد التاريخية في المدينة المنورة، ويقع على مرتفع من جبل سلع ضمن منطقة المساجد السبعة، على بُعد نحو ثلاثة كيلومترات من المسجد النبوي. ترتبط أهمية المسجد بأحداث غزوة الخندق، إذ يُنسب إلى الموضع الذي عسكر فيه النبي ﷺ وبعض أصحابه أثناء الغزوة، ولذلك اكتسب مكانة تاريخية بارزة في السيرة النبوية. شهد المسجد عدة مراحل من البناء والتجديد عبر العصور، بدءاً من عمارته في عهد عمر بن عبد العزيز عندما كان والياً على المدينة، ثم تجديده في العصور اللاحقة. وفي العهد السعودي حظي بعناية كبيرة من خلال أعمال الترميم والصيانة والمحافظة على طابعه التاريخي، ولا يزال قائماً حتى اليوم ضمن معالم المدينة المنورة المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية.||EN::"Masjid al-Fath, also known as the Mosque of the Parties or the Upper Mosque, is one of the most prominent historical mosques in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. It is located on an elevation of Jabal Sila' within the area of the Seven Mosques, at a distance of about three kilometers from the Prophet's Mosque. The importance of the mosque is linked to the events of the Battle of the Trench, as it is attributed to the site where the Prophet ﷺ and some of his Companions camped during the battle, and therefore it has acquired a prominent historical status in the prophetic biography. The mosque has witnessed several stages of construction and renewal across the ages, starting with its architecture during the era of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz when he was the governor of Madinah, and then its renovation in subsequent eras. In the Saudi era, it has received great care through restoration and maintenance works and the preservation of its historical character, and it still stands today among the landmarks of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah associated with the prophetic biography."||TR::Ahzab Mescidi veya Yukarı Mescit olarak da bilinen Fetih Mescidi, Medine-i Münevvere'deki en belirgin tarihi mescitlerden biridir ve Mescid-i Nebevi'ye yaklaşık üç kilometre mesafede, Yedi Mescitler bölgesinde Sila Dağı'nın yüksek bir noktasında yer almaktadır. Mescidin önemi Hendek Savaşı olaylarıyla bağlantılıdır; çünkü savaş sırasında Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ve bazı sahabelerinin karargâh kurduğu yere nispet edilmektedir ve bu nedenle Peygamber'in hayatında (Siyer) öne çıkan tarihi bir statü kazanmıştır. Mescit, Medine valisi olduğu dönemde Ömer bin Abdulaziz'in devrindeki inşasıyla başlayıp sonraki dönemlerde yenilenmesiyle birlikte çağlar boyunca birçok inşa ve yenileme aşamasına şahit olmuştur. Suudi Arabistan döneminde ise restorasyon, bakım çalışmaları ve tarihi karakterinin korunması yoluyla büyük bir özen görmüş olup, Medine-i Münevvere'nin Siyer ile ilgili simge yapıları arasında bugün hâlâ ayaktadır||ID::Masjid al-Fath, yang juga dikenal sebagai Masjid al-Ahzab atau Masjid Atas, adalah salah satu masjid bersejarah paling terkemuka di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan terletak di dataran tinggi Jabal Sila' di dalam kawasan Tujuh Masjid, pada jarak sekitar tiga kilometer dari Masjid Nabawi. Pentingnya masjid ini berkaitan dengan peristiwa Perang Khandaq, karena dinisbahkan ke tempat di mana Nabi ﷺ dan beberapa sahabatnya berkemah selama perang tersebut, sehingga masjid ini memperoleh kedudukan historis yang menonjol dalam sirah nabawiyah. Masjid ini telah menyaksikan beberapa tahap pembangunan dan pembaruan dari masa ke masa, dimulai dari pembangunannya pada masa Umar bin Abdul Aziz ketika beliau menjabat sebagai gubernur Madinah, kemudian pembaruannya pada era-era setelahnya. Pada era Saudi, masjid ini mendapatkan perhatian besar melalui pekerjaan restorasi, pemeliharaan, dan pelestarian karakter historisnya, dan masjid ini masih berdiri hingga hari ini di antara landmark Madinah Al-Munawwarah yang berkaitan dengan sirah nabawiyah||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/ThjmZ9TiEq4vE1p4A]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59560865414519,24.47782169469945,605.2909198700449</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مشربة أم إبراهيم</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::كانت مشربة أم إبراهيم من الصدقات النبوية المعروفة في المدينة المنورة،وأسهم التوسع العمراني في تغير اختفاء كثير من ملامحه التاريخية، وأصبحت معرفتها تعتمد بشكل رئيس على ما حفظته المصادر التاريخية والدراسات المتخصصة في تاريخ المدينة المنورة.||EN::Mashrabat Umm Ibrahim was one of the well-known prophetic charities in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Urban expansion contributed to the change and disappearance of many of its historical features, and knowing it has come to depend primarily on what historical sources and specialized studies on the history of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah have preserved||TR::Meşrebetü Ümmi İbrahim, Medine-i Münevvere'deki bilinen nebevi sadakalardan biriydi. Kentsel genişleme, onun tarihi özelliklerinin birçoğunun değişmesine ve ortadan kalkmasına katkıda bulunmuş olup, burası hakkındaki bilgi edinme süreci artık esas olarak tarihi kaynakların ve Medine-i Münevvere tarihi üzerine yapılan uzmanlaşmış çalışmaların muhafaza ettiği bilgilere dayanmaktadır||ID::Mashrabat Umm Ibrahim adalah salah satu sedekah kenabian yang terkenal di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Perluasan perkotaan telah berkontribusi pada perubahan dan hilangnya banyak fitur historisnya, sehingga pengetahuannya kini bergantung terutama pada apa yang telah dilestarikan oleh sumber-sumber sejarah dan studi-studi khusus tentang sejarah Madinah Al-Munawwarah||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/opJsSHMVT2pYjFdk8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.6325064122212,24.45143381285083,606.656469629378</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر سلمان الفارسي رضي الله عنه</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بئر سلمان الفارسي وتسمى بئرالفقير، كان يعمل فيها الصحابي الجليل سلمان الفارسي -رضي الله عنه-، وقد غرس النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم نخلًا بجوارها مقابل أن يُعتق سلمان، ومنذ مطلع العهد السعودي الزاهر تم ترميمها وتأهيل موقعها في عهد خادم الحرمين الشريفين الملك سلمان بن عبدالعزيز آل سعود||EN::The Well of Salman al-Farsi, also known as the Well of the Poor, was where the noble Companion Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) used to work. The Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) planted palm trees next to it in exchange for Salman's emancipation. Since the dawn of the prosperous Saudi era, it has been restored and its site rehabilitated during the era of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques, King Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud||TR::Fakir Kuyusu da denilen Selman-ı Farisi Kuyusu, yüce sahabe Selman-ı Farisi'nin (radıyallahu anh) çalıştığı yerdi. Peygamber Efendimiz (sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem), Selman'ın azat edilmesi karşılığında bunun yanına hurma ağaçları dikmişti. Parlak Suudi döneminin başlangıcından bu yana, İki Haremeyn Hizmetkârı Kral Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud döneminde restore edilmiş ve alanı yeniden imar edilmiştir||ID::Sumur Salman al-Farsi, yang juga disebut Sumur Al-Faqir, adalah tempat di mana Sahabat mulia Salman al-Farsi (semoga Allah meridhainya) biasa bekerja. Nabi (semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya) menanam pohon kurma di sampingnya sebagai imbalan agar Salman dimerdekakan. Sejak fajar era Saudi yang makmur, sumur tersebut telah dipugar dan situsnya direhabilitasi pada masa Pelayan Dua Tanah Suci, Raja Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/oMiHzEzCmnLhx92S6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.63262261470522,24.44465910010217,607.8015955906045</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر الأعواف</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بئر الأعواف من الآبار التي ثبت أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم توضأ منها، ولقد حرصت حكومة خادم الحرمين الشريفين بالمحافظة عليها||EN::The Well of Al-A'waf is one of the wells proven that the Prophet, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him, performed ablution from it, and the government of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques has been keen to preserve it.||TR::E'vaf Kuyusu, Hz. Peygamber -sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem-'in ondan abdest aldığı sabit olan kuyulardandır ve İki Haremeyn Hizmetkârı hükümeti bunu korumaya özen göstermiştir.||ID::Sumur Al-A'waf adalah salah satu sumur yang terbukti bahwa Nabi -semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya- berwudhu darinya, dan pemerintah Pelayan Dua Tanah Suci sangat antusias untuk melestarikannya.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/4DZ7erJwJT8GLq7dA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.63137549547611,24.44517492969911,607.7941266304306</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مزارع برقة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::صدقة برقة من الصدقات النبوية.، ولقد حرصت المملكة العربية السعودية على الاهتمام بها والمحافظة على الآثار النبوية||EN::Sadaqat Burqa is one of the prophetic charities, and the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has been keen to take care of it and preserve the prophetic antiquities||TR::Burka Sadakası nebevi sadakalardan biridir ve Suudi Arabistan Krallığı bununla ilgilenmeye ve nebevi eserleri korumaya özen göstermiştir||ID::Sedekah Burqa adalah salah satu sedekah kenabian, dan Kerajaan Arab Saudi sangat antusias untuk memerhatikannya serta melestarikan peninggalan-peninggalan kenabian||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/KFDkSKS7nFccEEHB8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.6361389,24.4488889,609.0570618960077</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>سوق المناخة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::يرجع تاريخ المناخة إلى العصر النبوي، عندما سعى الرسول ﷺ إلى تخصيص سوق للمسلمين في المدينة المنورة.فزار أولاً سوق بني قينقاع، ثم توجه إلى موضع سوق المدينة، فضرب الأرض برجله الشريفة وقال: «هذا سوقكم لا يُضيَّق، ولا يُؤخذ فيه خراج». ولقد طورت المملكة العربية السعودية السوق مع المحافظة على المظهر الحضاري للمسجد النبوي||EN::The history of Al-Manakhah dates back to the prophetic era, when the Messenger ﷺ sought to designate a market for Muslims in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. He first visited the market of Banu Qaynuqa, then headed to the site of the market of Madinah, struck the ground with his noble foot, and said: 'This is your market; it shall not be restricted, and no tax shall be levied on it.' The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has developed the market while preserving the civilizational appearance of the Prophet's Mosque||TR::Menâha'nın tarihi, Resul ﷺ'in Medine-i Münevvere'de Müslümanlar için bir pazar tahsis etmeye çalıştığı nebevi döneme dayanmaktadır. Önce Beni Kaynuka pazarı'nı ziyaret etmiş, ardından Medine pazarı'nın olduğu yere yönelmiş, mübarek ayağıyla yere vurarak şöyle buyurmuştur: 'Burası sizin pazarınızdır; daraltılmaz ve ondan haraç alınmaz.' Suudi Arabistan Krallığı, Mescid-i Nebevi'nin medeni görünümünü koruyarak pazarı geliştirmiştir.||ID::Sejarah Al-Manakhah kembali ke masa kenabian, ketika Rasulullah ﷺ berusaha untuk mengkhususkan sebuah pasar bagi umat Islam di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Beliau pertama kali mengunjungi pasar Bani Qainuqa, kemudian pergi ke lokasi pasar Madinah, lalu menjejakkan kakinya yang mulia ke tanah seraya bersabda: 'Ini adalah pasar kalian; tidak boleh disemppitkan, dan tidak pula diambil darinya pajak.' Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah mengembangkan pasar tersebut dengan tetap menjaga penampilan peradaban Masjid Nabawi.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/JyFhcP2BVnUEHjpb7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60473925405999,24.47090656161504,607.4882593549748</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حرة بني بياضة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::سُمِّيت هذه المنطقة بهذا الاسم نسبةً إلى بني بياضة، وهم بطنٌ من الأنصار ينتسبون إلى بياضة بن عامر بن زريق بن عبد حارثة من الخزرج.||EN::This region was named after Banu Bayadah, who are a clan of the Ansar belonging to Bayadah bin Amir bin Zurayq bin Abd Harithah from the Khazraj.||TR::Bu bölge, Hazrec'ten Beyada bin Amir bin Zureyk bin Abd Harise'ye mensup Ensâr'ın bir kolu olan Beni Beyada'ya nispetle bu ismi almıştır.||ID::Wilayah ini dinamakan demikian dinisbahkan kepada Bani Bayadah, yang merupakan sebuah klan dari kaum Ansar yang nasabnya kembali kepada Bayadah bin Amir bin Zurayq bin Abd Harithah dari suku Khazraj||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/PB6NR3jpsA7MwUdc9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60732053110904,24.44214038151123,617.0928893521741</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حرة شوران</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::تقع حرة شَوْران في الجهة الجنوبية للمدينة المنورة وتبعد سبع كيلو عن المسجد النبوي، وهي من الحرار الكبيرة ومساحتها كبيرة وتتميز بالتنوع الجغرافي قبل التوسع العمراني في حكومة خادم الحرمين الشريفين||EN::The Trench Site marks part of the defensive line dug by the Muslims during the Battle of the Trench to protect Madinah from invading forces.||TR::Hendek Bölgesi, Müslümanların Hendek Gazvesi sırasında Medine'yi savunmak için kazdığı savunma hattının bir bölümünü temsil eder.||ID::Lokasi Parit Khandaq menandai bagian dari garis pertahanan yang digali kaum Muslimin untuk melindungi Madinah dalam Perang Khandaq.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/fzjDJJXbT2p7mZs38]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60570548178366,24.41259697423202,642.9355487002114</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مقبرة شهداء الخندق</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::شهداء الخندق الذي استشهدوا في غزوة الخندق وهم أنَسْ بن أَوْس، وعَبدالله بن سَهل، والطُفَيل بن النعْمَان، وثَعلَبة بن غنمَة، وكَعْب بن زَيد رضي الله عنهم. وقد اعتنت حكومة المملكة العربية السعودية بالاهتمام بالمقبرة وتسويرها.||EN::The martyrs of the Trench, who were martyred in the Battle of the Trench, are Anas bin Aws, Abdullah bin Sahl, Al-Tufail bin Al-Nu'man, Tha'labah bin Ghanamah, and Ka'b bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them). The government of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has taken care of attending to the cemetery and fencing it||TR::Hendek Gazvesi'nde şehit olan Hendek şehitleri; Enes bin Evs, Abdullah bin Sehl, Tufeyl bin Nu'man, Sa'lebe bin Ganeme ve Ka'b bin Zeyd'dir (radıyallahu anhum). Suudi Arabistan Krallığı hükümeti, mezarlıkla ilgilenmeye ve onu duvarla çevirmeye özen göstermiştir||ID::Para syuhada Khandaq yang syahid dalam Perang Khandaq adalah Anas bin Aws, Abdullah bin Sahl, Al-Tufail bin Al-Nu'man, Tha'labah bin Ghanamah, dan Ka'b bin Zaid (semoga Allah meridhai mereka). Pemerintah Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah memberikan perhatian untuk merawat pemakaman tersebut dan memagarnya||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/V2iUHiAjHoVK2WTL6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.5953682678704,24.47767462758026,600.3838328196113</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مقبرة شهداء بدر</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غزوة بدر الكبرى في السنة الثانية من الهجرة واستشهد فيها عدد من الصحابة وهم من المهاجرين هم: عبيدة بن الحارث المطلبي القرشي. عمير بن أبي وقاص الزهري القرشي. صفوان بن وهب الفهري القرشي. عاقل بن البكير الليثي الكناني. ذو الشمالين بن عبد عمرو الخزاعي. مهجع بن صالح العكي. وثمانية من الأنصار هم: سعد بن خيثمة الأوسي. مبشر بن عبد المنذر العمري الأوسي. يزيد بن الحارث الخزرجي. عمير بن الحمام السَلَمي الخزرجي. رافع بن المعلى الزرقي الخزرجي. حارث بن سراقة النجاري الخزرجي. معوذ بن الحارث النجاري الخزرجي. عوف بن الحارث النجاري الخزرجي. وقد اعتنت حكومة المملكة العربية السعودية بالمقبرة وتسويرها.||EN::The Greater Battle of Badr took place in the second year of Hijrah, and a number of Companions were martyred in it. They include the following from the Muhajirun: Ubaydah bin al-Harith al-Mutallibi al-Qurashi, Umair bin Abi Waqqas al-Zuhri al-Qurashi, Safwan bin Wahb al-Fihri al-Qurashi, Aqil bin al-Bukayr al-Laithi al-Kinani, Dhu al-Shamalayn bin Abd Amr al-Khuza'i, and Mahja' bin Salih al-Aki. And eight from the Ansar: Sa'd bin Khaythamah al-Awsi, Mubashir bin Abd al-Mundhir al-Omari al-Awsi, Yazid bin al-Harith al-Khazraji, Umair bin al-Humam al-Sulami al-Khazraji, Rafi' bin al-Mu'alla al-Zurqi al-Khazraji, Harith bin Suraqah al-Najari al-Khazraji, Mu'awdh bin al-Harith al-Najari al-Khazraji, and Awf bin al-Harith al-Najari al-Khazraji. The government of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has taken care of the cemetery and fenced it||TR::Büyük Bedretül Kübra Gazvesi hicretin ikinci yılında gerçekleşmiş olup, onda muhacirlerden şu sahabeler şehit olmuştur: Ubeyde bin el-Haris el-Muttalibi el-Kureyşi, Umeyr bin Ebi Vakkas el-Zuhri el-Kureyşi, Safvan bin Vehb el-Fihri el-Kureyşi, Akil bin el-Bukeyr el-Leysi el-Kinani, Zu'ş-Şamaleyn bin Abd Amr el-Huza'i ve Mihca' bin Salih el-Aki. Ensar'dan ise sekiz kişi şunlardır: Sa'd bin Hayseme el-Evsi, Mubeşşir bin Abdilmünzir el-Ömeri el-Evsi, Yezid bin el-Haris el-Hazreği, Umeyr bin el-Humam es-Sülemi el-Hazreği, Rafi' bin el-Mu'alla ez-Zurki el-Hazreği, Haris bin Suraaka el-Neccari el-Hazreği, Muaviz bin el-Haris el-Neccari el-Hazreği ve Avf bin el-Haris el-Neccari el-Hazreği. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı hükümeti mezarlıkla ilgilenmiş ve onu duvarla çevirmiştir.||ID::Perang Badar Al-Kubra terjadi pada tahun kedua Hijriyah, dan sejumlah Sahabat syahid di dalamnya. Mereka dari kalangan Muhajirin adalah: Ubaydah bin al-Harith al-Mutallibi al-Qurashi, Umair bin Abi Waqqas al-Zuhri al-Qurashi, Safwan bin Wahb al-Fihri al-Qurashi, Aqil bin al-Bukayr al-Laithi al-Kinani, Dhu al-Shamalayn bin Abd Amr al-Khuza'i, dan Mahja' bin Salih al-Aki. Serta delapan orang dari kaum Ansar yaitu: Sa'd bin Khaythamah al-Awsi, Mubashir bin Abd al-Mundhir al-Omari al-Awsi, Yazid bin al-Harith al-Khazraji, Umair bin al-Humam al-Sulami al-Khazraji, Rafi' bin al-Mu'alla al-Zurqi al-Khazraji, Harith bin Suraqah al-Najari al-Khazraji, Mu'awdh bin al-Harith al-Najari al-Khazraji, dan Awf bin al-Harith al-Najari al-Khazraji. Pemerintah Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah memberikan perhatian pada pemakaman tersebut dan memagarnya||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/t3cL3RMSMbBLiCDy8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>38.7897269,23.7719809,106.8560702144074</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل الملائكة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::هو الموضع الذي فيه تأييد الملائكة للنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم في غزوة بدر قال تعالى: ﴿إِذْ تَسْتَغِيثُونَ رَبَّكُمْ فَاسْتَجَابَ لَكُمْ أَنِّي مُمِدُّكُم بِأَلْفٍ مِّنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ مُرْدِفِينَ﴾ [الأنفال: 9].||EN::t is the place where the angels supported the Prophet, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him, in the Battle of Badr. The Almighty said: 'When you sought help of your Lord and He answered you, Indeed, I will reinforce you with a thousand from the angels, rank upon rank' [Al-Anfal: 9]||TR::Burası, Bedr Gazvesi'nde meleklerin Hz. Peygamber -sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem-'e destek verdiği yerdir. Yüce Allah şöyle buyurmuştur: 'Hani Rabbinizden yardım diliyordunuz da O, size: "Şüphesiz ben sizi birbiri ardınca bin melekle destekleyeceğim" diye icabet etmişti.' [Enfâl: 9]."||ID::"Ini adalah tempat di mana para malaikat memberikan dukungan kepada Nabi -semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya- dalam Perang Badr. Allah Ta'ala berfirman: '(Ingatlah) ketika kamu memohon pertolongan kepada Tuhanmu, lalu Dia memperkenankan bagimu, "Sesungguhnya Aku akan mendatangkan bala bantuan kepada kamu dengan seribu malaikat yang datang berturut-turut." [Al-Anfal: 9].||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/Xn7yM2WnTcv3h94n8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>38.76458476047174,23.79380684875238,299.5772006571522</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر غرس</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::تقع بئر غرس، وتُعد من الآبار التاريخية المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية في المدينة المنورة. ويرجع اسمها إلى الغرس والزراعة التي اشتهرت بها المنطقة، فيما تذكر الروايات التاريخية أن البئر حفرها مالك بن النحاط، أحد أجداد الصحابي سعد بن خيثمة، الذي آلت إليه ملكيتها زمن الهجرة النبوية. وقد اكتسبت البئر مكانة دينية وتاريخية خاصة لورود أخبار تفيد بأن النبي ﷺ شرب من مائها وتوضأ منه واستعذب ماءها، كما رويت آثار تشير إلى وصيته لعلي بن أبي طالب رضي الله عنه بأن يُغسّل من مائها بعد وفاته.||EN::The Well of Ghars is located and is considered one of the historical wells associated with the prophetic biography in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Its name traces back to planting and agriculture for which the region was famous, while historical accounts mention that the well was dug by Malik bin al-Nuhad, one of the ancestors of the Companion Sa'd bin Khaythamah, whose ownership passed to him at the time of the prophetic migration. The well acquired a special religious and historical status due to reports stating that the Prophet ﷺ drank from its water, performed ablution with it, and found its water sweet. Furthermore, traditions have been narrated indicating his instruction to Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that he be washed with its water after his death||TR::Gars Kuyusu yer almakta olup, Medine-i Münevvere'de Hz. Peygamber'in hayatı (Siyer) ile bağlantılı tarihi kuyulardan biri olarak kabul edilmektedir. Adı, bölgenin ün saldığı dikim ve tarımdan gelmektedir; tarihî rivayetler ise bu kuyunun, nebevi hicret sırasında mülkiyeti kendisine geçen Sahabe Sa'd bin Hayseme'nin dedelerinden Malik bin Nuhad tarafından kazıldığını zikretmektedir. Kuyu, Hz. Peygamber ﷺ'in suyundan içtiği, ondan abdest aldığı ve suyunun tatlı olduğunu bulduğu yönünde haberlerin gelmesi nedeniyle özel bir dini ve tarihi statü kazanmıştır. Ayrıca, vefatından sonra Ali bin Ebu Talib'e (radıyallahu anh) kendi suyuyla yıkanmasını vasiyet ettiğine dair rivayetler nakledilmiştir."||ID::Sumur Ghars terletak dan dianggap sebagai salah satu sumur bersejarah yang berkaitan dengan sirah nabawiyah di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Namanya merujuk pada penanaman dan pertanian yang menjadi ciri khas wilayah tersebut, sementara catatan sejarah menyebutkan bahwa sumur tersebut digali oleh Malik bin al-Nuhad, salah satu kakek dari Sahabat Sa'd bin Khaythamah, yang kepemilikannya beralih kepadanya pada masa hijrah kenabian. Sumur ini memperoleh kedudukan religius dan historis yang khusus karena adanya riwayat yang menyebutkan bahwa Nabi ﷺ minum dari airnya, berwudhu darinya, dan mendapati airnya terasa tawar/segar. Selain itu, diriwayatkan pula atsar yang mengisyaratkan wasiat beliau kepada Ali bin Abi Talib (semoga Allah meridhainya) agar beliau dimandikan dengan airnya setelah wafatnya||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/G65jkF3gdF9nBTC38]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.6273216464627,24.44495080830531,606.3284177627618</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الدرع</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد الدرع ويُسمى ايضا مسجد الشيخين نسبة إلى جبلين، وكذلك مسجد البدائع وهذا الموقع عسكر فيه جيش المسلمين مع رسول الله ﷺ ليلة خروجهم لقتال المشركين في غزوة أُحد 15شوال 3 هـ. وصلى فيه النبي ﷺ الصلوات الخمس وبات فيه قبل التوجه لساحة المعركة.في هذا المكان قام النبي ﷺ برد بعض صغار الصحابة. وقد حرصت حكومة خادم الحرمين الشريفين بالمسجد وتطويره||EN::"Masjid al-Dir' (Mosque of the Armor/Shield), also called Masjid al-Shaykhayn in reference to two hills, as well as Masjid al-Bada'i'. At this site, the Muslim army encamped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night they went out to fight the polytheists in the Battle of Uhud on 15 Shawwal 3 AH. The Prophet ﷺ offered the five prayers in it and spent the night there before heading to the battlefield. In this place, the Prophet ﷺ sent back some of the young Companions. The government of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques has been keen to take care of the mosque and develop it.||TR::Zırh Mescidi (Mescid-i Dir'), iki tepeye nispetle Şeyheyn Mescidi ve ayrıca Bedâi Mescidi olarak da adlandırılır. Bu bölge, Müslüman ordusunun 15 Şevval H. 3 tarihinde Uhud Gazvesi'nde müşriklerle savaşmak üzere çıktıkları gece Allah'ın Resulü ﷺ ile birlikte karargâh kurduğu yerdir. Peygamber ﷺ burada beş vakit namazı kılmış ve savaş alanına gitmeden önce geceyi burada geçirmiştir. Bu mekânda Peygamber ﷺ bazı küçük yaştaki sahabeleri geri çevirmiştir. İki Haremeyn Hizmetkârı hükümeti mescidle ilgilenmeye ve onu geliştirmeye özen göstermiştir.||ID::Masjid al-Dir' (Masjid Baju Besi), yang juga dinamai Masjid al-Syaikhain dinisbahkan kepada dua bukit, serta Masjid al-Bada'i'. Lokasi ini adalah tempat pasukan kaum Muslimin berkemah bersama Rasulullah ﷺ pada malam keluarnya mereka untuk berperang melawan kaum musyrik dalam Perang Uhud pada 15 Syawal 3 H. Nabi ﷺ menunaikan shalat lima waktu di dalamnya dan bermalam di sana sebelum menuju ke medan pertempuran. Di tempat ini, Nabi ﷺ mengembalikan (menolak) sebagian Sahabat yang masih kecil. Pemerintah Pelayan Dua Tanah Suci telah berupaya keras memberikan perhatian pada masjid tersebut dan mengembangkannya||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/iUDmTPY7j7MZhoox8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60881320535584,24.48933568632545,601.5294792724231</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد بني أنيف</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::يُعد مسجد بني أُنيف، من المساجد التاريخية في منطقة قباء بالمدينة المنورة، ويقع جنوب غرب مسجد قباء. وقد ورد أن النبي ﷺ صلى في موضعه أثناء زيارته للصحابي طلحة بن البراء في مرضه||EN::Masjid Bani Unayf is considered one of the historical mosques in the Quba area in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, located southwest of Quba Mosque. It has been reported that the Prophet ﷺ prayed at its site during his visit to the Companion Talhah bin al-Bara' during his illness.||TR::Beni Üneyf Mescidi, Medine-i Münevvere'deki Kubâ bölgesinde yer alan tarihi mescitlerden biri olarak kabul edilir ve Kubâ Mescidi'nin güneybatısında yer alır. Hz. Peygamber ﷺ'in, hastalığı sırasında sahabe Talha bin el-Berâ'yı ziyareti esnasında bu mekânda namaz kıldığı rivayet edilmiştir||ID::Masjid Bani Unaif dianggap sebagai salah satu masjid bersejarah di kawasan Quba di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan terletak di sebelah barat daya Masjid Quba. Diriwayatkan bahwa Nabi ﷺ shalat di lokasinya saat mengunjungi Sahabat Talhah bin al-Bara' sewaktu beliau sakit||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/jUywEBxNZKVUTXtKA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61544705462619,24.43565345451015,615.8571209152201</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حصن بني واقف</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::يُعد حصن بني واقف من المعالم التاريخية الإسلامية في المدينة المنورة، سُمّي نسبة إلى بني واقف، وهم بطن من الأوس استقروا في هذه المنطقة، وتبرز أهميته التاريخية لورود روايات تفيد بأن النبي ﷺ صلى في مسجد بني واقف الواقع داخله، ويُعد الحصن أكبر حصون بني واقف.||EN::"Bani Waqif Fortress is considered one of the Islamic historical landmarks in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, named after Bani Waqif, who are a clan of the Aws who settled in this area. Its historical importance is highlighted by the presence of reports stating that the Prophet ﷺ prayed in the Bani Waqif Mosque located inside it, and the fortress is considered the largest of the Bani Waqif fortresses||TR::Beni Vâkıf Kalesi, Medine-i Münevvere'deki İslami tarihi simge yapılardan biri olarak kabul edilir ve adını bu bölgeye yerleşen Evs kabilesinin bir kolu olan Beni Vâkıf'tan almıştır. Tarihi önemi, Hz. Peygamber ﷺ'in kalesinin içinde yer alan Beni Vâkıf Mescidi'nde namaz kıldığını belirten rivayetlerin bulunmasıyla öne çıkmaktadır ve kale, Beni Vâkıf kalelerinin en büyüğü sayılmaktadır.||ID::Benteng Bani Waqif dianggap sebagai salah satu landmark bersejarah Islam di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, yang dinamai berdasarkan Bani Waqif, yaitu sebuah klan dari suku Aws yang menetap di wilayah ini. Keutamaan sejarahnya menonjol karena adanya riwayat-riwayat yang menyebutkan bahwa Nabi ﷺ shalat di Masjid Bani Waqif yang terletak di dalamnya, dan benteng ini dianggap sebagai benteng terbesar milik Bani Waqif||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/Be3hmmYUnXB7gwt86]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61984489820324,24.43669125628578,613.6085907709527</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة أحد</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غزوة أُحد: وقعت في السنة الثالثة للهجرة بين المسلمين وكفار قريش. خرج النبي ﷺ في نحو ألفٍ من المسلمين، ثم انسحب عبد الله بن أُبيّ بنحو ثلاثمائة رجل، فبقي مع النبي ﷺ قرابة سبعمائة مقاتل، في مقابل نحو ثلاثة آلاف من المشركين. وجعل النبي ﷺ خمسين من الرماة على جبل الرماة لحماية ظهر المسلمين، وأمرهم بلزوم مواقعهم. وبعد أن بدا النصر للمسلمين، ترك عدد من الرماة مواقعهم، فاستغل المشركون ذلك والتفوا على المسلمين، فاستشهد عدد من الصحابة، وفي مقدمتهم حمزة بن عبد المطلب رضي الله عنه، وأصيب النبي ﷺ. وقد طورت حكومة المملكة العربية السعودية الموقع من ضمن مشاريعها في المحافظة على الآثار التاريخية||EN::The Battle of Uhud took place in the third year of the Hijrah between the Muslims and the disbelievers of Quraish. The Prophet ﷺ went out with about one thousand Muslims, then Abdullah bin Ubayy withdrew with nearly three hundred men, leaving about seven hundred fighters with the Prophet ﷺ, compared to nearly three thousand polytheists. The Prophet ﷺ placed fifty archers on the Archers' Mountain to protect the Muslims' rear, ordering them to remain at their positions. After victory appeared to be for the Muslims, a number of archers left their positions, so the polytheists took advantage of this and encircled the Muslims. Consequently, a number of Companions were martyred, foremost among them Hamzah bin Abdul-Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him), and the Prophet ﷺ was injured. The government of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has developed the site as part of its projects to preserve historical antiquities||TR::Uhud Gazvesi, hicretin üçüncü yılında Müslümanlar ile Kureyş kâfirleri arasında gerçekleşti. Hz. Peygamber ﷺ yaklaşık bin Müslüman ile yola çıktı, ardından Abdullah bin Übey yaklaşık üç yüz kişiyle geri çekildi, böylece yaklaşık üç bin müşriğe karşı Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ile birlikte yaklaşık yedi yüz savaşçı kaldı. Hz. Peygamber ﷺ, Müslümanların arkasını korumak için Okçular Tepesi'ne elli okçu yerleştirdi ve onlara yerlerinden ayrılmamalarını emretti. Zafer Müslümanların lehine görünmeye başladıktan sonra, bazı okçular yerlerini terk etti, müşrikler bundan faydalanarak Müslümanları arkadan kuşattı, bunun üzerine başta Hamza bin Abdülmuttalib (radıyallahu anh) olmak üzere çok sayıda sahabe şehit oldu ve Hz. Peygamber ﷺ yaralandı. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı hükümeti, tarihi eserleri koruma projeleri kapsamında bu alanı geliştirmiştir||ID::Perang Uhud terjadi pada tahun ketiga Hijriyah antara kaum Muslimin dan kaum kafir Quraisy. Nabi ﷺ keluar bersama sekitar seribu kaum Muslimin, kemudian Abdullah bin Ubay mundur membawa sekitar tiga ratus orang, sehingga tersisa sekitar tujuh ratus pejuang bersama Nabi ﷺ, menghadapi sekitar tiga ribu kaum musyrik. Nabi ﷺ menempatkan lima puluh pemanah di Bukit Pemanah untuk melindungi bagian belakang kaum Muslimin, dan memerintahkan mereka untuk tetap di posisi mereka. Setelah kemenangan mulai tampak bagi kaum Muslimin, sejumlah pemanah meninggalkan posisi mereka, lalu kaum musyrik memanfaatkan hal tersebut dan mengepung kaum Muslimin, sehingga gugur sebagai syahid sejumlah Sahabat, yang terdepan di antaranya adalah Hamzah bin Abdul-Muttalib (semoga Allah meridhainya), dan Nabi ﷺ terluka. Pemerintah Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah mengembangkan situs ini sebagai bagian dari proyek-proyeknya dalam melestarikan peninggalan bersejarah||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/3q4ENGr1YFNxvzdr6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.6113130882414,24.50397102994774,600.9851734239051</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة بدر</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غزوة بدر الكبرى: وقعت في السنة الثانية للهجرة عند بدر، بين المسلمين وكفار قريش. خرج النبي ﷺ في نحو ثلاثمائة وبضعة عشر رجلًا، في مقابل نحو ألف مقاتل من قريش. وانتهت الغزوة بانتصار المسلمين، وقُتل من المشركين نحو سبعين وأُسر نحو سبعين، واستشهد من المسلمين أربعة عشر رجلًا.||EN::The Greater Battle of Badr took place in the second year of the Hijrah at Badr, between the Muslims and the disbelievers of Quraish. The Prophet ﷺ went out with about three hundred and a dozen men, compared to nearly one thousand fighters from Quraish. The battle ended with the victory of the Muslims, about seventy of the polytheists were killed and about seventy were captured, and fourteen men from the Muslims were martyred||TR::Büyük Bedir Gazvesi, hicretin ikinci yılında Bedir'de, Müslümanlar ile Kureyş kâfirleri arasında gerçekleşti. Hz. Peygamber ﷺ Kureyş'ten yaklaşık bin savaşçıya karşı yaklaşık üç yüz on küsur adamla yola çıktı. Gazve Müslümanların zaferiyle sona erdi; müşriklerden yaklaşık yetmiş kişi öldürüldü ve yaklaşık yetmiş kişi esir alındı, Müslümanlardan ise on dört adam şehit oldu.||ID::Perang Badar Al-Kubra terjadi pada tahun kedua Hijriyah di Badar, antara kaum Muslimin dan kaum kafir Quraisy. Nabi ﷺ keluar bersama sekitar tiga ratus belasan orang, menghadapi sekitar seribu pejuang dari Quraisy. Perang tersebut berakhir dengan kemenangan kaum Muslimin, sekitar tujuh puluh orang dari kaum musyrik tewas dan sekitar tujuh puluh orang ditawan, serta empat belas orang laki-laki dari kaum Muslimin gugur sebagai syahid.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/wa6KwrCQ3PnebnhC8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>38.78170680208984,23.77700220947299,123.8793954763847</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة الخندق</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غزوة الخندق (الأحزاب): وقعت في السنة الخامسة للهجرة، حين تحالفت قريش وغطفان وقبائل أخرى وساروا إلى المدينة في نحو عشرة آلاف مقاتل. وكان المسلمون قرابة ثلاثة آلاف رجل. وبإشارة سلمان الفارسي رضي الله عنه حُفر الخندق في الجهة المكشوفة من المدينة، فعجزت الأحزاب عن اقتحامها، واستمر الحصار حتى أرسل الله عليهم الريح فتفرق الجمع وانسحبوا، وقد حرصت المملكة العربية السعودية بالموقع وتطويره.||EN::The Battle of the Trench (Al-Ahzab/The Confederates) took place in the fifth year of the Hijrah, when Quraish, Ghatafan, and other tribes allied together and marched toward Madinah with about ten thousand fighters. The Muslims numbered nearly three thousand men. Upon the suggestion of Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him), the trench was dug on the exposed side of Madinah, rendering the Confederates unable to storm it. The siege continued until Allah sent upon them the wind, causing the gathering to disperse and withdraw. The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has been keen on the site and its development.||TR::Hendek (Ahzâb) Gazvesi, hicretin beşinci yılında Kureyş, Gatafân ve diğer kabilelerin müttefik olarak yaklaşık on bin savaşçıyla Medine'ye yürümesiyle gerçekleşti. Müslümanlar ise yaklaşık üç bin adamdı. Selman-ı Farisi'nin (radıyallahu anh) önerisiyle Medine'nin açıkta kalan tarafına hendek kazıldı, böylece Ahzâb birlikleri şehre girmekte aciz kaldı. Kuşatma, Allah üzerlerine rüzgârı gönderip topluluk dağılarak geri çekilene kadar devam etti. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı bu alana özen göstermiş ve onu geliştirmiştir.||ID::Perang Khandaq (Al-Ahzab) terjadi pada tahun kelima Hijriyah, ketika Quraisy, Ghatafan, dan suku-suku lainnya bersekutu dan bergerak menuju Madinah dengan membawa sekitar sepuluh ribu pejuang. Kaum Muslimin berjumlah hampir tiga ribu orang. Atas saran dari Salman al-Farsi (semoga Allah meridhainya), parit digali di bagian Madinah yang terbuka, sehingga pasukan sekutu gagal menerobosnya. Pengepungan berlanjut hingga Allah mengirimkan angin kepada mereka sehingga sekutu tersebut terpecah belah dan mundur. Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah memperhatikan situs ini dan mengembangkannya||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/LEBbxBuSGdf5fTae6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59529286840693,24.47705157615527,600.6928364313962</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الخليفة عمر بن الخطاب</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::أحد المساجد السبعة وينسب إلى الخليفة عمر بن الخطاب رضي الله عنه||EN::"One of the Seven Mosques, and it is attributed to the Caliph Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)."||TR::"Yedi Mescitler'den biri olup Halife Ömer bin el-Hattâb'a (radıyallahu anh) nispet edilmektedir."||ID::"Salah satu dari Tujuh Masjid, dan dinisbahkan kepada Khalifah Umar bin Khattab (semoga Allah meridhainya)."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/JRpj4oq11AW3zgtM8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59513911611427,24.47652429982055,600.1612295137422</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الخليفة أبي بكر</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::أحد المساجد السبعة ، وينسب إلى أبي بكر الصديق رضي الله عنه.||EN::"One of the Seven Mosques, and it is attributed to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him)."||TR::"Yedi Mescitler'den biri olup Ebu Bekir es-Sıddîk'a (radıyallahu anh) nispet edilmektedir."||ID::"Salah satu dari Tujuh Masjid, dan dinisbahkan kepada Abu Bakar ash-Shiddiq (semoga Allah meridhainya)."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/REmxvBJJGCaaYX3n7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59499104533641,24.47688006057288,599.9401279731493</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد سلمان الفارسي</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::أحد المساجد التاريخية السبعة الواقعة في منطقة الخندق، وسُمّي باسم الصحابي سلمان الفارسي رضي الله عنه، الذي أشار على النبي ﷺ بحفر الخندق||EN::"One of the seven historical mosques located in the Trench area, named after the Companion Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him), who suggested to the Prophet ﷺ the digging of the trench."||TR::"Hendek bölgesinde yer alan tarihi Yedi Mescitler'den biri olup, Hz. Peygamber ﷺ'e hendeğin kazılmasını öneren sahabe Selman-ı Farisi'ye (radıyallahu anh) atfen adlandırılmıştır."||ID::"Salah satu dari tujuh masjid bersejarah yang terletak di kawasan Khandaq, dan dinamai berdasarkan nama Sahabat Salman al-Farsi (semoga Allah meridhainya), yang mengusulkan kepada Nabi ﷺ untuk menggali parit."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/3R8dGDLBc2344xhdA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59560069689888,24.47741711512484,602.8692640263291</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الخليفة علي بن أبي طالب</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::أحد المساجد التاريخية السبعة المرتبطة بمنطقة غزوة الخندق، ونُسب إلى علي بن أبي طالب رضي الله عنه. يقع على في أرض مرتفعة.||EN::"One of the seven historical mosques associated with the area of the Battle of the Trench, and it is attributed to Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him). It is located on elevated ground."||TR::"Hendek Gazvesi bölgesiyle bağlantılı tarihi Yedi Mescitler'den biri olup Ali bin Ebu Talib'e (radıyallahu anh) nispet edilmiştir. Yüksek bir arazide yer almaktadır."||ID::"Salah satu dari tujuh masjid bersejarah yang berkaitan dengan kawasan Perang Khandaq, dan dinisbahkan kepada Ali bin Abi Talib (semoga Allah meridhainya). Masjid ini terletak di tanah yang tinggi."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/1SE4kyASAt9Ay5VA8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59540094363508,24.47578570352945,604.732519498993</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد سعد بن معاذ</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::أحد المساجد التاريخية السبعة المرتبطة بمنطقة غزوة الخندق، ونُسب إلى سعد بن معاذ رضي الله عنه أُصيب في غزوة الأحزاب بسهم في ذراعه، ثم حكم في بني قريظة، وتوفي رضي الله عنه سنة 5هـ.||EN::"One of the seven historical mosques associated with the area of the Battle of the Trench, and it is attributed to Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him). He was struck in the arm by an arrow during the Battle of Al-Ahzab (the Confederates), then he passed judgment on Banu Quraydhah, and he died (may Allah be pleased with him) in the year 5 AH."||TR::"Hendek Gazvesi bölgesiyle bağlantılı tarihi Yedi Mescitler'den biri olup Sa'd bin Muâz'a (radıyallahu anh) nispet edilmiştir. Ahzâb Gazvesi'nde kolundan bir okla yaralanmış, ardından Beni Kurayza hakkında hüküm vermiş ve H. 5 yılında vefat etmiştir (radıyallahu anh)."||ID::"Salah satu dari tujuh masjid bersejarah yang berkaitan dengan kawasan Perang Khandaq, dan dinisbahkan kepada Sa'd bin Mu'adh (semoga Allah meridhainya). Beliau terkena lemparan panah di lengannya pada Perang Al-Ahzab, kemudian memberikan keputusan hukum terhadap Bani Quraydhah, dan beliau wafat (semoga Allah meridhainya) pada tahun 5 H."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/iEEiwaf4fDn25CX78]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59501691967382,24.47582740134625,601.4860136939375</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل بني عبيد</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::جبل بني عبيد هو معلم تاريخي في المدينة المنورة، ارتبط بحدث بارز في السيرة النبوية أثناء غزوة الخندق (الأحزاب)؛ حيث كان موقعاً لـ "معجزة البشارات النبوية" عندما ضرب النبي ﷺ بصخرة صلبة عجز عنها الصحابة، فأضاءت ضرباته ببرقٍ كشف له وعاين فيه قصور اليمن والشام وقصر كسرى الأبيض بالمدائن، مبشراً بفتوح المسلمين المستقبلية لهذه الممالك.||EN::"Jabal Bani Ubayd is a historical landmark in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, associated with a prominent event in the prophetic biography during the Battle of the Trench (Al-Ahzab); where it was the site of the 'Miracle of Prophetic Glad Tidings' when the Prophet ﷺ struck a hard rock that the Companions were unable to break. His strikes illuminated with a lightning that revealed to him and through which he saw the palaces of Yemen, Levant (Sham), and the White Palace of Khosrow in Al-Mada'in, herald of the future Muslim conquests of these kingdoms."||TR::"Beni Ubeyd Dağı, Medine-i Münevvere'de tarihi bir simge yapı olup, Hendek (Ahzâb) Gazvesi sırasında nebevi siyerdeki belirgin bir olayla bağlantılıdır; zira sahabenin kırmaya güç yetiremediği sert bir kayaya Hz. Peygamber ﷺ'in vurmasıyla gerçekleşen 'Nebevi Müjdeler Mucizesi'nin yaşandığı yer olmuştur. Vuruşları, kendisine Yemen ve Şam saraylarını ve Medâin'deki Kısra'nın Beyaz Sarayı'nı gösteren ve gözleriyle gördüğü bir şimşekle aydınlanmış, Müslümanların bu krallıkları gelecekteki fetihlerini müdelemiştir."||ID::"Gunung Bani Ubayd adalah landmark bersejarah di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, yang berkaitan dengan peristiwa penting dalam sirah nabawiyah selama Perang Khandaq (Al-Ahzab); di mana tempat tersebut menjadi lokasi 'Mukjizat Kabar Gembira Kenabian' ketika Nabi ﷺ memukul batu keras yang tidak mampu dipecahkan oleh para Sahabat. Pukulan-pukulan beliau memancarkan kilat yang menyingkapkan bagi beliau dan beliau menyaksikan darinya istana-istana Yaman, Syam, dan Istana Putih Khosrow di Al-Mada'in, yang memberi kabar gembira atas penaklukan-penaklukan kaum Muslimin di masa depan terhadap kerajaan-kerajaan ini."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/V45dbZx4NdovC59BA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59164015484327,24.48425613663168,644.8290092277171</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>جبل قرين الصريحة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::جبل قرين صريحة هو موقع تاريخي مهم بالمدينة المنورة، ويُشتهر بأن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مر به عند قدومه للمدينة المنورة. وقد طورت حكومة خادم الحرمين الشريفين الموقع والمواقع حولها||EN::"Jabal Qurayn Sariyhah is an important historical site in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, and it is known that the Prophet, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him, passed by it upon his arrival to Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. The government of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques has developed the site and the sites around it."||TR::"Kurayn Sarıha Dağı, Medine-i Münevvere'de önemli bir tarihi alan olup, Hz. Peygamber -sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem-'in Medine-i Münevvere'ye gelişi sırasında oradan geçtiği bilinmektedir. İki Haremeyn Hizmetkârı hükümeti alanı ve etrafındaki alanları geliştirmiştir."||ID::"Gunung Qurayn Sarihah adalah situs bersejarah penting di Madinah Al-Munawwarah, dan terkenal bahwa Nabi -semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya- melewatinya saat kedatangan beliau ke Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Pemerintah Pelayan Dua Tanah Suci telah mengembangkan situs tersebut dan situs-situs di sekitarnya."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/UmZ8UmpWuQVMW8rNA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60995384550539,24.41310817144724,667.5489772490126</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>وادي العقيق المبارك</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::وادي العقيق من أشهر أودية المدينة المنورة. ارتباط بسيرة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، وسمي بالوادي المبارك لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام «أتاني الليلة آت من ربي فقال: صلّ في هذا الوادي المبارك». وقد طورت المملكة العربية السعودية الموقع والاهتمام به.||EN::"Wadi al-Aqiq is one of the most famous valleys in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. It is associated with the biography of the Prophet, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him, and was called the Blessed Valley due to his saying, peace and blessings be upon him: 'Tonight a visitor came to me from my Lord and said: Pray in this blessed valley.' The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has developed the site and taken care of it."||TR::"Akîk Vadisi, Medine-i Münevvere'nin en ünlü vadilerinden biridir. Hz. Peygamber -sallallahu aleyhi ve sellem-'in siyeri ile bağlantılıdır ve O'nun (aleyhissalâtü vesselâm) 'Bu gece Rabbimden bana gelen bir ziyaretçi: Bu mübarek vadide namaz kıl dedi' buyurması nedeniyle Mübarek Vadi olarak adlandırılmıştır. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı alanı geliştirmiş ve ona özen göstermiştir."||ID::"Lembah al-Aqiq adalah salah satu lembah paling terkenal di Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Lembah ini berkaitan dengan sirah Nabi -semoga shalawat dan salam Allah tercurah kepadanya-, dan dinamai Lembah yang Diberkahi karena sabda beliau -shalawat dan salam tercurah kepadanya-: 'Malam ini datang kepadaku utusan dari Tuhanku lalu berkata: Shalatlah di lembah yang diberkahi ini.' Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah mengembangkan situs tersebut dan memberikan perhatian kepadanya."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/pqWie5t3HMJmH1SN8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.57762886567688,24.4540030491537,609.8066952990794</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>وادي قناة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::وادي قناة من أشهر أودية المدينة المنورة.||EN::"Wadi Qanah is one of the most famous valleys in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah."||TR::"Kanât Vadisi, Medine-i Münevvere'nin en ünlü vadilerinden biridir."||ID::"Lembah Qanah adalah salah satu lembah paling terkenal di Madinah Al-Munawwarah."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/RCmdEKyc7P2ySSsF7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.62315796777547,24.49626518665963,612.1549893823843</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غار حراء</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غار حراء: يقع في جبل النور بمكة المكرمة، وكان النبي ﷺ يخلو فيه قبل البعثة، وفيه نزل عليه أول الوحي بقوله تعالى: ﴿اقرأ باسم ربك الذي خلق﴾. وقد اعتنت المملكة العربية السعودية بالموقع من خلال تطوير محيط جبل النور وإنشاء حي حراء الثقافي ومعرض الوحي لإثراء تجربة الزوار والتعريف بتاريخ المكان وبداية الرسالة النبوية||EN::"Hira Cave: Located in Jabal al-Nour in Makkah al-Mukarramah, the Prophet ﷺ used to seclude himself in it before the advent of his prophecy, and in it the first revelation descended upon him with the saying of the Almighty: ﴿Recite in the name of your Lord who created﴾. The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has taken care of the site by developing the surroundings of Jabal al-Nour and establishing the Hira Cultural District and the Revelation Exhibition to enrich the visitors' experience and to introduce the history of the place and the beginning of the prophetic message."||TR::"Hira Mağarası: Mekke-i Mükerreme'deki Nur Dağı'nda yer almaktadır; Hz. Peygamber ﷺ peygamberlik öncesinde burada inzivaya çekilirdi ve ilk vahiy Yüce Allah'ın ﴿Yaratan Rabbinin adıyla oku﴾ buyruğuyla burada kendisine inmiştir. Suudi Arabistan Krallığı, Nur Dağı'nın çevresini geliştirerek ve ziyaretçilerin deneyimini zenginleştirmek, mekanın tarihini ve nebevi mesajın başlangıcını tanıtmak amacıyla Hira Kültür Mahallesi ile Vahiy Sergisi'ni kurarak bu alana özen göstermiştir."||ID::"Gua Hira: Terletak di Jabal al-Nuur di Makkah al-Mukarramah, Nabi ﷺ biasa menyendiri (berkhalwat) di dalamnya sebelum kerasulan, dan di dalamnya wahyu pertama turun kepada beliau dengan firman Allah Ta'ala: ﴿Bacalah dengan menyebut nama Tuhanmu yang menciptakan﴾. Kerajaan Arab Saudi telah memberikan perhatian pada situs ini melalui pengembangan kawasan sekitar Jabal al-Nuur serta pembangunan Kawasan Kebudayaan Hira dan Pameran Wahyu untuk memperkaya pengalaman para pengunjung dan memperkenalkan sejarah tempat tersebut serta permulaan risalah kenabian."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/noHckwXJHunjs9cu5]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.86627714812107,21.45814930317579,526.3707288301725</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بادية بني سعد</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بادية بني سعد: هي الديار التي نشأ فيها النبي ﷺ في طفولته الأولى في كنف مرضعته حليمة السعدية رضي الله عنها من بني سعد بن بكر من هوازن وهذا هو الموقع الصحيح لبادية بني سعد وتسمى أوطاس وهي بادية شاسعة (تحذير الطريق وعر ويتطلب سيارة دفع رباعي)||EN::"Badiyat Bani Sa'd: It is the homeland where the Prophet ﷺ grew up in his early childhood under the care of his wet nurse Halimah al-Sa'diyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) from Bani Sa'd bin Bakr of Hawazin. This is the correct location for Badiyat Bani Sa'd, which is called Awtas, and it is a vast desert area (Warning: The road is rugged and requires a four-wheel-drive vehicle)."||TR::"Beni Sa'd Çölü (Bâdiyesi): Hz. Peygamber ﷺ'in erken çocukluk döneminde, Havâzin kabilesinin Beni Sa'd bin Bedr kolundan olan sütannesi Halîme es-Sa'diyye'nin (radıyallahu anhâ) himayesinde yetiştiği diyardır. Burası Beni Sa'd Çölü'nün doğru konumudur ve Evtâs olarak adlandırılır; engin bir çöldür (Uyarı: Yol engebeli olup dört çeker araç gerektirmektedir)."||ID::"Badiyat Bani Sa'd: Ini adalah daerah tempat tumbuh kembangnya Nabi ﷺ pada masa kanak-kanak awal beliau dalam asuhan ibu susuan beliau, Halimah al-Sa'diyyah (semoga Allah meridhainya) dari Bani Sa'd bin Bakr dari suku Hawazin. Ini adalah lokasi yang benar untuk Badiyat Bani Sa'd yang dinamai Awtas, dan merupakan padang pasir yang sangat luas (Peringatan: Jalanannya terjal/kasar dan membutuhkan kendaraan empat roda/4WD)."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/DPQ8HzZoYoEHDb8n8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>40.6177527772245,22.0540963528304,1031.973832535189</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>شعب بني هاشم مولد النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::هذا موضع شعب بني هاشم وهو أشهر الأقوال في تحديد مكان مولد النبي ﷺ. وقد آلت الدار بعد الهجرة إلى عقيل بن أبي طالب وذريته، ثم اشتراها محمد بن يوسف الثقفي، وفي سنة 171هـ حجّت الخيزران أم هارون الرشيد، فشرت المكان وجعلته مسجدا، وفي العهد السعودي وافق الملك عبدالعزيز على إنشاء مكتبة مكة المكرمة في الموضع سنة 1370هـ/1950م، فشُيّد المبنى ليكون مكتبة عامة، ولا يزال قائمًا .||EN::This is the location of the She'ib (valley/quarter) of Banu Hashim, which is the most famous opinion in identifying the birthplace of the Prophet ﷺ. After the Hijrah, the house passed into the ownership of Aqeel ibn Abi Talib and his descendants, and was later purchased by Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Thaqafi. In the year 171 AH, Al-Khayzuran, the mother of Harun al-Rashid, performed Hajj, purchased the place, and turned it into a mosque. During the Saudi era, King Abdulaziz agreed to establish the Makkah Al-Mukarramah Library at this site in the year 1370 AH / 1950 CE, so the building was constructed to serve as a public library, and it still stands today.||TR::Bura Banu Haşim Vadisi'dir (Şi'b Banu Haşim) ve Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ doğum yerinin belirlenmesinde en ünlü görüştür. Hicretten sonra ev, Akil bin Ebi Talib ve soyuna geçmiş, ardından Muhammed bin Yusuf el-SekaFi tarafından satın alınmıştır. Hicri 171 yılında Harun Reşid'in annesi el-Hayzuran hacca gelerek mekânı satın almış ve orayı camiye dönüştürmüştür. Suudi döneminde ise Kral Abdülaziz, Hicri 1370 / Miladi 1950 yılında bu alanda Mekke-i Mükerreme Kütüphanesi'nin kurulmasını onaylamış, böylece halk kütüphanesi olarak bina inşa edilmiştir ve halen varlığını sürdürmektedir.||ID::Ini adalah lokasi Syi'ib Bani Hasyim, dan ini merupakan pendapat paling terkenal dalam menentukan tempat kelahiran Nabi ﷺ. Setelah Hijrah, rumah tersebut beralih kepemilikannya kepada Aqil bin Abi Thalib dan keturunannya, kemudian dibeli oleh Muhammad bin Yusuf ats-Tsaqafi. Pada tahun 171 H, Al-Khayzuran, ibu dari Harun ar-Rasyid, menunaikan ibadah haji, lalu membeli tempat tersebut dan menjadikannya sebuah masjid. Pada era Arab Saudi, Raja Abdulaziz menyetujui pendirian Perpustakaan Makkah al-Mukarramah di lokasi tersebut pada tahun 1370 H / 1950 M, maka bangunan tersebut didirikan untuk menjadi perpustakaan umum, dan masih berdiri hingga saat ini.||MAPS::]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.82996848865433,21.42492656649157,298.8233586029481</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد السقيا</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد السقيا من المواضع التي توقف النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم واستعرض الجيش ودعاء لأهل المدينة وهو في طريقه إلى بدر، بُني في عهد الخليفة عمر بن عبدالعزيز، وفي عهد حكومة خادم الحرمين الشريفين حفظه الله اعتنت بالمسجد والاهتمام به.||EN::Al-Suqya Mosque is one of the sites where the Prophet ﷺ stopped, reviewed the army, and prayed for the people of Madinah on his way to Badr. It was built during the reign of Caliph Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and during the era of the government of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques, may Allah protect him, the mosque was cared for and attended to.||TR::Suqya Camii, Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ Bedir yolundayken durduğu, orduyu gözden geçirdiği ve Medine halkı için dua ettiği mekânlardan biridir. Halife Ömer bin Abdülaziz döneminde inşa edilmiştir; İki Kutsal Cami'nin Hizmetkârı'nın hükümeti döneminde ise (Allah onu korusun) camiye özen gösterilmiş ve önem verilmiştir.||ID::Masjid As-Suqya adalah salah satu tempat di mana Nabi ﷺ berhenti, memeriksa pasukan, และ berdoa untuk penduduk Madinah saat beliau dalam perjalanan menuju Badr. Masjid ini dibangun pada masa Khalifah Umar bin Abdul Aziz, dan pada masa pemerintahan Pelayan Dua Kota Suci, semoga Allah memeliharanya, masjid ini mendapat perhatian dan perawatan.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/waA8Kgrj91rzsp4e6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.60004147343425,24.46089113082633,610.5421315907299</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد بني حرام</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد بني حرام: مسجد تاريخي يقع في شعب بني حرام عند سفح جبل سلع، في منازل بني سلمة من الأنصار، ويُعرف أيضًا بمسجد جابر بن عبدالله رضي الله عنه، وفي هذا الموضع وقعت معجزة تكثير الطعام للنبي ﷺ وأصحابه أثناء حفر الخندق.||EN::Bani Haram Mosque: A historical mosque located in the She'ib (valley/quarter) of Bani Haram at the foot of Mount Sela, in the dwellings of Bani Salimah among the Ansar. It is also known as the Mosque of Jabir ibn Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him. In this location, the miracle of multiplying food for the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions occurred during the digging of the Trench.||TR::Beni Haram Camii: Sel Dağı'nın eteğindeki Beni Haram Vadisi'nde, Ensar'dan Beni Seleme'nin yerleşim yerinde bulunan tarihi bir camidir. Ayrıca Câbir bin Abdullah (Allah ondan razı olsun) Camii olarak da bilinir. Bu mekânda, Hendek kazımı sırasında Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ve ashabı için yemeğin çoğaltılması mucizesi gerçekleşmiştir.||ID::Masjid Bani Haram: Sebuah masjid bersejarah yang terletak di Syi'ib Bani Haram di kaki Gunung Sila', di pemukiman Bani Salamah dari kaum Ansar. Masjid ini juga dikenal sebagai Masjid Jabir bin Abdullah radhiyallahu 'anhu. Di tempat inilah terjadi mukjizat melimpahnya makanan untuk Nabi ﷺ dan para sahabat beliau saat penggalian Parit (Khandaq).||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/fv4Noarmj6GckvAP8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59725290099572,24.47311910179664,605.2975071902148</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة تبوك</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::في هذا الموضع صلى النبي صلى الله عله وسلم وجيشه أثناء مقاهم في غزوة تبوك ، وفي العهد السعودي رعت المملكة العربية السعودية بالمسجد وأعادت بناه||EN::In this location, the Prophet ﷺ and his army prayed during their stay in the Battle of Tabuk, and during the Saudi era, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia cared for the mosque and rebuilt it.||TR::Bu mekânda Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ve ordusu Tebük Gazvesi'ndeki konaklamaları sırasında namaz kılmıştır; Suudi döneminde ise Suudi Arabistan Krallığı camiye özen göstermiş ve onu yeniden inşa etmiştir.||ID::Di tempat inilah Nabi ﷺ dan pasukannya shalat selama mereka tinggal dalam Perang Tabuk, dan pada era Arab Saudi, Kerajaan Arab Saudi merawat masjid tersebut dan membangunnya kembali.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/ayCx3LSyzmCWAomD8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>36.55760051596596,28.38400297858408,766.6223167214062</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>حصن كعب الأشراف</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::حصن كعب بن الأشرف: حصن أثري من حصون بني النضير جنوب المدينة المنورة، بُني بالحجارة السوداء فوق هضبة صخرية. وينسب إلى كعب بن الأشرف الذي عادى النبي ﷺ وحرّض قريشًا على المسلمين، فقتل في السنة الثالثة للهجرة.||EN::Ka'b ibn al-Ashraf Fortress: An archaeological fortress from the fortresses of Banu Nadir in the south of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, built of black stones on a rocky plateau. It is attributed to Ka'b ibn al-Ashraf, who was hostile to the Prophet ﷺ and incited Quraysh against the Muslims, and was killed in the third year of the Hijrah.||TR::Ka'b bin el-Eşref Kalesi: Medine-i Münevvere'nin güneyinde, Banu Nadir kalelerinden biri olan, kayalık bir plato üzerinde siyah taşlardan inşa edilmiş tarihi bir kaledir. Hz. Peygamber'e ﷺ düşmanlık eden و Müslümanlara karşı Kureyş'i kışkırtan, Hicri üçüncü yılda öldürülen Ka'b bin el-Eşref'e nispet edilmektedir.||ID::Benteng Ka'b bin al-Asyraf: Sebuah benteng peninggalan sejarah dari benteng-benteng Bani Nadhir di selatan Madinah al-Munawwarah, dibangun dari batu-batu hitam di atas dataran tinggi berbatu. Benteng ini dinisbatkan kepada Ka'b bin al-Asyraf yang memusuhi Nabi ﷺ dan menghasut kaum Quraisy terhadap umat Islam, lalu dia terbunuh pada tahun ketiga Hijriah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/L96QCdbrq242MEoE6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.63362569882083,24.41871554986302,618.8453473370315</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر خاتم النبي ﷺ (أريس)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بئر الخاتم من أهم الآبار في المدينة المنورة، لأن النبي ﷺ قد جلس على طرفها ، وبشر أبا بكر وعمر وعثمان رضي الله عنهم بالجنة، ثم سقط خاتم النبي ﷺ من يد عثمان بن عفان  رضي الله عنه في هذا البئر.||EN::Al-Khatam Well is one of the most important wells in Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, because the Prophet ﷺ sat on its edge and gave glad tidings of Paradise to Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, then the ring of the Prophet ﷺ fell from the hand of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, into this well.||TR::Hâtem Kuyusu, Medine-i Münevvere'deki en önemli kuyulardan biridir; çünkü Hz. Peygamber ﷺ onun kenarında oturmuş ve Ebû Bekir, Ömer ile Osman'ı (Allah onlardan razı olsun) cennetle müjdelemiştir, ardından Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ yüzüğü Osman bin Affân'ın (Allah ondan razı olsun) elinden bu kuyuya düşmüştür.||ID::Sumur Al-Khatam adalah salah satu sumur terpenting di Madinah al-Munawwarah, karena Nabi ﷺ pernah duduk di tepinya dan memberi kabar gembira berupa surga kepada Abu Bakar, Umar, dan Utsman radhiyallahu 'anhum, kemudian cincin Nabi ﷺ jatuh dari tangan Utsman bin Affan radhiyallahu 'anhu ke dalam sumur ini.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/SpzCWDLz2exFzezx6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.61659939093343,24.43898393662838,610.9116922927525</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>شهداء غزوة الطائف</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::استشهد في غزوة الطائف – كما ذكر ابن إسحاق – اثنا عشر رجلًا، وهم: سعيد بن سعيد بن العاص بن أمية. عُرفطة بن جناب، وقيل: ابن حباب. عبد الله بن أبي بكر الصديق رضي الله عنهما، وقد أُصيب بسهم يوم الطائف ثم مات من أثره في المدينة بعد وفاة النبي ﷺ. عبد الله بن أبي أمية بن المغيرة. عبد الله بن عامر بن ربيعة. السائب بن الحارث بن قيس بن عدي. عبد الله بن الحارث بن قيس بن عدي. جُليحة بن عبد الله. ثابت بن الجذع. الحارث بن سهل بن أبي صعصعة. المنذر بن عبد الله. رُقيم بن ثابت بن ثعلبة بن زيد بن لوذان بن معاوية.||EN::Twelve men were martyred in the Battle of Ta'if – as mentioned by Ibn Ishaq – and they are: Sa'id ibn Sa'id ibn al-Aas ibn Umayyah. Urfutah ibn Janab, and it was said: Ibn Hubab. Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr as-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both, who was struck by an arrow on the day of Ta'if and later died from its effect in Al-Madinah after the death of the Prophet ﷺ. Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah. Abd Allah ibn Aamir ibn Rabi'ah. As-Sa'ib ibn al-Harith ibn Qays ibn Adi. Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Qays ibn Adi. Julaihah ibn Abd Allah. Thabit ibn al-Jid'u. Al-Harith ibn Sahl ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah. Al-Mundhir ibn Abd Allah. Ruqaym ibn Thabit ibn Tha'labah ibn Zayd ibn Lawdhan ibn Mu'awiyah.||TR::Taif Gazvesi'nde – İbn İshak'ın belirttiği gibi – on iki adam şehit olmuştur; onlar şunlardır: Sa'id bin Sa'id bin el-Âs bin Ümeyye. Urfuta bin Cenâb, (veya İbn Hubâb denildi). Abdullâh bin Ebî Bekir es-Sıddîk (Allah her ikisinden de razı olsun); Taif günü bir okla yaralanmış, ardından Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ vefatından sonra Medine'de bu yaranın tesiriyle vefat etmiştir. Abdullâh bin Ebî Ümeyye bin el-Mugîre. Abdullâh bin Âmir bin Rebi'a. Es-Sâib bin el-Hâris bin Kays bin Adî. Abdullâh bin el-Hâris bin Kays bin Adî. Culeyha bin Abdullâh. Sâbit bin el-Ciz'u. El-Hâris bin Sehl bin Ebî Sa'sa'a. El-Münzir bin Abdullâh. Rukaym bin Sâbit bin Sa'lebe bin Zeyd bin Lûzân bin Muâviye.||ID::Dua belas orang gugur sebagai syahid dalam Perang Tha'if – sebagaimana disebutkan oleh Ibn Ishaq – dan mereka adalah: Sa'id bin Sa'id bin al-Aas bin Umayyah. 'Urfuthah bin Janab, dan dikatakan: Ibn Hubab. Abdullah bin Abi Bakr ash-Shiddiq radhiyallahu 'anhuma, yang terkena panah pada hari Tha'if kemudian meninggal akibat luka tersebut di Madinah setelah wafatnya Nabi ﷺ. Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah bin al-Mughirah. Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi'ah. As-Sa'ib bin al-Harith bin Qays bin 'Adi. Abdullah bin al-Harith bin Qays bin 'Adi. Julaihah bin Abdullah. Thabit bin al-Jid'u. Al-Harith bin Sahl bin Abi Sa'sa'ah. Al-Mundhir bin Abdullah. Ruqaym bin Thabit bin Tha'labah bin Zayd bin Lawdhan bin Mu'awiyah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/Gk4XVW7pqGmUKnYU7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>40.40931883005532,21.27030764325918,1679.15255984685</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة الطائف</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غزوة الطائف: وقعت سنة 8هـ بعد حُنين، وسار إليها النبي ﷺ في نحو 12 ألفًا من المسلمين، فحاصر ثقيفًا في حصونها عدة أيام، ثم رفع الحصار وعاد. وأسلمت ثقيف بعد ذلك ووفدت على النبي ﷺ.||EN::The Battle of Ta'if: It took place in the year 8 AH after Hunayn, and the Prophet ﷺ marched to it with about 12,000 Muslims, besieging Thaqif in their fortresses for several days, then raised the siege and returned. Thaqif embraced Islam after that and came as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ.||TR::Taif Gazvesi: Hicri 8 yılında Huneyn'den sonra gerçekleşmiştir; Hz. Peygamber ﷺ yaklaşık 12 bin Müslüman ile oraya yürümüş, Sakîf kabilesini kalelerinde birkaç gün kuşatmış, ardından kuşatmayı kaldırıp geri dönmüştür. Sakîf kabilesi daha sonra İslam'ı kabul etmiş ve heyet halinde Hz. Peygamber'e ﷺ gelmiştir.||ID::Perang Tha'if: Terjadi pada tahun 8 H setelah Perang Hunain, dan Nabi ﷺ berangkat menuju ke sana bersama sekitar 12.000 umat Islam, lalu mengepung suku Thaqif di benteng-benteng mereka selama beberapa hari, kemudian mengangkat pengepungan dan kembali. Suku Thaqif masuk Islam setelah itu dan datang sebagai utusan kepada Nabi ﷺ.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/22Bm8pBz9VQDxzHW7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>40.40812281066555,21.26998765886058,1679.839157558469</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد البيعة (العقبة)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد تاريخي شهد بيعة العقبة بين النبي ﷺ والأنصار، والتي مهدت لهجرة المسلمين إلى المدينة المنورة. بُني المسجد سنة 144هـ/761م بأمر الخليفة العباسي أبي جعفر المنصور، وشهد عددًا من الترميمات عبر العصور. وقد أصبح اليوم من المعالم التاريخية البارزة في مكة المكرمة، وهو ضمن مشروع الأمير محمد بن سلمان لتطوير المساجد التاريخية، مع المحافظة على طابعه وقيمته المعمارية والتاريخية.||EN::A historical mosque that witnessed the Pledge of Aqaba between the Prophet ﷺ and the Ansar, which paved the way for the migration of Muslims to Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. The mosque was built in the year 144 AH / 761 CE by order of the Abbasid Caliph Abu Ja'far al-Mansur, and witnessed a number of restorations throughout the ages. Today, it has become one of the prominent historical landmarks in Makkah Al-Mukarramah, and it is within Prince Mohammed bin Salman Project for the Development of Historical Mosques, while preserving its architectural and historical character and value.||TR::Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ile Ensar arasında gerçekleşen ve Müslümanların Medine-i Münevvere'ye hicretine zemin hazırlayan Akabe Biatı'na tanıklık etmiş tarihi bir camidir. Cami, Hicri 144 / Miladi 761 yılında Abbasi Halifesi Ebû Ca'fer el-Mansûr'un emriyle inşa edilmiş ve çağlar boyunca birtakım restorasyonlar görmüştür. Günümüzde Mekke-i Mükerreme'nin önde gelen tarihi simgelerinden biri haline gelmiştir ve mimari ile tarihi dokusu ve değeri korunarak Prens Muhammed bin Selman Tarihi Camileri Geliştirme Projesi kapsamında yer almaktadır.||ID::Sebuah masjid bersejarah yang menjadi saksi Bai'at 'Aqabah antara Nabi ﷺ dan kaum Ansar, yang merintis jalan bagi hijrahnya umat Islam ke Madinah al-Munawwarah. Masjid ini dibangun pada tahun 144 H / 761 M atas perintah Khalifah Abbasiyah Abu Ja'far al-Mansur, dan mengalami sejumlah renovasi sepanjang masa. Kini, masjid ini menjadi salah satu landmark bersejarah yang menonjol di Makkah al-Mukarramah, dan termasuk dalam Proyek Pangeran Mohammed bin Salman untuk Pengembangan Masjid-Masjid Bersejarah, dengan tetap menjaga karakter serta nilai arsitektur dan sejarahnya.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/ejdyRNvUNxFEBjRS8]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.86750691818757,21.42456269067714,355.5608710120376</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غار ثور</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::غار ثور: يقع في جبل ثور جنوب مكة المكرمة، وفيه اختبأ النبي ﷺ وأبو بكر الصديق رضي الله عنه ثلاث ليالٍ في بداية الهجرة إلى المدينة. وقد اعتنت المملكة بالموقع من خلال مراكز خدمة الزوار، ومشروع حي جبل ثور الثقافي الذي يضم مرافق ثقافية ومعرضًا للهجرة النبوية لإبراز تاريخ المكان وإثراء تجربة الزائر.||EN::Thawr Cave: It is located in Mount Thawr south of Makkah Al-Mukarramah, and in it the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr as-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, hid for three nights at the beginning of the migration to Al-Madinah. The Kingdom has taken care of the site through visitor service centers and the Cultural Mount Thawr Neighborhood Project, which includes cultural facilities and an exhibition of the Prophetic Migration to highlight the history of the place and enrich the visitor’s experience.||TR::Sevr Mağarası: Mekke-i Mükerreme'nin güneyindeki Sevr Dağı'nda yer almakta olup, Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ve Ebû Bekir es-Sıddîk (Allah ondan razı olsun) Medine'ye hicretin başlangıcında burada üç gece saklanmışlardır. Krallık; ziyaretçi hizmet merkezleri ve mekânın tarihini ön plana çıkarmak ile ziyaretçi deneyimini zenginleştirmek amacıyla kültürel tesisler ve Peygamber'in Hicreti Sergisi'ni barındıran Sevr Dağı Kültür Mahallesi Projesi aracılığıyla bu alana özen göstermiştir.||ID::Gua Thawr: Terletak di Gunung Thawr di selatan Makkah al-Mukarramah, dan di sinilah Nabi ﷺ bersama Abu Bakar ash-Shiddiq radhiyallahu 'anhu bersembunyi selama tiga malam pada awal hijrah ke Madinah. Kerajaan telah merawat lokasi tersebut melalui pusat-pusat layanan pengunjung dan Proyek Kawasan Budaya Gunung Thawr yang mencakup fasilitas-fasilitas budaya serta pameran Hijrah Nabi untuk menonjolkan sejarah tempat tersebut dan memperkaya pengalaman pengunjung.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/adQGs4LNPFrWUDb46]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.85003649958083,21.37734287077669,746.2567500879201</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الحديبية</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد تاريخي يقع في منطقة الحديبية غرب مكة المكرمة، ويرتبط بأحداث صلح الحديبية سنة 6هـ، حين خرج النبي ﷺ قاصدًا العمرة ومعه نحو 1400 من الصحابة، فمنعتهم قريش من دخول مكة. وفي الحديبية جرت بيعة الرضوان تحت الشجرة، ثم عُقد الصلح بين النبي ﷺ وقريش،||EN::A historical mosque located in the Al-Hudaybiyyah area west of Makkah Al-Mukarramah, associated with the events of the Treaty of Al-Hudaybiyyah in the year 6 AH, when the Prophet ﷺ set out intending to perform Umrah accompanied by about 1,400 of the Companions, but Quraysh prevented them from entering Makkah. In Al-Hudaybiyyah, the Pledge of Al-Ridwan took place under the tree, then the treaty was concluded between the Prophet ﷺ and Quraysh.||TR::Mekke-i Mükerreme'nin batısındaki el-Hudeybiye bölgesinde yer alan tarihi bir cami olup, Hicri 6 yılında Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ yaklaşık 1400 sahabi ile birlikte Umre niyetiyetiyle yola çıktığı ve Kureyş'in onları Mekke'ye girmekten alıkoyduğu Hudeybiye Antlaşması olaylarıyla bağlantılıdır. Hudeybiye'de ağacın altında Rıdvan Biatı gerçekleşmiş, ardından Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ile Kureyş arasında barış antlaşması akdedilmiştir.||ID::Sebuah masjid bersejarah yang terletak di kawasan Al-Hudaibiyah di sebelah barat Makkah al-Mukarramah, terikat dengan peristiwa Perjanjian Al-Hudaibiyah pada tahun 6 H, ketika Nabi ﷺ berangkat dengan maksud melaksanakan umrah bersama sekitar 1.400 sahabat, namun kaum Quraisy menghalangi mereka untuk memasuki Makkah. Di Al-Hudaibiyah, terjadi Bai'at ar-Ridhwan di bawah pohon, kemudian dilangsungkan perjanjian damai antara Nabi ﷺ dan kaum Quraisy.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/6DLK3adHb1xjMFMNA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.62571446286499,21.44207976409232,144.1430592917725</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر طوى</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بئر تاريخية تقع في وادي طُوى بحي جرول شمال غربي المسجد الحرام، على مسافة تقارب 1.3 كم منه، وترتبط بعدد من أحداث السيرة النبوية. فقد كان النبي ﷺ ينزل بوادي طوى عند قدومه إلى مكة، ويبيت فيه حتى يصبح، ثم يصلي ويغتسل قبل دخولها، وثبت ذلك في حديث عبدالله بن عمر رضي الله عنهما. ويرتبط الوادي كذلك بـفتح مكة؛ إذ بات النبي ﷺ فيه قبل دخولها، ثم أصبح فدخل مكة، كما نُقل نزوله به في بعض أسفاره إلى مكة. وكان عبدالله بن عمر رضي الله عنهما يقتدي بالنبي ﷺ، فيبيت بذي طوى ويغتسل قبل دخول مكة. وتحظى بئر طوى ومحيطها اليوم بالعناية ضمن جهود الهيئة الملكية لمدينة مكة المكرمة والمشاعر المقدسة لتأهيل وإبراز المواقع التاريخية المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية.||EN::A historical well located in Tuwa Valley in the Jarwal neighborhood northwest of the Al-Masjid al-Haram, at a distance of approximately 1.3 km from it, and associated with a number of events in the Prophetic Biography. The Prophet ﷺ used to dismount in Tuwa Valley upon his arrival in Makkah, spend the night in it until morning, and then pray and perform ghusl (bath) before entering it; this is confirmed in the hadeeth of Abd Allah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. The valley is also associated with the Conquest of Makkah, as the Prophet ﷺ spent the night in it before entering it, then woke in the morning and entered Makkah, and his staying in it was also reported during some of his journeys to Makkah. Abd Allah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to follow the example of the Prophet ﷺ, spending the night in Dhu Tuwa and performing ghusl before entering Makkah. Today, Tuwa Well and its surroundings receive care as part of the efforts of the Royal Commission for Makkah City and Holy Sites to rehabilitate and highlight historical sites associated with the Prophetic Biography.||TR::Mescid-i Haram'ın kuzeybatısında, Ondan yaklaşık 1,3 km uzaklıkta, Cervel mahallesindeki Tuvâ Vadisi'nde yer alan ve Peygamber'in Hayatı'ndaki (Siyer) birtakım olaylarla bağlantılı olan tarihi bir kuyudur. Hz. Peygamber ﷺ Mekke'ye geldiğinde Tuvâ Vadisi'nde konaklar, sabaha kadar orada geceler, ardından Mekke'ye girmeden önce namaz kılıp gusül alırdı; bu durum Abdullah bin Ömer'in (Allah her ikisinden de razı olsun) hadisinde sabit olmuştur. Vadi aynı zamanda Mekke'nin Fethi ile de bağlantılıdır; nitekim Hz. Peygamber ﷺ Mekke'ye girmeden önce orada gecelemiş, ardından sabah olunca Mekke'ye girmiştir, ayrıca Mekke'ye yaptığı bazı yolculuklarında da orada konakladığı nakledilmiştir. Abdullah bin Ömer (Allah her ikisinden de razı olsun) Hz. Peygamber'i ﷺ örnek alır, Zî Tuvâ'da geceler ve Mekke'ye girmeden önce gusül alırdı. Günümüzde Tuvâ Kuyusu ve çevresi, Mekke-i Mükerreme Şehri ve Kutsal Mekânlar Kraliyet Komisyonu'nun Peygamber'in Hayatı ile bağlantılı tarihi mekânları ihya etme ve ön plana çıkarma çabaları kapsamında özen görmektedir.||ID::Sebuah sumur bersejarah yang terletak di Lembah Thuwa di kawasan Jarwal, sebelah barat laut Al-Masjid al-Haram, dengan jarak sekitar 1,3 km darinya, dan terikat dengan sejumlah peristiwa Sirah Nabawiyah. Nabi ﷺ biasa singgah di Lembah Thuwa saat tiba di Makkah, bermalam di sana hingga subuh, lalu shalat dan mandi sebelum memasukinya; hal ini telah shahih dalam hadits Abdullah bin Umar radhiyallahu 'anhuma. Lembah ini juga terikat dengan Pembebasan Kota Makkah (Fath Makkah), di mana Nabi ﷺ bermalam di sana sebelum memasukinya, lalu pada pagi hari beliau masuk ke Makkah, sebagaimana diriwayatkan pula persinggahan beliau di sana dalam sebagian perjalanan beliau ke Makkah. Abdullah bin Umar radhiyallahu 'anhuma selalu meneladani Nabi ﷺ, dengan bermalam di Dzu Thuwa dan mandi sebelum memasuki Makkah. Saat ini, Sumur Thuwa dan sekitarnya mendapat perhatian dalam kerangka upaya Komisi Kerajaan untuk Kota Makkah al-Mukarramah dan Tempat-Tempat Suci untuk merehabilitasi dan menonjolkan situs-situs bersejarah yang terikat dengan Sirah Nabawiyah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/PaT4XKtq1i7S8AQLA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.8165375600514,21.4315995238967,282.813669668803</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة حنين</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::وقعت في السنة الثامنة للهجرة بعد فتح مكة، حين خرج النبي ﷺ لمواجهة قبيلة هوازن في وادي حُنين. وكان مع المسلمين نحو اثني عشر ألفًا؛ عشرة آلاف ممن خرجوا معه لفتح مكة وألفان من أهل مكة. وفي بداية المعركة باغتت هوازن المسلمين من شعاب الوادي، فاضطربت الصفوف وتراجع كثير منهم، وثبت النبي ﷺ ومعه جماعة من أصحابه، ثم عاد المسلمون إلى القتال حتى تحقق لهم النصر. وقد خلد القرآن أحداثها في سورة التوبة بقوله تعالى: ﴿وَيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ إِذْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ﴾ [التوبة: 25].||EN::It occurred in the eighth year of the Hijrah after the Conquest of Makkah, when the Prophet ﷺ set out to face the tribe of Hawazin in the Valley of Hunayn. There were about twelve thousand with the Muslims; ten thousand of those who set out with him for the Conquest of Makkah and two thousand from the people of Makkah. At the beginning of the battle, Hawazin ambushed the Muslims from the ravines of the valley, so the ranks were disrupted and many of them retreated, while the Prophet ﷺ remained steadfast along with a group of his Companions, then the Muslims returned to the fight until victory was achieved for them. The Qur'an immortalized its events in Surat At-Tawbah in the words of the Exalted: ﴿And [also some reward] on the day of Hunayn, when your great number pleased you﴾ [At-Tawbah: 25].||TR::Mekke'nin Fethi'nden sonra Hicri sekizinci yılda, Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ Huneyn Vadisi'nde Hevâzin kabilesiyle karşılaşmak üzere yola çıkmasıyla gerçekleşmiştir. Müslümanların yanında yaklaşık on iki bin kişi vardı; on bini Mekke'nin Fethi için kendisiyle birlikte yola çıkanlardan, iki bini ise Mekke halkındandı. Savaşın başlangıcında Hevâzin, vadinin geçitlerinden Müslümanlara baskın yaptı, böylece saflar bozuldu ve birçoğu geri çekildi, ancak Hz. Peygamber ﷺ ve ashâbından bir grup kararlılıkla yerlerinde kaldı, ardından Müslümanlar savaşa geri döndü ve nihayet zafer onlar için gerçekleşti. Kur'an-ı Kerim, Tevbe Suresi'nde Yüce Allah'ın şu buyruğuyla onun olaylarını ölümsüzleştirmiştir: ﴿Huneyn gününde de (Allah size yardım etmişti); hani çokluğunuz sizi böbürlendirmişti...﴾ [Tevbe: 25].||ID::Terjadi pada tahun kedelapan Hijriah setelah Pembebasan Kota Makkah (Fath Makkah), ketika Nabi ﷺ berangkat untuk menghadapi suku Hawazin di Lembah Hunain. Bersama umat Islam ada sekitar dua belas ribu orang; sepuluh ribu dari mereka yang berangkat bersama beliau untuk Pembebasan Makkah dan dua ribu dari penduduk Makkah. Pada awal pertempuran, Hawazin menyergap umat Islam dari celah-celah lembah, sehingga barisan menjadi kacau dan banyak dari mereka yang mundur, namun Nabi ﷺ tetap bertahan bersama sekelompok sahabat beliau, kemudian umat Islam kembali bertempur hingga kemenangan berhasil diraih oleh mereka. Al-Qur'an mengabadikan peristiwa tersebut dalam Surah At-Taubah melalui firman Allah Ta'ala: ﴿Dan (ingatlah) perang Hunain, yaitu diwaktu kamu menjadi congkak karena banyaknya jumlahmu...﴾ [At-Taubah: 25].||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/w5cKd1q6cmrdEFuz7]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>40.05522650303425,21.51989979804695,471.1030928627388</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بَحْرَة الرُّغاء</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بحرة الرُّغاء: موضع تاريخي في وادي لِيَّة على طريق النبي ﷺ إلى الطائف سنة 8هـ بعد غزوة حُنين. نزل النبي ﷺ فيه وبُني له مسجد فصلى فيه، وكان فيه حصن مالك بن عوف النَّصري، قائد هوازن في حُنين، فأمر النبي ﷺ بهدمه فهُدم، ثم واصل المسلمون سيرهم نحو الطائف.||EN::Bahrat al-Rugha': A historical location in the Liyyah Valley on the path of the Prophet ﷺ to Ta'if in the year 8 AH after the Battle of Hunayn. The Prophet ﷺ stayed there and a mosque was built for him where he prayed. In it was the fortress of Malik ibn 'Awf al-Nasri, the leader of Hawazin in Hunayn, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered its demolition and it was demolished, then the Muslims continued their journey toward Ta'if.||TR::Bahratü’r-Ruğâ: Huneyn Gazvesi'nden sonra Hicri 8 yılında Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ Taif yolunda, Liyye Vadisi'nde yer alan tarihi bir mekândır. Hz. Peygamber ﷺ orada konaklamış ve kendisi için bir cami inşa edilerek orada namaz kılmıştır. Burada, Huneyn'de Hevâzin'in komutanı olan Mâlik bin Avf en-Nasrî'nin kalesi bulunuyordu; Hz. Peygamber ﷺ onun yıkılmasını emretti ve kale yıkıldı, ardından Müslümanlar Taif'e doğru yürüyüşlerine devam ettiler.||ID::Bahrah ar-Rugha': Sebuah lokasi bersejarah di Lembah Liyyah dalam jalur perjalanan Nabi ﷺ menuju Tha'if pada tahun 8 H setelah Perang Hunain. Nabi ﷺ singgah di sana dan dibangunkan sebuah masjid untuk beliau lalu beliau shalat di dalamnya. Di tempat itu terdapat benteng Malik bin 'Auf an-Nashri, pemimpin suku Hawazin dalam Perang Hunain, maka Nabi ﷺ memerintahkan untuk meruntuhkannya lalu benteng itu diruntuhkan, kemudian umat Islam melanjutkan perjalanan mereka menuju Tha'if.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/oUjEFbWmGDXULemb6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>40.54078823439649,21.24449883839136,1582.926554700879</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>مسجد الجعرانة</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::مسجد الجعرانة: مسجد تاريخي يقع شمال شرقي مكة المكرمة بنحو 25 كم، في الموضع الذي نزل فيه النبي ﷺ بعد غزوة حُنين والطائف سنة 8هـ، وقسّم فيه غنائم حُنين، ثم أحرم منه لعمرة الجعرانة. وقد شهد المسجد توسعات وتجديدات متعاقبة، وحظي في العهد السعودي بعناية كبيرة وتطوير للخدمات والمرافق، مع المحافظة على مكانته التاريخية المرتبطة بالسيرة النبوية.||EN::Ji'ranah Mosque: A historical mosque located approximately 25 km northeast of Makkah Al-Mukarramah, at the location where the Prophet ﷺ stayed after the Battles of Hunayn and Ta'if in the year 8 AH, and distributed the spoils of Hunayn, then entered the state of ihram from it for the Umrah of Ji'ranah. The mosque has witnessed successive expansions and renovations, and during the Saudi era, it received great care and development of services and facilities, while preserving its historical status associated with the Prophetic Biography.||TR::Cîrâne Camii: Mekke-i Mükerreme'nin yaklaşık 25 km kuzeydoğusunda, Hicri 8 yılında Huneyn ve Taif gazvelerinden sonra Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ konakladığı, Huneyn ganimetlerini paylaştırdığı ve ardından Cîrâne Umresi için ihrama girdiği mekânda yer alan tarihi bir camidir. Cami, birbirini izleyen genişletme ve yenileme çalışmalarına tanıklık etmiş, Suudi döneminde ise Peygamber'in Hayatı ile bağlantılı tarihi konumunu koruyarak hizmetlerin ve tesislerin geliştirilmesiyle büyük ilgi görmüştür.||ID::Masjid Ji'ranah: Sebuah masjid bersejarah yang terletak sekitar 25 km di sebelah timur laut Makkah al-Mukarramah, di lokasi tempat Nabi ﷺ singgah setelah Perang Hunain dan Tha'if pada tahun 8 H, dan membagikan rampasan perang Hunain di sana, kemudian berihram darinya untuk Umrah Ji'ranah. Masjid ini telah mengalami perluasan dan renovasi secara bertahap, serta mendapat perhatian besar dan pengembangan fasilitas dan layanan pada era Arab Saudi, dengan tetap menjaga kedudukan sejarahnya yang terikat dengan Sirah Nabawiyah.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/6VPoeV4VY2i2k4Bm6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.95152465301635,21.56822721922843,460.7411321822863</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر الروحاء</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بئر الروحاء بئر تاريخية تقع في وادي الروحاء جنوب غربي المدينة المنورة، على الطريق القديم الواصل بين المدينة المنورة ومكة المكرمة، وكانت الروحاء من المنازل المعروفة التي تنزل بها القوافل والحجاج للتزود بالماء والراحة. وقد ارتبط الموضع بالسيرة النبوية؛ إذ مرّ به النبي ﷺ في عدد من أسفاره، ومن أشهرها مسيره إلى غزوة بدر||EN::Al-Rawha' Well is a historical well located in the Al-Rawha' Valley southwest of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, on the ancient road connecting Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah and Makkah Al-Mukarramah. Al-Rawha' was one of the well-known stations where caravans and pilgrims would dismount to resupply with water and rest. The location has been associated with the Prophetic Biography, as the Prophet ﷺ passed through it during a number of his journeys, the most famous of which was his march to the Battle of Badr.||TR::Ravhâ Kuyusu, Medine-i Münevvere'nin güneybatısında, Medine-i Münevvere ile Mekke-i Mükerreme'yi birbirine bağlayan eski yol üzerinde, Ravhâ Vadisi'nde yer alan tarihi bir kuyudur. Ravhâ, kervanların ve hacıların su tedarik etmek ve dinlenmek için konakladıkları bilinen konaklama yerlerinden biriydi. Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ birtakım yolculuklarında oradan geçmesiyle bu mekân Peygamber'in Hayatı (Siyer) ile bağlantılı hale gelmiştir; bu yolculukların en ünlüsü ise Bedir Gazvesi'ne yürüyüşüdür.||ID::Sumur Al-Rauha' adalah sebuah sumur bersejarah yang terletak di Lembah Al-Rauha' di sebelah barat daya Madinah al-Munawwarah, di jalur kuno yang menghubungkan Madinah al-Munawwarah dan Makkah al-Mukarramah. Al-Rauha' merupakan salah satu persinggahan terkenal tempat kafilah dan jemaah haji singgah untuk mengambil pasokan air dan beristirahat. Lokasi ini terikat dengan Sirah Nabawiyah; di mana Nabi ﷺ melintasinya dalam sejumlah perjalanan beliau, yang paling terkenal di antaranya adalah perjalanan beliau menuju Perang Badr.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/zGjMNye39n9Fncad6]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.1681466253778,24.07968463201461,548.2269037105702</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة خيبر</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::وقعت غزوة خيبر في السنة السابعة للهجرة، عندما خرج النبي ﷺ من المدينة في نحو 1400 من المسلمين إلى واحة خيبر شمال المدينة المنورة. وكانت خيبر  تنتشر فيها حصون منيعة يسكنها اليهود. بدأ المسلمون بفتح الحصون تباعًا حتى انتصر المسلمون وصالح النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أهلها على أن يعملوا فيها وللنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم نصف زرعها وثمارها||EN::The Battle of Khaybar occurred in the seventh year of the Hijrah, when the Prophet ﷺ set out from Al-Madinah with about 1,400 Muslims to the oasis of Khaybar north of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah. Khaybar contained formidable fortresses inhabited by Jews. The Muslims began conquering the fortresses one by one until the Muslims achieved victory, and the Prophet ﷺ made peace with its people on the condition that they work in it and half of its crops and fruits belong to the Prophet ﷺ.||TR::Hayber Gazvesi, Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ Medine'den yaklaşık 1400 Müslüman ile Medine-i Münevvere'nin kuzeyindeki Hayber vahasına doğru yola çıkmasıyla Hicri yedinci yılda gerçekleşmiştir. Hayber'de Yahudilerin ikamet ettiği müstahkem kaleler bulunuyordu. Müslümanlar kaleleri sırayla fethetmeye başladı, nihayet Müslümanlar zafer kazandı ve Hz. Peygamber ﷺ, orada çalışmaları ve ürün ile meyvelerinin yarısı Hz. Peygamber'e ﷺ ait olması şartıyla halkıyla barış yaptı.||ID::Perang Khaybar terjadi pada tahun ketujuh Hijriah, ketika Nabi ﷺ berangkat dari Madinah bersama sekitar 1.400 umat Islam menuju oase Khaybar di sebelah utara Madinah al-Munawwarah. Di Khaybar tersebar benteng-benteng kokoh yang dihuni oleh kaum Yahudi. Umat Islam mulai menaklukkan benteng-benteng tersebut satu per satu hingga umat Islam meraih kemenangan, dan Nabi ﷺ berdamai dengan penduduknya dengan syarat mereka menggarap tanah tersebut serta separuh dari hasil tanaman dan buah-buahannya milik Nabi ﷺ.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/FkVFuoxnJcyV1NzF9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.2679350750326,25.73072924361237,718.1850358224556</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غزوة الأبواء</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::أول غزوة خرج فيها النبي ﷺ بنفسه بعد الهجرة، وكانت في شهر صفر سنة 2هـ. سار المسلمون من المدينة حتى بلغوا الأبواء، في الطريق بين مكة والمدينة، لاعتراض عير لقريش، إلا أنه لم يقع قتال. وفي الأبواء عقد النبي ﷺ صلحًا مع بني ضَمرة على الموادعة، ثم عاد إلى المدينة. وتسمى هذه الغزوة أيضًا غزوة وَدّان لقرب الموضعين من بعضهما.||EN::The first battle in which the Prophet ﷺ went out in person after the Hijrah, and it took place in the month of Safar in the year 2 AH. The Muslims marched from Al-Madinah until they reached Al-Abwa', on the road between Makkah and Al-Madinah, to intercept a caravan belonging to Quraysh, but no fighting occurred. In Al-Abwa', the Prophet ﷺ concluded a peace treaty with Banu Damrah for mutual peaceful coexistence, then returned to Al-Madinah. This battle is also called the Battle of Waddan due to the proximity of the two locations to each other.||TR::Hicretten sonra Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ bizzat katıldığı ilk gazve olup, Hicri 2 yılının Sefer ayında gerçekleşmiştir. Müslümanlar, Kureyş'e ait bir kervanın önünü kesmek amacıyla Medine'den yola çıkarak Mekke ile Medine arasındaki yol üzerinde bulunan el-Ebvâ'ya kadar ulaştılar, ancak bir savaş gerçekleşmedi. Hz. Peygamber ﷺ el-Ebvâ'da Banu Damra kabilesi ile barışçıl ilişki ve dostluk antlaşması akdetti, ardından Medine'ye döndü. Bu gazve, iki mekânın birbirine yakınlığı sebebiyle Veddân Gazvesi olarak da adlandırılır.||ID::Perang pertama yang diikuti oleh Nabi ﷺ secara langsung setelah Hijrah, dan terjadi pada bulan Safar tahun 2 H. Umat Islam berangkat dari Madinah hingga mencapai Al-Abwa', di jalan antara Makkah dan Madinah, untuk menghadang kafilah milik Quraisy, namun tidak terjadi pertempuran. Di Al-Abwa', Nabi ﷺ mengadakan perjanjian damai dengan Bani Dhamrah untuk saling menjaga perdamaian, kemudian kembali ke Madinah. Perang ini disebut juga Perang Waddan karena berdekatan lokasi keduanya satu sama lain.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/qR7PmZ9J2Zt3eAVg9]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.08726327090159,23.10200454030169,73.68938668049162</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>بئر أهاب</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::بئر تاريخية من آبار المدينة المنورة، كانت تقع في الحرة الغربية، وعُرفت في بعض المصادر المتأخرة باسم «بئر زمزم». ورد أن النبي ﷺ مر بها||EN::A historical well among the wells of Al-Madinah Al-Munawwarah, it was located in the Western Harrah, and was known in some later sources as "Zamzam Well". It was reported that the Prophet ﷺ passed by it.||TR::Medine-i Münevvere kuyularından tarihi bir kuyu olup, Batı Harre'de yer almaktaydı ve bazı geç dönem kaynaklarında "Zamzam Kuyusu" adıyla biliniyordu. Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ oradan geçtiği rivayet edilmiştir.||ID::Sebuah sumur bersejarah dari sumur-sumur di Madinah al-Munawwarah, dahulunya terletak di Harrah Barat, dan dikenal dalam beberapa sumber belakangan dengan nama "Sumur Zamzam". Diriwayatkan bahwa Nabi ﷺ pernah melewatinya.||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/eFcTQb1sqpj7oZdFA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.59225841103012,24.45531737638462,624.9183926024718</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>غدير خم</name>
    <description><![CDATA[AR::من المواضع التي صلى فيها النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وأوصى باهل بيته فقال عليه الصلاة والسلام ألا أيها الناس فإنما أنا بشر يوشك أن يأتي رسول ربي فأجيب وأنا تارك فيكم ثقلين  أولهما كتاب الله فيه الهدى والنور فخذوا بكتاب الله واستمسكوا به فحث على كتاب الله ورغب فيه ثم قال وأهل بيتي أذكركم الله في أهل بيتي أذكركم الله في أهل بيتي أذكركم الله في أهل بيتي||EN::One of the locations where the Prophet ﷺ prayed and gave counsel regarding the members of his household (Ahl al-Bayt), saying, peace and blessings be upon him: "O people, I am only a human being; soon the messenger of my Lord (the Angel of Death) may come to me and I will respond. I am leaving among you two weighty things: the first of them is the Book of Allah, in which there is guidance and light, so hold fast to the Book of Allah and adhere to it." Thus, he urged adherence to the Book of Allah and encouraged it, then he said: "And the members of my household; I remind you of Allah concerning the members of my household, I remind you of Allah concerning the members of my household, I remind you of Allah concerning the members of my household."||TR::Hz. Peygamber'in ﷺ namaz kıldığı ve ehlibeyti hakkında tavsiyede bulunduğu mekânlardan biridir; nitekim O'na salât ve selâm olsun şöyle buyurmuştur: "Haberiniz olsun ki ey insanlar! Ben ancak bir insanım; Rabbimin elçisinin (ölüm meleğinin) gelmesi ve benim de ona icabet etmem yakındır. Ben sizin aranızda iki paha biçilmez emanet (sekaleyn) bırakıyorum: Bunların ilki, içinde hidayet ve nur bulunan Allah'ın Kitabı'dır; Allah'ın Kitabı'na sarılın ve ona sımsıkı tutunun." Böylece Allah'ın Kitabı'na teşvik etmiş و ona yönlendirmiştir, ardından şöyle buyurmuştur: "Ve ehlibeytim; ehlibeytim konusunda size Allah'ı hatırlatırım, ehlibeytim konusunda size Allah'ı hatırlatırım, ehlibeytim konusunda size Allah'ı hatırlatırım."||ID::Salah satu tempat di mana Nabi ﷺ shalat dan berpesan tentang ahli baitnya (keluarganya), beliau shalallahu 'alaihi wa sallam bersabda: "Ketahuilah wahai manusia, sesungguhnya aku hanyalah seorang manusia, hampir tiba saatnya utusan Tuhanku (malaikat maut) datang lalu aku memenuhinya. Dan aku meninggalkan di tengah-tengah kalian dua hal yang berat: yang pertama adalah Kitabullah, di dalamnya terdapat petunjuk dan cahaya, maka pegang teguhlah Kitabullah dan berpeganglah padanya." Beliau mendorong untuk berpegang pada Kitabullah dan menganjurkannya, kemudian beliau bersabda: "Dan ahli baitku; aku ingatkan kalian kepada Allah tentang ahli baitku, aku ingatkan kalian kepada Allah tentang ahli baitku, aku ingatkan kalian kepada Allah tentang ahli baitku."||MAPS::https://maps.app.goo.gl/jJ2BUSJ7qQgDe1rFA]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>39.20958779487356,22.74226275994134,46.48052221886036</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
